{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies","id":1445034,"title":"Since everyone is doing Legacies...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-21T06:10:03-07:00","id":1445034,"title":"Since everyone is doing Legacies...","content":"For a while now I have had some ideas for some Legacies. For a while now I have been in awe of the concepts. For a while now I wished for awesome mechanics to match awesome concepts. For a while now I realized I am too much of an amateur to make those mechanics and too lazy to ask for help.<br /> <br /> Now I am asking for help. Three Legacies. We agree on which to do first. When I am satisfied or the community offers no further help we move on to the next Legacy. <br /> <br /> 1. Death priests (Obrimos)<br /> <br /> Aron Ra once made the case that all religions have in their doctrine the idea that there is some essence of self (soul or what have you) that continues on in some other form. Whether or not he is right, it convinced me that the Underworld in this setting has sympathy with religions in general and that the Krewes of the sin-eaters are just the ones that tapped this link.<br /> <br /> Yes, this is the crossover Legacy. The founder made the link and connected the religious aspects of his Path to the Underworld to form this Legacy (and overcome the inferior Arcanum limits). Treats all Krewes as parent &quot;Order&quot;, because it is actually connected to the Krewe-binding ceremony. Treats Krewe ceremonies as an extension of the Death Arcanum with greatly simplified mechanics and superior casting. Works to groom the Krewe into the image of the supernal itself so Catabasis can reclaim a facet of reality in the name of whatever higher power you believe in.<br /> <br /> 2. Duelists (Path undecided)<br /> <br /> <br /> The founder is a junky of the Duel Arcane. Thought to himself about making a Legacy based on the same, making Legacy Attainments just for winning Duels. Prime as the Primary Arcanum (haha) to aid his spell-casting in the Duel and Fate as the optional Arcanum to add extra rules and penalties to the Duel, such as immediately losing if you so much as indirectly cheat. <br /> <br /> Then he (or she or they if you want) realized that some Consilia may consider this illegal. The plan? Use the Duel Arcane to win the right to create and use the Legacy. Going after all the office-holding mages and beat them in the Duel, then use their influence to set up the next match and getting the ball rolling. The quest can double as the indoctrination part of the Legacy, using the act of legalizing it to create it. If the contrarian Free Council disagrees? Beat their leaders, if they insist that this should be done by vote? Beat enough of their numbers to sway the votes. Replace the founder with your character and you have got a chronicle on your hands.<br /> <br /> 3. Unashamed (Mastigos)<br /> <br /> <br /> As I contemplated the implications of Legacy Wisdom I realized that psychos can now have sqeaky clean Wisdom if you just commit your crimes through Legacy Attainments. Let's take this to its logical extreme. Imagine a Legacy whose entire symbolism and premise was to stretch Legacy Wisdom to all-encompassing extremes. Legacy Attainments can shed some limits if they resonate well with the Theory and by abandoning the Practices you can make strange Attainments that conforms closely with whatever the Theory is, or at least that is how I understand it.<br /> <br /> This Legacy is the experiment of a Thearch who figured that by making Legacy Attainments that passively alter how the mind and soul respond to transgressions he can remove all Acts of Hubris from the mage through immunity. Problem? He didn't really believe shame has any value. He also dismissed the arguments of others that the supernatural races deserve better then servitude to humanity, or the questions of if humanity should rule so absolutely over a universe of other sentient beings, or if placing so much power in the hands of billions won't tear the universe apart again over petty disputes. That mindset devised a Legacy that makes one behave like the Rapt, so the Silver Ladder denounced him as Enraptured so as not to do any soul-searching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T07:19:58-07:00","id":1445043,"title":"","content":"On my phone and incapable of much contribution, but...<br /> <br /> Death Priests! Looks a lot like what I wanted to do for homebrew (five Legacies, each of one Path, for all major supernaturals \u2014 the idea was given first by Dataweaver, one of many homebrewers around here). I thought solely of Ceremonies, rather than Krewes and Catabasis, so that\u2019s new. <br /> <br /> Duelists. Are they named Flambeau, by chance? <br /> <br /> The Unashamed? Hmm... by that alone, it just looks like Left-Handed mages who happen to rely on Attainments. We might want something more focused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T07:30:27-07:00","id":1445045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies#post1445034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a while now I have had some ideas for some Legacies. For a while now I have been in awe of the concepts. For a while now I wished for awesome mechanics to match awesome concepts. For a while now I realized I am too much of an amateur to make those mechanics and too lazy to ask for help.<br /> <br /> Now I am asking for help. Three Legacies. We agree on which to do first. When I am satisfied or the community offers no further help we move on to the next Legacy.<br /> <br /> 1. Death priests (Obrimos)<br /> <br /> Aron Ra once made the case that all religions have in their doctrine the idea that there is some essence of self (soul or what have you) that continues on in some other form. Whether or not he is right, it convinced me that the Underworld in this setting has sympathy with religions in general and that the Krewes of the sin-eaters are just the ones that tapped this link.<br /> <br /> Yes, this is the crossover Legacy. The founder made the link and connected the religious aspects of his Path to the Underworld to form this Legacy (and overcome the inferior Arcanum limits). Treats all Krewes as parent &quot;Order&quot;, because it is actually connected to the Krewe-binding ceremony. Treats Krewe ceremonies as an extension of the Death Arcanum with greatly simplified mechanics and superior casting. Works to groom the Krewe into the image of the supernal itself so Catabasis can reclaim a facet of reality in the name of whatever higher power you believe in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea! I would do Death/Prime for the legacy, and try and have it permanently change the resonance of the Underworld through religious devotion. Kinda like mage the ascension now that I think of it. I like this one the most out of the three. *I have never read Giest before, so standard rules when someone doesn\u2019t know what they are talking about apply*<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies#post1445034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Duelists (Path undecided)<br /> <br /> <br /> The founder is a junky of the Duel Arcane. Thought to himself about making a Legacy based on the same, making Legacy Attainments just for winning Duels. Prime as the Primary Arcanum (haha) to aid his spell-casting in the Duel and Fate as the optional Arcanum to add extra rules and penalties to the Duel, such as immediately losing if you so much as indirectly cheat.<br /> <br /> Then he (or she or they if you want) realized that some Consilia may consider this illegal. The plan? Use the Duel Arcane to win the right to create and use the Legacy. Going after all the office-holding mages and beat them in the Duel, then use their influence to set up the next match and getting the ball rolling. The quest can double as the indoctrination part of the Legacy, using the act of legalizing it to create it. If the contrarian Free Council disagrees? Beat their leaders, if they insist that this should be done by vote? Beat enough of their numbers to sway the votes. Replace the founder with your character and you have got a chronicle on your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m going to start with that I find the concept boring. But, by no means let that stop you. (I find the duel arcane boring in general.) The legacy definitely has a place in the silver ladder and AA. I would argue it\u2019s even very legal, if annoying. Does one penalize the person with higher arcanum in normal duels? Because in the end it\u2019s just more mystical power that really only brought to bear in a specialized set of circumstances.<br /> On the legacy it\u2019s self, prime/ fate set this up as a Orbimos aka the mighty, and I think your arcana spread is good. Mastigos might be interested, with their annoy everyone to make them better themselves thing. It ignores their arcanum, but resonates with their symbolism so your mileage may vary.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies#post1445034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Unashamed (Mastigos)<br /> <br /> <br /> As I contemplated the implications of Legacy Wisdom I realized that psychos can now have sqeaky clean Wisdom if you just commit your crimes through Legacy Attainments. Let's take this to its logical extreme. Imagine a Legacy whose entire symbolism and premise was to stretch Legacy Wisdom to all-encompassing extremes. Legacy Attainments can shed some limits if they resonate well with the Theory and by abandoning the Practices you can make strange Attainments that conforms closely with whatever the Theory is, or at least that is how I understand it.<br /> <br /> This Legacy is the experiment of a Thearch who figured that by making Legacy Attainments that passively alter how the mind and soul respond to transgressions he can remove all Acts of Hubris from the mage through immunity. Problem? He didn't really believe shame has any value. He also dismissed the arguments of others that the supernatural races deserve better then servitude to humanity, or the questions of if humanity should rule so absolutely over a universe of other sentient beings, or if placing so much power in the hands of billions won't tear the universe apart again over petty disputes. That mindset devised a Legacy that makes one behave like the Rapt, so the Silver Ladder denounced him as Enraptured so as not to do any soul-searching.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I have opinions on this. This should flat out be a guardian and seer legacy. No if\u2019s or buts. They would definitely steal it given the chance. While their masques can do the job, this is almost as easy to develop for a mage, and will cover a wider ground if every attainment removes several acts of hubris. (I\u2019m not saying it should be guardians only or even guardians primary, but they WILL acquire it. So will seers, they will want this just as hard if not more so.)<br /> <br /> On to the silver ladder, and I imagine they would be quite divided on the issue. On the one hand this is a MASSIVE middle finger to the limitations of the world. Some would probably cite it as great progress to breaking the soul cage. Others would argue that the legacy originator is now a equally massive threat to the Consilium. For bonus points, I would run the founder as a Harry Dresden type destructive savior, casually burning buildings through negligence and poor choices on a regular basis and casually saving hundreds if not thousands of lives on a equally regular basis. This creates a more interesting story in my opinion. Much like hunter, it\u2019s now hard to tell when your companion has slipped over the slippery slope. Because, let\u2019s be honest, every legacy has had its monsters. Because that\u2019s what mages are, monsters with too much power and not enough self control, that happen to be people.<br /> <br /> This should be a prime only legacy. You are switching the symbolism of a mage to a rapt without going all the way. A really nasty weaving effect in essence. This legacy probably is the result of archmastery, I think template modification is a thing you can do. I would have the legacy members be having their long term nimbus happening ALL the time, as a reference to Dresden and to show how little control they have. Everything should read them as at 1 wisdom, and they can neither raise nor lower it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-21-2021, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T18:56:24-07:00","id":1445175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies#post1445034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a while now I have had some ideas for some Legacies. For a while now I have been in awe of the concepts. For a while now I wished for awesome mechanics to match awesome concepts. For a while now I realized I am too much of an amateur to make those mechanics and too lazy to ask for help.<br /> <br /> Now I am asking for help. Three Legacies. We agree on which to do first. When I am satisfied or the community offers no further help we move on to the next Legacy.<br /> <br /> 1. Death priests (Obrimos)<br /> <br /> Aron Ra once made the case that all religions have in their doctrine the idea that there is some essence of self (soul or what have you) that continues on in some other form. Whether or not he is right, it convinced me that the Underworld in this setting has sympathy with religions in general and that the Krewes of the sin-eaters are just the ones that tapped this link.<br /> <br /> Yes, this is the crossover Legacy. The founder made the link and connected the religious aspects of his Path to the Underworld to form this Legacy (and overcome the inferior Arcanum limits). Treats all Krewes as parent &quot;Order&quot;, because it is actually connected to the Krewe-binding ceremony. Treats Krewe ceremonies as an extension of the Death Arcanum with greatly simplified mechanics and superior casting. Works to groom the Krewe into the image of the supernal itself so Catabasis can reclaim a facet of reality in the name of whatever higher power you believe in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a few ideas for this. The Prime Alternate Attainments I think I could lift straight from another religious-themed Obrimos Legacy I created (though I don't think I've posted it).<br /> <br /> The Death Attainments sort of depend on how conciliatory to Ghosts you want to be, but I have ideas there, too: the first Attainment should be <s>a Ghosts only <i>Exorcist's Eye</i> (advanced duration) (there's no real reason Death should need Spirit to see ghosts this way)</s> <i>Speak With the Dead</i> (advanced duration); second could be <i>Ghost Shield</i> (advanced duration) or <i>Touch of the Grave</i> (advanced duration), I prefer the former because it's protective and touching ghosts is... eh; third is <i>Ectoplasm</i> (instant, advanced duration), this allows ghosts to Manifest and can feed Plasm to your Sin-Eater friends; fourth is <i>Exorcism</i> (instant) for those truly intransigent ghosts; fifth is <i>Create Anchor</i> (advanced duration) for ghosts you want to stick around for a while longer so you can help them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Duelists (Path undecided)<br /> <br /> <br /> The founder is a junky of the Duel Arcane. Thought to himself about making a Legacy based on the same, making Legacy Attainments just for winning Duels. Prime as the Primary Arcanum (haha) to aid his spell-casting in the Duel and Fate as the optional Arcanum to add extra rules and penalties to the Duel, such as immediately losing if you so much as indirectly cheat.<br /> <br /> Then he (or she or they if you want) realized that some Consilia may consider this illegal. The plan? Use the Duel Arcane to win the right to create and use the Legacy. Going after all the office-holding mages and beat them in the Duel, then use their influence to set up the next match and getting the ball rolling. The quest can double as the indoctrination part of the Legacy, using the act of legalizing it to create it. If the contrarian Free Council disagrees? Beat their leaders, if they insist that this should be done by vote? Beat enough of their numbers to sway the votes. Replace the founder with your character and you have got a chronicle on your hands. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, with how... incredibly limited the Duel Arcane is, you're better off with a Style Merit than an entire arcane duelist Legacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Unashamed (Mastigos)<br /> <br /> As I contemplated the implications of Legacy Wisdom I realized that psychos can now have sqeaky clean Wisdom if you just commit your crimes through Legacy Attainments. Let's take this to its logical extreme. Imagine a Legacy whose entire symbolism and premise was to stretch Legacy Wisdom to all-encompassing extremes. Legacy Attainments can shed some limits if they resonate well with the Theory and by abandoning the Practices you can make strange Attainments that conforms closely with whatever the Theory is, or at least that is how I understand it.<br /> <br /> This Legacy is the experiment of a Thearch who figured that by making Legacy Attainments that passively alter how the mind and soul respond to transgressions he can remove all Acts of Hubris from the mage through immunity. Problem? He didn't really believe shame has any value. He also dismissed the arguments of others that the supernatural races deserve better then servitude to humanity, or the questions of if humanity should rule so absolutely over a universe of other sentient beings, or if placing so much power in the hands of billions won't tear the universe apart again over petty disputes. That mindset devised a Legacy that makes one behave like the Rapt, so the Silver Ladder denounced him as Enraptured so as not to do any soul-searching. </div> </div> </div>Just go Rapt if you want to be Rapt. Also, they'd declare the Legacy Left-Handed, denouncing someone as Rapt is silly since it's pretty easy to verify if someone is Rapt.<br /> <br /> Practically, this is way too broad, it's far better to figure out what Acts of Hubris you want to be able to commit (for research, of course) and build a Legacy around that than trying to be this generic.<br /> <br /> Legacies need to be both tightly focused and have useful Attainments for people to want to use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 04-23-2021, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T19:20:09-07:00","id":1445182,"title":"","content":"For the Duelists, how about an Attainment that lets them declare the Duel on non-Awakened?<br /> <br /> Quite potent and nasty, since very few beings would be able to counter that. Sleepers certainly can\u2019t, and neither can most Sleepwalkers. Proximi, and certain entities such as spirits and \u2018major templates\u2019 like vampires and werewolves might be able to do <i>something</i>, albeit still at a massive disadvantage.<br /> <br /> A related idea would be making this Duelist Legacy not limited to the Duel Arcane, and expanding its interests to the concept/symbol of The Duel itself. There\u2019s something poetic and evocative about two individuals, unwilling to bend, invoking sacred violence as the final testament of their willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-21-2021, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T04:39:44-07:00","id":1445641,"title":"","content":"To clarify: I have never made a Legacy before. That is why I wanted more help than suggestions and wanted to focus on one at a time. Since you guys did not choose I will pick for you.<br /> <br /> Duelists. <br /> <br /> As for your first imput, Hermit. Flambeau?<br /> <br /> As for the input of both TempleBuilder and Proindrakenzol. You must have missed some key points so I will bring them to your attention. In the supplement: &quot;Nameless and Accursed&quot;, it gives an off-hand mention that through the Duel might literally makes right. Whenever you win in such a Duel reality adjusts so that you are more correct than you were before, the symbol of your victory accepted into the heavens. It was obtuse in how much adjustment is done though. <br /> <br /> Don't forget that the Duel is not that limited a part of mage society. It is in place because the tempers of reality warpers will not always yield to a court and the stakes of such can be disastrous. Both containing the collateral damage and venting rage, its role is not trivial. If you are not convinced then ask yourselves why the Lex Magica accepts it as binding and valid. Think about it. Imagine if a court dispute in real life accepted the result of a video game match instead, why would mages of a modern democratic world resort to trial by (simulated) combat?<br /> <br /> This Legacy is not the same thing as having greater skill in general magic. If mages suspect that this produces an overwhelming advantage that almost no one can overcome, of course some would cry foul. The Duel Arcane has some internal rules that impose themselves on all who restrict themselves to its hypothetical space. No Yantras or overReaching. If you fail to further break your opponent with an attack then you cannot attack with that Arcanum again until your foe further breaks. Rules such as these and others not mentioned will be altered by the Attainments of this Legacy. Those without the Legacy will know that if they ever get into a dispute with a member then all the member has to do is be force the issue into a Duel instead of a court and win every time. Those without will of course want to question the legality of the Legacy to avoid this.<br /> <br /> If that doesn't convince you, I don't know what to say. This is what the thread will focus on for a while.<br /> <br /> To Hermit again, elaborate on your last paragraph. I am confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T09:03:23-07:00","id":1445674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1445641#post1445641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify: I have never made a Legacy before. That is why I wanted more help than suggestions and wanted to focus on one at a time. Since you guys did not choose I will pick for you.<br /> <br /> Duelists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. For reference, I have made only one legacy and have never played a game of mage. I\u2019m not exactly comfortable telling you what to do. I\u2019m not exactly clear on what help you wanted. Did you want symbolism help, or attainments or general idea discussion?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1445641#post1445641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the input of both TempleBuilder and Proindrakenzol. You must have missed some key points so I will bring them to your attention. In the supplement: &quot;Nameless and Accursed&quot;, it gives an off-hand mention that through the Duel might literally makes right. Whenever you win in such a Duel reality adjusts so that you are more correct than you were before, the symbol of your victory accepted into the heavens. It was obtuse in how much adjustment is done though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a page number? If the duel makes might into right, then it draws off the Fathers symbolism. Or maybe a hybrid of the Father and the General.<br /> <br /> ( My reasoning for this is that the Father IS \u201cdon\u2019t question authority\u201d and might is merely another form of authority.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1445641#post1445641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that the Duel is not that limited a part of mage society. It is in place because the tempers of reality warpers will not always yield to a court and the stakes of such can be disastrous. Both containing the collateral damage and venting rage, its role is not trivial. If you are not convinced then ask yourselves why the Lex Magica accepts it as binding and valid. Think about it. Imagine if a court dispute in real life accepted the result of a video game match instead, why would mages of a modern democratic world resort to trial by (simulated) combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it\u2019s useful. Mage can settle disputes where neither is wrong in a nonviolent manner as you mentioned. It\u2019s a historical way of settling arguments, and mages are all about ancient traditions. On a wide scale it prevents a majority of mage murder by other mage, (so they can die by their own hubris or mistakes). I never doubted that it was important, I just thought that it was boring. Clearly, you do not find it boring, so by all means go make this legacy. I will continue offering my advice and options, until they are unwanted or unneeded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1445641#post1445641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Legacy is not the same thing as having greater skill in general magic. If mages suspect that this produces an overwhelming advantage that almost no one can overcome, of course some would cry foul. The Duel Arcane has some internal rules that impose themselves on all who restrict themselves to its hypothetical space. No Yantras or overReaching. If you fail to further break your opponent with an attack then you cannot attack with that Arcanum again until your foe further breaks. Rules such as these and others not mentioned will be altered by the Attainments of this Legacy. Those without the Legacy will know that if they ever get into a dispute with a member then all the member has to do is be force the issue into a Duel instead of a court and win every time. Those without will of course want to question the legality of the Legacy to avoid this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here is that, rules as written, the duels are heavily skewed towards the mage with more power and more doors. I don\u2019t remember the exact odds, but the rules don\u2019t really allow for evening the odds. I\u2019m more than fine with a legacy punching above their metaphysical weight, but the rules for the duel are just lacking in a number of ways. There are no merits for the duel, to represent greater skill at the duel. There is only the same basic setup for everyone, two people on a flat plane fighting each other. The strategy to it is very simple, and there is not much depth. Any legacy about will radically alter the balance of power. In my opinion, if you want this legacy to work, the duel must be more complex, so there is room both for new interesting battles without the legacy and with it. I suggest fighting styles and merits for every duel focused order and one for every arcanum. That way there is some variety in fights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1445641#post1445641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that doesn't convince you, I don't know what to say. This is what the thread will focus on for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it convinced me you want this legacy. I\u2019m not sure it addressed my personal problems with the duel arcane, but I still will still offer advice and opinions. Just because I don\u2019t like something doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s bad. It just means we don\u2019t agree. As long as the legacy becomes something that you like, then it fulfilled it\u2019s purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T09:32:17-07:00","id":1445677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1445641#post1445641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify: I have never made a Legacy before. That is why I wanted more help than suggestions and wanted to focus on one at a time. Since you guys did not choose I will pick for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I straight up gave you an outline for the Death Priest Legacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the input of both TempleBuilder and Proindrakenzol. You must have missed some key points so I will bring them to your attention. </div> </div> </div>I didn't miss anything, I'm well aware of the flavor surrounding the Duel Arcane (though you're significantly overstating its reality warping properties, which are incredibly minor and limited to influencing opinion and iterpretation), but that doesn't make the mechanics of the Duel Arcane any broader, nor does it make its relative use any more interesting or solid for a Legacy: there isn't a lot of Mystery in the Duel Arcane, and being better at it doesn't really help with the vast majority of Mysteries. It's a political cudgel that only works as long as everyone else is willing to play along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the supplement: &amp;quot;Nameless and Accursed&amp;quot;, it gives an off-hand mention that through the Duel might literally makes right. Whenever you win in such a Duel reality adjusts so that you are more correct than you were before, the symbol of your victory accepted into the heavens. It was obtuse in how much adjustment is done though. </div> </div> </div><br /> No actual adjustment to reality is done, winning a Duel Arcane doesn't let you make the sky green. What it does do is allow you to stake out claims for Mysteries or Hallows or make sure your theory comes to the fore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't forget that the Duel is not that limited a part of mage society. It is in place because the tempers of reality warpers will not always yield to a court and the stakes of such can be disastrous. Both containing the collateral damage and venting rage, its role is not trivial. If you are not convinced then ask yourselves why the Lex Magica accepts it as binding and valid. Think about it. Imagine if a court dispute in real life accepted the result of a video game match instead, why would mages of a modern democratic world resort to trial by (simulated) combat? </div> </div> </div>The answer to that is easy: other than the Free Council, Mages aren't particularly democratic. And the Duel Arcane is an option of second-to-last resort with a ton of political consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Legacy is not the same thing as having greater skill in general magic. If mages suspect that this produces an overwhelming advantage that almost no one can overcome, of course some would cry foul. The Duel Arcane has some internal rules that impose themselves on all who restrict themselves to its hypothetical space. No Yantras or overReaching. If you fail to further break your opponent with an attack then you cannot attack with that Arcanum again until your foe further breaks. Rules such as these and others not mentioned will be altered by the Attainments of this Legacy. Those without the Legacy will know that if they ever get into a dispute with a member then all the member has to do is be force the issue into a Duel instead of a court and win every time. Those without will of course want to question the legality of the Legacy to avoid this. </div> </div> </div>As long as you understand that the Duel Arcane is mechanically limited (meaning there's not a lot of design space that doesn't just break it) and that a reasonable Consilium will not consider the outcome of any Duel Arcane with someone with this Legacy to be valid, since it's fundamentally cheating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T10:34:43-07:00","id":1445685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1445677#post1445677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and that a reasonable Consilium will not consider the outcome of any Duel Arcane with someone with this Legacy to be valid, since it's fundamentally cheating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it though? If one has a higher arcanum rating or higher attributes, is that not just a form of metaphysical power? A legacy that buffs the legacy owner only can be considered to be similar metaphysical power. Technically every mage can accesses the legacy after gnosis two. Of course, the comparison to performance enhancing drugs is a valid argument...<br /> <br /> I agree that in the duel arcane\u2019s current form, any extra power would break it. But if we refine the duel, maybe something interesting would result. Maybe a legacy devoted to the duel would not be out of place in that context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T21:15:11-07:00","id":1445778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1445641#post1445641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for your first imput, Hermit. Flambeau?</div> </div> </div> </div>House Flambeau is a playable group belonging to the protagonist faction, the Order of Hermes, in the TRPG, Ars Magica. They are self-proclaimed knights and adventurers, known both in- and out-of universe for their affinity with fire magic, and a warlike tendency who often declare battles and wars against other mages both belonging to and outside the Order for sake of the Order as a whole.<br /> <br /> I namedropped them because the Duel Arcane is, in some way, also a means of violence that seeks to contain the damage mages can do to each other and anybody nearby; seems to fit the Flambeau AFAIK. I mentioned them because Ars Magica heavily inspired Mage: The Ascension, which in turn is the spiritual predecessor of Mage: The Awakening. It helps we already have a group in MtAw whose motif and name goes way back to Ars Magica; the Tremere.<br /> <br /> It was largely me trying to be funny, so don't think about it that much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To Hermit again, elaborate on your last paragraph. I am confused. </div> </div> </div>By my last paragraph, you meant this right?<br /> <br /> <i>A related idea would be making this Duelist Legacy not limited to the Duel Arcane, and expanding its interests to the concept/symbol of The Duel itself. There\u2019s something poetic and evocative about two individuals, unwilling to bend, invoking sacred violence as the final testament of their willpower.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> This is somewhat related to what others said about a Legacy <i>solely</i> focused on the Duel Arcane; it's hard to build one, and it's hard to narrate one. My proposal was about making a Legacy about duels in general, similarly to how, say, the Eleventh Question is about investigation, and the House of Ariadne is about urban divination. Something like...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Yantras</b>: equipping personal weaponry such as rapiers or pistols (+2); a crowd in anticipation of the mage and her subject fighting (+1); declaring the subject of a spell as the mage's rival or nemesis (+2); revealing something about the mage herself that would make the subject antagonize her (+1, +2 if the antagonism escalates into intent of violence)<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations</b>: 'dueling' someone, defined as contesting him one-to-one in otherwise mundane actions; openly gathering information about declared rivals and nemeses; abandoning more peaceful means of resolving a conflict in favor of battle; reflecting on past victories and defeats<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment</b>: Mind 1 spell &quot;Mental Scan,&quot; with Reach assigned to instant use. Count as exceptional success when used on a rival or nemesis while dueling him.<br /> <b>Optional</b>: When using the main effect, can also ask the question available via the Prime 1 spell &quot;Supernal Vision.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment</b>: When using Mind Mage Armor, can spend a Willpower point instead of Mana to deflect attacks.<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Prime Mage Armor extends to magically enhanced attacks, such as an enhanced sword. Still does not defend against natural attacks made by magical beings, such as werewolf claws.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment</b>: Access following bonuses for the Duel Arcane: add half of Mind dots, rounded up, to Doors; can use the Mind Arcanum a second time when failing to open a Door with it; when defeated; does not lose Willpower points when defeated; can instantly resolve the Defeated Condition by declaring the Duel Arcane on another mage<br /> <b>Optional</b>: With appropriate ritual, Prime 3 spell &quot;Display of Power&quot; with Reach assigned to Advanced Scale. Affects Sleepers and Sleepwalkers as well. Sleepers automatically lose. Sleepwalkers can temporarily perceive the Supernal World, and rolls solely Attribute for attacks and defenses. Proximi can roll Attribute + highest dot rating of a Blessing. Non-Supernal supernatural creatures may roll Attribute + a suitable trait, at Storyteller discretion. When non-mages attack, failing to opening a Door disables the use of that Attribute, not the Arcanum-equivalent.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something like that. That was just a quick suggestion, in no way checked for accuracy/balance/clarity, and definitely not intending to override your own ideas for the homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T03:44:54-07:00","id":1445947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1445778#post1445778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I namedropped them because the Duel Arcane is, in some way, also a means of violence that seeks to contain the damage mages can do to each other and anybody nearby; seems to fit the Flambeau AFAIK. I mentioned them because Ars Magica heavily inspired Mage: The Ascension, which in turn is the spiritual predecessor of Mage: The Awakening. It helps we already have a group in MtAw whose motif and name goes way back to Ars Magica; the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if it was different in early versions but as of 5e it's actually the Tremere who developed the Duel Arcane analogue. Flambeau prefer just outright warfare.<br /> <br /> That said, the <i>Ars</i> Tremere would be an interesting basis for a duellist legacy, though they're less duelling junkies and more about capitalising on a small area of expertise to take political power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T19:08:32-07:00","id":1446016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1445947#post1445947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure if it was different in early versions but as of 5e it's actually the Tremere who developed the Duel Arcane analogue. Flambeau prefer just outright warfare.<br /> <br /> That said, the <i>Ars</i> Tremere would be an interesting basis for a duellist legacy, though they're less duelling junkies and more about capitalising on a small area of expertise to take political power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that \u201cmore about capitalising...\u201d thing was why I chose against referring to (re-referring to?) Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T06:14:14-07:00","id":1446095,"title":"","content":"Will respond and contribute again once I had the night's sleep I missed and reviewed the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T03:22:03-07:00","id":1446258,"title":"","content":"I am back. Just want to get this out of the way immediately so I can concentrate on a longer post. One of you asked for a page number and another thought I was either mistaken or a lier.<br /> <br /> In the supplement &quot;Nameless and Accursed&quot;, page 14: there is a section called &quot;Consilium and Caucus&quot;. The second paragraph contains the passing reference that winning the Duel Arcane does literally make the winner more right than the loser by way of altering the Supernal.<br /> <br /> I don't think this property is because of the Exarchs though. I have my own theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T04:23:09-07:00","id":1446269,"title":"","content":"Getting back to the Duelists:<br /> <br /> I say we should focus on the basics. As in almost everything up to the first two Attainments. I say almost because I don't care much for how they dress or how they organize. If you want to fill those in I won't stop you nor will I join you.<br /> <br /> Parentage: Acanthus, Adamantine Arrow. The Seers have been trying to get a hold of it and the Silver Ladder is still recovering from the beating they took during the founding of the Legacy. Chances are that both will gain access to the Legacy eventually. <br /> <br /> Doctrine<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Prime 2, 1 dot in either Brawl, Weaponry, or Firearms, 1 dot in Intimidation. Your magic in the Duel will be stylized after your choice of offensive skills. <br /> <br /> Initiation: the would-be Duelist must win the Duel Arcane, the stakes must include the right to join the Legacy. This so far is starting a tradition of potential students being made to fight for the right to join. They at least spend a week being prepped so that the initiation does not fail to take because they misunderstood the theory, symbolism, or fall short in any awkward way.<br /> <br /> Theory: understanding rights as protected freedoms, might literally does make right because that is where rights come from. How else are they to be protected? The trappings of modern society distract us from the fact that force of law is how the government grants rights, so we delude ourselves in thinking we moved past this truth, as though we ever could. (Yes, the founder is fatalistic and cynical.) Mystical might makes factual right, given that mages can rewrite reality. If you value something like morality or ambition, speak truth to power and don't falter for cowardly excuses. <br /> <br /> From a certain point of view, that may have been bleak. In the Chronicles of Darkness it doesn't seem out of place.<br /> <br /> Magic<br /> <br /> Primary Arcanum: Prime<br /> Secondary Arcanum: Fate<br /> <br /> Still not sure what the Yantras and Oblations should be. I think they should be modeled after a more warlike version of the Acanthus symbolism, following the legends of heroes and gods in divine combat, need inspiration. Norse? At least that is fatalistic. Greco-Roman? Suitably glorious. <br /> <br /> After reading your review and answering follow-up questions, I will post my plan for how the Attainments should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T05:07:58-07:00","id":1446274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446258#post1446258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am back. Just want to get this out of the way immediately so I can concentrate on a longer post. One of you asked for a page number and another thought I was either mistaken or a lier.<br /> <br /> In the supplement &quot;Nameless and Accursed&quot;, page 14: there is a section called &quot;Consilium and Caucus&quot;. The second paragraph contains the passing reference that winning the Duel Arcane does literally make the winner more right than the loser by way of altering the Supernal.<br /> <br /> I don't think this property is because of the Exarchs though. I have my own theory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The text is:<br /> <br /> <i>winning<br /> a Duel Arcane literally makes one mage more right than the other,<br /> as <b>the symbol of their victory</b> is Truthfully written into the<br /> Supernal itself</i><br /> <br /> Emphasis mine. The Fallen concept here that becomes Supernally reinforced by the Duel Arcane seems to be &quot;I am the victor and you the loser&quot; rather than &quot;What I claim about (the subject) is right.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless you <i>did</i> mean that? If so, then you're right.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> About Yantras and Oblations... Hmm, well I already gave my ideas for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T08:23:13-07:00","id":1446288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446258#post1446258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am back. Just want to get this out of the way immediately so I can concentrate on a longer post. One of you asked for a page number and another thought I was either mistaken or a lier.</div> </div> </div> </div> That was me. I asked because in my mind you were mistaken, or I was. If you could find the page number, I could read the passage myself and decide for myself. I have been wrong before, and I will be wrong in the future. The intention was not hostile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446258#post1446258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the supplement &quot;Nameless and Accursed&quot;, page 14: there is a section called &quot;Consilium and Caucus&quot;. The second paragraph contains the passing reference that winning the Duel Arcane does literally make the winner more right than the loser by way of altering the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div> I reread the part, going to have to say that I think if it literally warped reality like you say, it would be worded differently. It just says that the Supernal remembers your victory forever, unless someone can erase it. This would even survive archmastery, I think. It\u2019s like scoring a debate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446258#post1446258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this property is because of the Exarchs though. I have my own theory.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do tell. My point was that anything using the exarchs symbolism draws from them. And I believe that might makes right is a exarchal philosophy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446269#post1446269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting back to the Duelists:<br /> <br /> I say we should focus on the basics. As in almost everything up to the first two Attainments. I say almost because I don't care much for how they dress or how they organize. If you want to fill those in I won't stop you nor will I join you.</div> </div> </div> </div> But fashion is so much fun. Why would you deprive yourself of it? (I\u2019m joking by the way).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446269#post1446269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Parentage: Acanthus, Adamantine Arrow. The Seers have been trying to get a hold of it and the Silver Ladder is still recovering from the beating they took during the founding of the Legacy. Chances are that both will gain access to the Legacy eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe the silver ladder would immediately take the legacy into themselves, unless the legacy was in total ideological opposition. The silver ladder would definitely use it to make false lions, and probably use the main part of the legacy as pawns<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not convinced this ISN\u2019T a origin seer legacy but seers would want it too if it isn\u2019t. Free Council might have a member who is really into the legacy, but I don\u2019t think it fits them very well.<br /> <br /> Side note: do you have beef with the silver ladder? Every legacy you propose has them lose badly or be stupid evil... even though the legacy philosophy suits them fine. (It\u2019s fine if you do, evil silver ladder is definitely a valid genre.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446269#post1446269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doctrine<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Prime 2, 1 dot in either Brawl, Weaponry, or Firearms, 1 dot in Intimidation. Your magic in the Duel will be stylized after your choice of offensive skills.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know you want this to be a warrior legacy, but the duel is as much a debate as it is a fight. If the legacy makes it to the silver ladder, they might choose to emphasize the debate part and not the fighting part. Maybe they chose persuasion or politics instead of intimidation. Food for thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446269#post1446269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Initiation: the would-be Duelist must win the Duel Arcane, the stakes must include the right to join the Legacy. This so far is starting a tradition of potential students being made to fight for the right to join. They at least spend a week being prepped so that the initiation does not fail to take because they misunderstood the theory, symbolism, or fall short in any awkward way.</div> </div> </div> </div> Seems good enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446269#post1446269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theory: understanding rights as protected freedoms, might literally does make right because that is where rights come from. How else are they to be protected? The trappings of modern society distract us from the fact that force of law is how the government grants rights, so we delude ourselves in thinking we moved past this truth, as though we ever could. (Yes, the founder is fatalistic and cynical.) Mystical might makes factual right, given that mages can rewrite reality. If you value something like morality or ambition, speak truth to power and don't falter for cowardly excuses.</div> </div> </div> </div> Alright, I still see might makes right as empowering and drawing from the exarchs. The ones in question are the Father, the General, and the Raptor. The thing with the exarchs is anything that draws on their symbolism empowers them. The Father is all the words you accepted because of a logical fallacy. The General is every person who threatens violence to force a action.The Raptor is the cruelty inherent in nature where only the mighty should survive. Might makes right as a philosophy draws on all three. I think the founder might even be a closeted seer.<br /> <br /> This is not a bad thing. Arguably, one can reclaim the symbolism from the exarchs with legacies and ascension. I think that a duty coming with the power, to use power responsibly, would shift symbolism away from the exarchs. But I think that part should be up to the members who sign up, not the legacy itself. This is at least very close to the line separating diamond and seer. Again, that\u2019s not a bad thing. Gives more drama.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446269#post1446269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a certain point of view, that may have been bleak. In the Chronicles of Darkness it doesn't seem out of place.</div> </div> </div> </div> nah, it\u2019s perfect. Werewolf has plenty of might makes right in the pure and forsaken. For better or worse it\u2019s a very human philosophy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446269#post1446269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic<br /> <br /> Primary Arcanum: Prime<br /> Secondary Arcanum: Fate<br /> <br /> Still not sure what the Yantras and Oblations should be. I think they should be modeled after a more warlike version of the Acanthus symbolism, following the legends of heroes and gods in divine combat, need inspiration. Norse? At least that is fatalistic. Greco-Roman? Suitably glorious.</div> </div> </div> </div> If these are styled after champions, the a yantra of brawl or weaponry roll to get a plus two is not out of order. I think oblations would be winning a competition, (ie debate, fist fight, chess, etc... all of which are forms the duel might take). Another would be actually fighting the duel win or lose. Another might be practicing might makes right or something about the philosophy of the legacy. A fourth oblation could be practice with chosen style?<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t forget Orbimos, aka the mighty. They might like a legacy that says they are always right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446269#post1446269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading your review and answering follow-up questions, I will post my plan for how the Attainments should work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, do you plan on revamping the duel at all? Or using someone else\u2019s? It will help me with attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T21:51:41-07:00","id":1446911,"title":"","content":"TempleBuilder<br /> <br /> About the reality warping nature of the Duel.<br /> <br /> It did say that it &quot;literally&quot; made the winner more right. I don't think that in-universe the developers can use the term &quot;literally&quot; the way we do. The term can be used for hyperbole (though I don't like it) but how can you tell what is hyperbolic in an ultra-absurd setting? A werewolf can do battle with stationary like those from &quot;paper mario and the origami king&quot;, and it would make sense because the Hisil allows for that. If we seriously had to deal with that then the term &quot;literally&quot; would have to be regulated, because miscommunication can kill in this setting. <br /> <br /> Also, since when did writing symbols into the Supernal meant anything other than warping reality? The closest I can remember is the &quot;notice&quot; system for the Exarchal Dreams condition and the Exarchs are building a bridge to your soul.<br /> <br /> So no, I expect them to use these words for that meaning. In any case, I also expect them to comment on the Duel from time to time and provide more elaboration. Eventually we will know for certain who was right so I see little point in arguing about it further. This Legacy will continue with the assumption that reality is warped and if I am wrong then it can just continue to exist as headcanon, as it is now.<br /> <br /> Will post again tonight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T23:09:33-07:00","id":1446917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446274#post1446274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The text is:<br /> <br /> <i>winning<br /> a Duel Arcane literally makes one mage more right than the other,<br /> as <b>the symbol of their victory</b> is Truthfully written into the<br /> Supernal itself</i><br /> <br /> Emphasis mine. The Fallen concept here that becomes Supernally reinforced by the Duel Arcane seems to be &quot;I am the victor and you the loser&quot; rather than &quot;What I claim about (the subject) is right.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless you <i>did</i> mean that? If so, then you're right.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> About Yantras and Oblations... Hmm, well I already gave my ideas for now.</div> </div> </div> </div> Quoted so I can remember exact wording.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s late and I probably don\u2019t have the proper frame of reference or Mind for this, but I\u2019m pretty sure the reality warping you mentioned is completely limited to those conditions you get for winning or losing the duel. The Supernal gets written with, Victor and Loser, and the respective mage gets branded with the respective symbol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T01:19:52-07:00","id":1446927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1446917#post1446917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Quoted so I can remember exact wording.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s late and I probably don\u2019t have the proper frame of reference or Mind for this, but I\u2019m pretty sure the reality warping you mentioned is completely limited to those conditions you get for winning or losing the duel. The Supernal gets written with, Victor and Loser, and the respective mage gets branded with the respective symbol.</div> </div> </div> </div>We will see, anywho. <br /> <br /> The idea of this Legacy having exarchal resonance despite being opposed to them brings up some interesting questions. Before the Exarchs Ascended the Supernal must have somehow defined them as tyrants, assuming that is what they were. So just as other words are used to define any particular word, there must have been some pre-Exarch symbolism that allows brutal concepts, practices, and philosophies without referring to Them. But does it really work that way? We know enough about how the Hisil works to understand that not every spirit of broad phenomena is super powerful, commanding only a tiny portion of their purview until they excel at their ecology. What about the Supernal? If two synonymous concepts compete, how does the Supernal handle it?<br /> <br /> Great questions for another thread when I am done here, unless you guys think it worth debating here. Tomorrow I should get back to the actual mechanics. I will just assume that the Legacy does not automatically affirm the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T08:04:33-07:00","id":1446979,"title":"","content":"There is a old thread about the difference between spirits and Supernal Entities. It had a post from the line developer at the time. I will post the link if I can find it. I remember it boiling down to spirit getting broader as the get stronger, and Supernal entities getting purer.<br /> <br /> We probably should take the discussion out of this thread, I think it would only distract from the legacies at this point. We CAN keep it here, but I think it will get more views and comments if we take it outside.<br /> <br /> Well, even if it does affirm them, there is a argument to stealing the exarchs tools. One might, if they are careful, reclaim a portion of the exarchs power for themselves. It\u2019s playing with fire, but some risks have to be taken.<br /> <br /> Well, if you believe the Free Council, humans can make new symbols. Even if there were previous symbols of tyrants, the exarchs mantled them, and made them integral to the workings of the Supernal. The human origin of the exarchs are probably long dead for all intents and purposes, they are their symbolism now. Every Tetarch that ascends reinforces the Exarchs symbolism. The Exarchs probably absorb the new ascended being into themselves, so that they have no rivals.<br /> <br /> side note: the symbol of tyrants was chose because the nature of tyrants requires them to have power that they can use without limit. The Exarchs wanted absolute control over reality, so took the option that would let them use it however they wanted. It\u2019s intriguing that humanity plays such a central part in the Exarchs ideal world. Thanks to the Exarchs, humanity will always be important, groveling at the feet of their masters. The Exarchs, for all their power, NEED humanity to be oppressed in order to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T04:58:42-07:00","id":1447176,"title":"","content":"Okey then. <br /> <br /> I may have said something like this before, but now I should put it together. <br /> <br /> All the Attainments in this Legacy will be unusual. Not based on some conventional Praxis that you could practice for. <br /> <br /> Prime will provide an in-Duel advantage. Perhaps an opportunity to break another Door with an Exceptional Success? Or become immune to another offensive Arcanum with the same? I am thinking of allowing the use of Yantras in the Duel and containing the consequences of the same within the hypothetical space. Like &quot;sacrificing&quot; the same sacrament and &quot;breaking&quot; the same Obligation for power over and over again. There definitely needs to be some strict mechanics to make sense of Yantras in this context though. Since shielding powers tend to be the second dot I am thinking that the second Attainment should grant either a resistance or additional Doors equal to Prime. Not sure which. Just list a couple of options like I just did and eventually we will refine and cull this down to five.<br /> <br /> Fate will provide additional rules. So far I am thinking that it will be free if agreed upon by both parties or costing mana if not or if the other party did not understand what they were agreeing to. The detail I will not budge on is that it applies both ways. If the Duelist does not want to be cheated then she should not cheat. One option is the pledge of no cheating. If someone attempts to cheat then they will lose a Door, and successful cheating loses them the Duel. Another option is the pledge of the magnanimous. If the winner abuses the loser in anyway then they lose the Triumphant condition, or absent that suffer reciprocal abuse. Should the winner make meaningful reparations to the the loser, then the loser will lose the the Defeated condition and the winner receives a boon. Still work-shopping that. With your input we should get excellent pledges. <br /> <br /> To summarize: Prime breaks the rules (generally) and Fate makes the rules. All in favor of the Duelist of course. The finished product shouldn't have these two contradicting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T08:50:57-07:00","id":1447206,"title":"","content":"The corebook describes what the results of winning a Duel Arcane are; you gain the Triumphant Condition, giving your social rolls against other mages who are aware of your win exceptional success on three successes rather than five, and grants Beats (Arcane Beats?) when you throw your success in another mage's face. Meanwhile the loser of the Duel gains the Defeated Condition, which prevents them from spending Willpower or using magic to harm the one who beat them, and is subject to an immediately formed Strong sympathy.<br /> <br /> That is how the system represents the meaning of &quot;literally makes one mage more right than the other&quot;. I think a key thing of interpreting that statement is how it is confined to the relationship between two people.<br /> <br /> Consider also the fact that, while the symbol of your loss in the Supernal impedes your capacity to use magic, nothing stops you from, say, shooting the victor in their dumb face if the opportunity should arise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T11:03:41-07:00","id":1447236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1445182#post1445182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Duelists, how about an Attainment that lets them declare the Duel on non-Awakened?<br /> <br /> Quite potent and nasty, since very few beings would be able to counter that. Sleepers certainly can\u2019t, and neither can most Sleepwalkers. Proximi, and certain entities such as spirits and \u2018major templates\u2019 like vampires and werewolves might be able to do <i>something</i>, albeit still at a massive disadvantage.<br /> <br /> A related idea would be making this Duelist Legacy not limited to the Duel Arcane, and expanding its interests to the concept/symbol of The Duel itself. There\u2019s something poetic and evocative about two individuals, unwilling to bend, invoking sacred violence as the final testament of their willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I am going to back up 21C Hermit on this and recommend this. The fate component could in fact increase ALL dueling aspects, with strong boons to both sides if they duel 1v1, invoking the champion challenging the leader of the opposite army to a duel, and them accepting it.<br /> <br /> Prime could potentially bring the duel to anyone if they accept, even mortals who would temporarily have Quiescence suppressed. (Because forcing your opponent to have a mental breakdown during a cinematic fight is probably not good from a narrative standpoint.) Have Prime focus and intensify the conditions so the loser can\u2019t fight back after they lose.<br /> <br /> Both are mid range attainments, and can probably easily fit in the legacy. Just my two cents.<br /> <br /> Edit: Have the boons come into effect after the Duel, that way they can\u2019t effect the outcome of the duel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-03-2021, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T08:56:11-07:00","id":1448133,"title":"","content":"Maybe it was 21c Hermit's comments but one of you got me thinking back to material on balance and power creep. I just started remembering the sourcebook Legacies: the sublime. Near the end after all the Legacies were introduced it started offering advice on how to homebrew Legacies and one of its strongest points was to not create &quot;super&quot; Legacies, especially super combat Legacies.<br /> <br /> Never create Legacies, or really any content, that forces everyone to obtain the same just to compete. So &quot;super&quot; Legacies are only permissible if restricted in scope and focus. For example: you can make a Legacy about being the best mage fencers, because that doesn't translate to &quot;I win everytime&quot;.<br /> <br /> It also reminded me of the video on power creep from &quot;extra credits&quot;. That YouTube channel sounds like boring college homework but really they about game design. I highly recommend it. They taught me about the dangers of escalating power in perpetual games, which got me thinking about how Chronicles of Darkness handled it. The philosophy of &quot;choices, not obligations&quot; alongside a roughly proportional cost in exp and &quot;magic&quot; points helps. They especially used the logic of incomparables, features with a non-numeric relationship to each other, to great affect. Unlike some MMORPG, characters are created and discarded with regularity so you never permanently out-level some feature. My tangential musings don't do it justice, so watch the actual video if what I said intrigued you.<br /> <br /> Back to Legacies. I wanted to create a super Legacy, but I also wanted it to be a playable concept that avoided dragon-ball logic and going super saiyan and shit like that. To justify really strong Attainments I would need to really focus it, but some gimmick like fencing would not cut it. I needed something both narrow and important to really shine. You guys (or at least one of you) complained about how limited the Duel Arcane is, when that was the point. It is also indisputable important, not just because of its power to limit casualties but also to claim an unofficial authority. If you can press an issue to the point of Dueling and win everytime until mages just give up and start pleading for a good deal, then you are a pseudo-Hierarch. Yet these skills can tempt others to resort to blackmail, assassination, and other tricks that these Attainments are worthless against, because you are not actually a better fighter in normal combat. This means that the Legacy does not immunize against uncertainty and drama, the necessities of engaging stories. <br /> <br /> Maybe I rambled too much, I just want to make clear why I will not dilute the themes by making the Duel all-applicable. This is a specialist Legacy. It was never meant to be brought beyond that scope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T10:11:51-07:00","id":1448139,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve got a final in a few minutes, but dark eras 2 has rules for bringing Changelings into the duel. Just add a fate component, that interprets their contracts as arcanum, and arcanum as hostile oaths. They are actually more powerful than mages at the duel early on, but have less options for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T19:53:11-07:00","id":1448287,"title":"","content":"So, for the Duelists (y\u2019know I kinda like this name after all) a focus on the Duel Arcane, not just Duels in general? \u201cI\u2019m\u201d gonna need some brain-works to expand upon it...<br /> <br /> For now, aside from strengthening your own Doors and involving non-Awakened on the Duel, I\u2019m thinking of alternate forms of the Duel. Like... a riddle contest? A cook-off, maybe? (Then again cook off is more about me going to fix myself lunch now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T20:25:28-07:00","id":1448289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448287#post1448287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For now, aside from strengthening your own Doors and involving non-Awakened on the Duel, I\u2019m thinking of alternate forms of the Duel. Like... a riddle contest? A cook-off, maybe? (Then again cook off is more about me going to fix myself lunch now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow Chess is a variant I've always been rather fond of, for all that it's a little\u2026 involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.the