by":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T20:53:15-07:00","id":1448292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448290#post1448290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh? We had \u2018Chess Arcane\u2019 or something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it\u2019s a duel using Pok\u00e9mon... I mean spirits in the shadow. Since spirits can\u2019t really die, is really that cruel to let them fight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T21:39:43-07:00","id":1448296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448290#post1448290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? We had \u2018Chess Arcane\u2019 or something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tome of the Mysteries, p124, sidebar.<br /> <br /> It's a modification of the standard spell for the Duel Arcane so that your &quot;sword&quot; generates temporary spirits called Dueling Pawns running on the same basic aesthetic guidelines as Spirit Manse; your &quot;shield&quot; works normally but you can also maneuver within the dueling space to physically avoid attacks, and on any given turn you can use your sword to create a Pawn, enhance an existing one, or command any number of Pawns to attack or defend other targets in the dueling space; your active Pawns can have &quot;damage&quot; diverted from you to them at cost to their Resistance (being destroyed when it hits zero), and any attack they make against non-spirits does damage in the normal way a Duel works.<br /> <br /> It's less Pok\u00e9mon and more tactical RPG with extra Nimbus flavor, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T21:47:37-07:00","id":1448297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448296#post1448296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tome of the Mysteries, p124, sidebar.<br /> <br /> It's a modification of the standard spell for the Duel Arcane so that your &quot;sword&quot; generates temporary spirits called Dueling Pawns running on the same basic aesthetic guidelines as Spirit Manse; your &quot;shield&quot; works normally but you can also maneuver within the dueling space to physically avoid attacks, and on any given turn you can use your sword to create a Pawn, enhance an existing one, or command any number of Pawns to attack or defend other targets in the dueling space; your active Pawns can have &quot;damage&quot; diverted from you to them at cost to their Resistance (being destroyed when it hits zero), and any attack they make against non-spirits does damage in the normal way a Duel works.<br /> <br /> It's less Pok\u00e9mon and more tactical RPG with extra Nimbus flavor, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, could have sworn there was a duel option using \u201creal\u201d spirits... but that does sound much more interesting than the normal duel. Honestly, any more depth to the duel is a good thing in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T22:28:16-07:00","id":1448298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448292#post1448292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe it\u2019s a duel using Pok\u00e9mon... I mean spirits in the shadow. Since spirits can\u2019t really die, is really that cruel to let them fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>It involves the usurpation of the free will of sentient beings to settle disputes, forcing them to fight to the death, because the mage is ok with their pain since he took the necessary precautions to ensure they survive the torturous experience. Its an Act of Hubris to be sure, but a Legacy Attainment can void that problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T22:32:17-07:00","id":1448299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448298#post1448298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It involves the usurpation of the free will of sentient beings to settle disputes, forcing them to fight to the death, because the mage is ok with their pain since he took the necessary precautions to ensure they survive the torturous experience. Its an Act of Hubris to be sure, but a Legacy Attainment can void that problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, it was mostly a joke about Pok\u00e9mon morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T16:57:56-07:00","id":1448914,"title":"","content":"It can't be a fight to the death if all participants survive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T05:59:37-07:00","id":1448971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448299#post1448299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know, it was mostly a joke about Pok\u00e9mon morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently the pokemon can just leave their trainers if unsatisfied for whatever reason. Happened in-show but never the game because that may be frustrating for the player. Since I am not an expert you can take it all with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> Now back to Legacies. You guys were really interested in or convinced that the Seers and the Thearchs should also obtain this Legacy. Now I realize an ambiguity. To get into a Legacy the mage must match it either in Path, Order or Praxis for the first Attainment. The Legacy's Path is determined respective to the founder and the Praxis by whatever spell served as the base for the first Attainment. Yet where do does it ever clarify how the Order is determined? This not a trivial question since this Legacy has no Praxis for the first Attainment and therefore would get locked solely in the Acanthus Path otherwise. I have guesses and assumptions and theories as probably do you all, but I acknowledge that I have no confirmation on how it works. Can anyone in the Order join once one of their members gets it? What about an infiltrator to the Order? How does actual loyalties affect the mages ability to call on an Order's symbolism? Odds are that will be a separate thread.<br /> <br /> Back to Attainments. Working model:<br /> <br /> The first one allows Yantras, further rules to be refined. Considering making Dedication a requirement. <br /> <br /> The second one acts as a shield. Whether in the form of additional Doors or a penalty to offensive magic.<br /> <br /> The third one expands on Arcana immunity from evading damage by adding another option for obtaining it. Not decided if the enemy is aware of such.<br /> <br /> The fourth forces the enemy to pay for their offers with their own Doors, if failed the Duelist must sacrifice a Door as usual. <br /> <br /> The fifth is some kind of terrible offensive power. Considering using the rote quality for using an attribute rated above five dots. <br /> <br /> As for pledges? One idea is the chance to end the Duel and escape for another time, but attempting should be risky with high stakes on your Doors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T21:29:28-07:00","id":1449616,"title":"","content":"Guys? Have you all dropped from the thread? I wasn't even done yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T22:37:13-07:00","id":1449618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1449616#post1449616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys? Have you all dropped from the thread? I wasn't even done yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure most of 'us' were waiting for something else <i>you'd</i> write - I mean, you were the OP and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T13:23:50-07:00","id":1449695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448971#post1448971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apparently the pokemon can just leave their trainers if unsatisfied for whatever reason. Happened in-show but never the game because that may be frustrating for the player. Since I am not an expert you can take it all with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> Now back to Legacies. You guys were really interested in or convinced that the Seers and the Thearchs should also obtain this Legacy. Now I realize an ambiguity. To get into a Legacy the mage must match it either in Path, Order or Praxis for the first Attainment. The Legacy's Path is determined respective to the founder and the Praxis by whatever spell served as the base for the first Attainment. Yet where do does it ever clarify how the Order is determined? This not a trivial question since this Legacy has no Praxis for the first Attainment and therefore would get locked solely in the Acanthus Path otherwise. I have guesses and assumptions and theories as probably do you all, but I acknowledge that I have no confirmation on how it works. Can anyone in the Order join once one of their members gets it? What about an infiltrator to the Order? How does actual loyalties affect the mages ability to call on an Order's symbolism? Odds are that will be a separate thread.</div> </div> </div> </div> To be fair, that was mostly me. I kinda ignore how Mages might Obtain Legacies when determining who would have the Legacy. It's Mages, somehow they are going to obtain the shiny magical power if only to examine. I always use who would WANT the Legacy. Fact is, this Legacy has real Narrow but Strong power. It's Philosophy fits both the Seers and the Adamantine Arrow, and The Silver Ladder would be interested in it from a practical standpoint. Free Council might have individuals interested, and Mysterium would probably want to store the legacy for safe keeping, the the Guardians would probably only use it to infiltrate one of the other groups and shun it otherwise.<br /> Soul Stones ignore all other requirements, I think.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448971#post1448971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to Attainments. Working model:<br /> <br /> The first one allows Yantras, further rules to be refined. Considering making Dedication a requirement.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds like a Weaving to me, adding Yantras Properties to the Duel. Maybe do something else for this Attainment, and put this as the third Attainment?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448971#post1448971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second one acts as a shield. Whether in the form of additional Doors or a penalty to offensive magic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Shielding, obviously. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448971#post1448971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The third one expands on Arcana immunity from evading damage by adding another option for obtaining it. Not decided if the enemy is aware of such.</div> </div> </div> </div> umm, what? Could you re explain this one? Are you wanting Another Shielding effect?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448971#post1448971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fourth forces the enemy to pay for their offers with their own Doors, if failed the Duelist must sacrifice a Door as usual.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, that's neat. Sever Oaths is probably what you want to base it on. Also Legacy Attainments don't roll for their Attainment, so this can't fail to my knowledge.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448971#post1448971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fifth is some kind of terrible offensive power. Considering using the rote quality for using an attribute rated above five dots.</div> </div> </div> </div> I personally don't like dice modifiers as attainments they are kinda boring. Maybe have the person Use Multiple Arcanum at one time?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1448971#post1448971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for pledges? One idea is the chance to end the Duel and escape for another time, but attempting should be risky with high stakes on your Doors.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1449616#post1449616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys? Have you all dropped from the thread? I wasn't even done yet.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was busy when I first looked at this thread...and kinda forgot you posted something afterward. My bad.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T00:49:05-07:00","id":1450672,"title":"","content":"Before I fully delved into the effort of refining this Legacy I reviewed the rules of both Legacies and the Duel Arcane. I even did it again and found subtle details I missed. I bring this up because I am actually shocked that you didn't meticulously review as well.<br /> <br /> No, the particular source of initiation whether a living tutor or otherwise does not remove the requirements of initiation.<br /> <br /> No, I am not going to restrict myself to the practices because I already decided to make my Attainments strange Attainments. This means I just have to be concerned about staying in the Ruling Arcanum and comparable power range. I know there are some advantages to using Praxis as a base but I will bite that bullet.<br /> <br /> Arcana immunity is referring to the rule that you cannot offensively use the same Arcanum on the same Door again. It is easy to deduce that this may result in a cycle of terror and relief as you are running out of Arcana to throw at your foe only to crack her defenses and find your options returning. If you run out then you will have to go pure defensive while your foe goes pure offensive so the Duel will quickly end or stall. This is why the negotiation mechanics is vital to getting it moving again. <br /> <br /> No, Sever Oaths belongs to the Fate Arcanum and sometimes Attainments do roll dice. To be fair, I couldn't find any clear mention of when Attainments behave this way rulewise.<br /> <br /> I find rereading the material fascinating because I notice things I didn't before. For entering the Legacy by way of Praxis you get one mundane experience and one arcane beat, but it also says cashing in your Praxis for Attainments gets you one arcane experience and beat. I am assuming that the initiation was an exception rather than a mistake. I used to think I couldn't make a Legacy Attainment indefinite and even commented on these forums likewise, but checking again I appear to have been wrong.<br /> <br /> Thinking of another pledge...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T09:15:13-07:00","id":1450691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450672#post1450672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I fully delved into the effort of refining this Legacy I reviewed the rules of both Legacies and the Duel Arcane. I even did it again and found subtle details I missed. I bring this up because I am actually shocked that you didn't meticulously review as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Look, I know you are probably very excited about this, but it's been a month and some change. With one post a week from you, it's hard to maintain emotional and intellectual interest. This isn't meant to attack you, you probably have a very good reason to do so, just to explain the reality of the situation. I did do both of those things... a month ago. But I'm forgetful, and busy now. Secondly, you really didn't post any specific information. It's hard to comment when there is just so little there. These all being strange attainments doesn't help at all.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450672#post1450672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the particular source of initiation whether a living tutor or otherwise does not remove the requirements of initiation.</div> </div> </div> </div> So you are saying that a Guardian of the Veil can't teach a Free Councilor despite their orders rejecting it. If this was true, nobody would care about such things, because it wouldn't work. That's both a very strict reading of the rules, and unhelpful to the game in my opinion. A tutor teaching someone outside the orders should count as if they were in the order specifically for weird legacies without a Praxis. Otherwise Legacies could never be unattached to a mage's personal symbolism if they made it themselves.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450672#post1450672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I am not going to restrict myself to the practices because I already decided to make my Attainments strange Attainments. This means I just have to be concerned about staying in the Ruling Arcanum and comparable power range. I know there are some advantages to using Praxis as a base but I will bite that bullet.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, you are not going to get a lot of help that way. I have made 4 legacies, all use strange attainments at some point. I got the least comments on those, because they have the least rules. Your best bet is to have normal attainments, until they are activated in the duel arcane. This both gets you the effect you want, and gives the legacy a use outside the Duel, which they desperately need. As someone outside your head, I do not have any real way to help you if you abandon the Legacy regular rules. This is also the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1443545#post1443545\">best advice</a> I have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1443700#post1443700\">been given</a> on legacy creation. I strongly advise you use it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450672#post1450672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcana immunity is referring to the rule that you cannot offensively use the same Arcanum on the same Door again. It is easy to deduce that this may result in a cycle of terror and relief as you are running out of Arcana to throw at your foe only to crack her defenses and find your options returning. If you run out then you will have to go pure defensive while your foe goes pure offensive so the Duel will quickly end or stall. This is why the negotiation mechanics is vital to getting it moving again.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh yeah, Turtling. Yeah this legacy is going to break the duel into splinters.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450672#post1450672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Sever Oaths belongs to the Fate Arcanum and sometimes Attainments do roll dice. To be fair, II couldn't find any clear mention of when Attainments behave this way rulewise.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes it is. This is a Prime/Fate and you should use Fate optional Attainments at some point. The reason why I suggested sever oaths is because it alters the rules of the agreement, in a Fate way. The only time they roll dice is in the Clash of Wills, everything else is automatically successful. Now it may be withstood, but that doesn't roll dice.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450672#post1450672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find rereading the material fascinating because I notice things I didn't before. For entering the Legacy by way of Praxis you get one mundane experience and one arcane beat, but it also says cashing in your Praxis for Attainments gets you one arcane experience and beat. I am assuming that the initiation was an exception rather than a mistake. I used to think I couldn't make a Legacy Attainment indefinite and even commented on these forums likewise, but checking again I appear to have been wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually go the opposite way and say that is clearly a mistake. Being wrong is part of Life, only thing that matters is what we learn from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 06-03-2021, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T23:58:36-07:00","id":1450919,"title":"","content":"Alright then, I didn't realize you guys minded the pace so much. Should have complained earlier. I do have other things to do but I can push it up to a post a day, or two days if I am feeling lazy. I hope to finish by next week because I too want to move on.<br /> <br /> Thankfully you are wrong about the requirements of initiation for you have forgotten the magical word &quot;or&quot;. What a word. Path, Order, or Praxis are more options rather than restrictions. Were you desperately searching for a work around because you missed this piece? Because I wouldn't blame you if that was the information you thought you had to work with.<br /> <br /> As for Arcana immunity second option I am considering making it that the breaking of another Door. I might add the restriction of an Exceptional success. Maybe I will also add the trade-away of mana or excess successes. Depends on how well you make the case.<br /> <br /> I was thinking that the consequences of Yantras could be purely simulated, then I realized I would have to translate those consequences to broken Doors so I am open to suggestions to resolve that. Maybe instead the first Attainment could be about an opening strike or advantage to start the Duel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T01:05:39-07:00","id":1450922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450919#post1450919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright then, I didn't realize you guys minded the pace so much. Should have complained earlier. I do have other things to do but I can push it up to a post a day, or two days if I am feeling lazy. I hope to finish by next week because I too want to move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>People don't generally complain when their interest vanes unless they're absolutely hooked. Rather, they tend to forget, so complaining becomes an impossibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thankfully you are wrong about the requirements of initiation for you have forgotten the magical word &amp;quot;or&amp;quot;. What a word. Path, Order, or Praxis are more options rather than restrictions. Were you desperately searching for a work around because you missed this piece? Because I wouldn't blame you if that was the information you thought you had to work with. </div> </div> </div>No one said you need to fulfil two or more of those requirements. The discussion was about how the Order requirement comes into being.<br /> <br /> Personally I think having Path/Order be a hard requirement is semi-nonsensical and much prefer to see it as how someone may join the Legacy more legitimately. If someone, regardless of Path and Order, manages to find a Daimonomikon, Soul Stone or Soul of a Legacy member, or a willing/&quot;willing&quot; tutor, they could absolutely join that Legacy in my games.<br /> In fact, even though by RAW you definitely need to fulfil Path, Order or have an equivalent Praxis, I'm having doubts it's supposed to be a hard rule. Rather, the intention might be that you have to follow those rule to join a Legacy without having to procure one of the methods of initiation during play.<br /> <br /> As for refunding Praxes: It makes more sense you get an Arcane Experience (and an Arcane Beat) since only Arcane Experiences can be used to buy Praxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T05:27:17-07:00","id":1450949,"title":"","content":"There is also the concern of why anyone would Duel such a mage. Since the effects of the Attainments are very overt, they will become evident by the end of the first bout. The Duel Arcane is a matter that needs to be authorized by the Consilium, often happening as a public event and always recorded by the Lex. Therefore keeping a low profile is improbable.<br /> <br /> The purpose of the Duel Arcane is to act as a final conflict resolution method, a way to prevent escalation when traditional mediation has failed. When people know that someone is specialized in the Duel, they may refuse to engage them. Since a mage who chose this Legacy is likely Duel happy, it means more escalation, which is a net loss for the Consilium. In which case, it would make sense to issue a law where the mage's opponent may demand they appoint a proxy in their stead and another that states that the mage themselves can only act as a proxy to another Duel if both parties agree. All this would lead to a very weird dynamic to how the character may approach it.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I agree that basing the Attainments on more traditional spells might be better. Not only does this make calibrating for balance a lot simpler, but also forces you to contemplate the nuances of how to build your toolkit to better synergize for the Duel. How do they plan to get the time to setup such abilities? What is the general modus operandi of their approach, honorable, utilitarian, something else ? Right now its not clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-04-2021, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T08:53:36-07:00","id":1450960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450919#post1450919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright then, I didn't realize you guys minded the pace so much. Should have complained earlier. I do have other things to do but I can push it up to a post a day, or two days if I am feeling lazy. I hope to finish by next week because I too want to move on.</div> </div> </div> </div> Look, please don\u2019t neglect real life. I would like like you to have a faster update schedule, but not at a cost to you. Like I said, that wasn\u2019t supposed to be a attack. It was noting why I didn\u2019t \u201cmeticulously review as well\u201d. I have a tendency to come off as more aggressive and negative then I want. I\u2019m sorry I gave you the wrong impression. This is a interesting legacy, and I want to see the final result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450919#post1450919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thankfully you are wrong about the requirements of initiation for you have forgotten the magical word &quot;or&quot;. What a word. Path, Order, or Praxis are more options rather than restrictions. Were you desperately searching for a work around because you missed this piece? Because I wouldn't blame you if that was the information you thought you had to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually I didn\u2019t. I\u2019m not sure if you intended this but your phrasing seems condescending or passive aggressive. So I\u2019m going to ignore that. I do not believe in rules as worded being the best way to run a game. Personally I believe that the initiation rules are too strict for Mage. Magic is so personal in this that any member of any path can be called to a legacy. Sure it will be tinted by their path, and many legacies would have a strong bias towards the \u201cnormal\u201d legacy members, but unless the legacy clearly states they only accept a certain path or order, I think anyone should be able to learn from a teacher. The initiation rules are also the least important part of the Legacy. The yantras, and oblations do more for the legacy than the initiation rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450919#post1450919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Arcana immunity second option I am considering making it that the breaking of another Door. I might add the restriction of an Exceptional success. Maybe I will also add the trade-away of mana or excess successes. Depends on how well you make the case.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe lift the restrictions on multiple doors being lifted in exchange for being immune to a extra Arcanum per attack or after a door has been lifted, chose one arcanum to start immune to. Have the choice of adding it to your opponent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450919#post1450919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking that the consequences of Yantras could be purely simulated, then I realized I would have to translate those consequences to broken Doors so I am open to suggestions to resolve that. Maybe instead the first Attainment could be about an opening strike or advantage to start the Duel.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would say make it so they always go first, and then give them a bonus for it. Maybe the informed condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 06-04-2021, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T01:35:29-07:00","id":1451028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1450922#post1450922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People don't generally complain when their interest vanes unless they're absolutely hooked. Rather, they tend to forget, so complaining becomes an impossibility.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No one said you need to fulfil two or more of those requirements. The discussion was about how the Order requirement comes into being.<br /> <br /> Personally I think having Path/Order be a hard requirement is semi-nonsensical and much prefer to see it as how someone may join the Legacy more legitimately. If someone, regardless of Path and Order, manages to find a Daimonomikon, Soul Stone or Soul of a Legacy member, or a willing/&amp;quot;willing&amp;quot; tutor, they could absolutely join that Legacy in my games.<br /> In fact, even though by RAW you definitely need to fulfil Path, Order or have an equivalent Praxis, I'm having doubts it's supposed to be a hard rule. Rather, the intention might be that you have to follow those rule to join a Legacy without having to procure one of the methods of initiation during play.<br /> <br /> As for refunding Praxes: It makes more sense you get an Arcane Experience (and an Arcane Beat) since only Arcane Experiences can be used to buy Praxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got confused there for a bit. Now I think I got it. You are thinking that maybe the creators should not have bothered making the Path/Order/Praxis requirements?<br /> <br /> Even if that is not what you mean I have found absolutely no evidence that it is anything other than a hard rule, so of course that is my &quot;interpretation&quot;. You seem to have come to the conclusion that the Path/Order/Praxis can replace the methods of initiation but I can't find that anywhere. My understanding is that the methods represent ways of accessing the Legacy and are essential regardless of how eligible you are.<br /> <br /> I have no grounded explanation for why the Path/Order/Praxis thing is a thing, though I have headcanon. Maybe there needs to be some kind of symbolic link to serve as the axis of a rearranging Gnosis, a still point to keep it all grounded. Sure it is hot air, here's what isn't: it is precedented that summoned Supernal/Abyssal entities can help connect mages to Legacies. So if you really need to then let's say there is a Supernal service you can call to circumvent those issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T01:52:53-07:00","id":1451029,"title":"","content":"TempleBuilder<br /> <br /> I think you failed to notice that an exceptional success in an attack in the Duel does not open multiple Doors. I blame how it is superficially a social maneuver turned aggressive for this mistake. What really happens is that your next spell is blessed for how excessive you were.<br /> <br /> Still, I think you are onto something for making the option have a cost. Perhaps when an Exceptional Success happens you could forgo the blessing for something else. Maybe we could do something like that for the final Attainment, versatility rather than raw power on all points. Maybe make the dice bonus from breaking Doors a currency or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T05:44:52-07:00","id":1451044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1451028#post1451028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to have come to the conclusion that the Path/Order/Praxis can replace the methods of initiation but I can't find that anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not what I'm saying.<br /> There are two parts to joining a Legacy (ignoring general trait limits on Gnosis and Arcana): Fulfilling a prerequisite, and going through initiation.<br /> 1.) The prerequisites (sharing Path with the originator, being part of an associated Order, or having an equivalent Praxis) is horribly underexplained. Does these limits exist within the setting, or are they artificial limits imposed on the game?<br /> 1.a.) If it's the former, how does the associated Order prerequisite form? And why do these limits exist in-setting?<br /> 1.b.) But if it's instead an artificial prerequisite placed on the game that doesn't reflect the setting, then it makes a lot more sense that fulfilling one of the prerequisites merely means you don't have to go out of your way to steal a Daimonomikon or Soul Stone or Soul; you're just accepted and either get to read a Daimonomikon or get a tutor assigned to you or just do whatever the Legacy does to initiate new members.<br /> By RAW it's definitely the former because any exceptions aren't detailed, but it's also very dissatisfying because of how underexplained it is. And anyone who has enough experience with 2e CofD books knows that much of what's written doesn't accurately reflect what the writers intended because OPP doesn't seem to have a developmental editing phase to catch such stuff in their process. What I mean is, if anything in CofD feels underexplained, there's a good chance it actually is and that RAW (rules as written) does not match RAI (rules as intended).<br /> <br /> 2.) Initiation, however, is very adequately explained. You always have to go through initiation because that's how it's done in-setting. What I'm saying is that you can gloss over that part (meaning, it happens in the game, but you don't have to play it out since it's not interesting to play) if the character is just accepted by the other members of the Legacy due to having shown enough aptitude or shared values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T07:02:14-07:00","id":1451049,"title":"","content":"I always saw the originating Path and Order as diplomatic facilitators. If you are of the same Order or Path, a mentor will be much more compelled to teach them. This does not restrict others from being thought, they just need to put more time and work into convincing a teacher. This means than a member of the Guardians that wants to learn a Silver Ladder Legacy can gain that tutelage easily should they have bought one dot of Order Status:Silver Ladder or earned enough respect through their actions.<br /> <br /> Some Legacies are actively suppressed outside and/or inside their Orders. The Guardians of the Veil tend to target ones that make it more difficult for them to obtain intel on their targets (the Bearers of the Eternal Voice are one example) or that make parsing out the truth on their terms more difficult (such as the Eleventh Question). The Arrow would actively work against the propagation of any Legacies that cleave to Vedantus principles, due to the fundamental incompatibility with their philosophy. In order for outsiders to obtain mentors in these cases, it would probably require a major boon from the teacher or Order.<br /> <br /> Finally, a mage can always try to appropriate the knowledge. Stealing a Daimonomika, mentally controlling a mentor, procuring souls and soul stones from traffickers allow the mage to initiate themselves into it. Such an usurpation will certainly earn the ire of other members once it comes to light, if not outright escalation due to them becoming a sympathetic liability. <br /> <br /> In summary, the originating Path and Order represent the path of least resistence for the mage to be taught, other approaches carry their own set of complications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-05-2021, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T09:19:26-07:00","id":1451059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1451029#post1451029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TempleBuilder<br /> <br /> I think you failed to notice that an exceptional success in an attack in the Duel does not open multiple Doors. I blame how it is superficially a social maneuver turned aggressive for this mistake. What really happens is that your next spell is blessed for how excessive you were.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah I did notice actually, I was suggesting that the defense get much stronger at the cost of effectively lowering health through allowing multiple doors being removed. That would simulate Quick Draw and Iaijutsu Duels. In retrospect, I think the cost might be way too high.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1451029#post1451029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I think you are onto something for making the option have a cost. Perhaps when an Exceptional Success happens you could forgo the blessing for something else. Maybe we could do something like that for the final Attainment, versatility rather than raw power on all points. Maybe make the dice bonus from breaking Doors a currency or something.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm biased to Power with a Cost, I think every legacy I have made has the concept somewhere. I think the best way to go about it for the duelists is trade-offs. Increase speed, lower attack. Increase defense, lower speed. Increase attack, maybe remove a previous immunity. I don't know, I just think it's interesting to have more options for the duel.<br /> <br /> As for the Initiation mechanics, I think it comes down to personal preference. If you want a setting where some people can't join a certain legacy even if they really want to because of the restrictions on legacy and weird first attainments, use the rules in the book. If you prefer a more liberal setting, allow tutors or tutoring objects get around the restrictions. I prefer the latter, mostly because I don't find the former interesting. Even in cases where the legacy only accepts a single path, it often fails at using that paths symbolism well (*cough* 1e Roses of Eden *cough*). The legacies that only come from a single order then to do a bit better with order symbolism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T03:04:51-07:00","id":1452299,"title":"","content":"Had some issues this past week, made my way here again at 2 A.M. I just missed these forums. <br /> <br /> You guys surprised me with the interpretation of Path/Order/Praxis being diplomatic facilitators and I needed a day to wrap my head around that. I never came across that before. What's next, someone going to say that the Clan requirements for Kindred Bloodlines is optional too? It seemed utterly arbitrary to me. Eventually I began to measure it more precisely and even revisited the rules. <br /> <br /> Having done that, I am not sure your interpretation is even possible. Because I still don't know how Legacies get attached to Orders enough to allow initiation I can't say your completely wrong for certain. The other two options are a bit different though. Legacies always have a Path option linked to the founder, this shouldn't always be the case if it was a matter of diplomacy. Perhaps a founder had a sacred mission he would never entrust to another mage just because they shared a Path and his Order agreed to keep the Legacy for said mission. According to the rules it is going to still have the Path as an option for initiation anyway, so what is going on here if you are correct? <br /> <br /> Praxis makes the least sense of all. Having neither the shared experience of a Path or shared ideology of an Order, who would trust a mage who merely prepared to receive the first Attainment? If the creators meant what you said instead then why did they mention nothing of diplomacy? The language of the section sounds pretty definitive, using &quot;must&quot; and &quot;requirement&quot; to describe the Path and Order options. They said it was &quot;possible&quot; to enter with a Praxis and it could fail due to &quot;unusual Attainments&quot; rather than anything related to diplomacy.<br /> <br /> I am not interested in arguing any further though. The games are customizable anyway because no one polices the sessions but Storytellers who don't always prioritize tradition. As far as I am concerned a Supernal Boon solves the problem, I assumed anyone else would arrive at the same conclusion. Just do what makes you happy.<br /> <br /> As for the the first Attainment. I am thinking that a Duelist can bank the extra successes from breaking Doors so that she can build more Doors to protect herself. Before she attempts the next spell she must decide how much of the bonus she wants to keep and how much she wants to invest in Door making. The question then is how many are needed. Perhaps ten minus Prime dots? Eleven minus the lesser of Resolve and Composure?<br /> <br /> Another Pledge came to mind. Probably going to be the fifth one. Whoever wins the Duel can cast a spell as an Attainment to enforce the terms of the Duel. For the purposes of Factors and Reach assume it is a fifth dot Attainment. Just as Legacy Attainments can be limited or expanded in scope to match the Theory the same is true with this spell-as-Attainment and whatever would help claim the prize, arbitrated by the Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T05:20:19-07:00","id":1452307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1452299#post1452299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had some issues this past week, made my way here again at 2 A.M. I just missed these forums. <br /> <br /> You guys surprised me with the interpretation of Path/Order/Praxis being diplomatic facilitators and I needed a day to wrap my head around that. I never came across that before. What's next, someone going to say that the Clan requirements for Kindred Bloodlines is optional too? It seemed utterly arbitrary to me. Eventually I began to measure it more precisely and even revisited the rules. <br /> <br /> Having done that, I am not sure your interpretation is even possible. Because I still don't know how Legacies get attached to Orders enough to allow initiation I can't say your completely wrong for certain. The other two options are a bit different though. Legacies always have a Path option linked to the founder, this shouldn't always be the case if it was a matter of diplomacy. Perhaps a founder had a sacred mission he would never entrust to another mage just because they shared a Path and his Order agreed to keep the Legacy for said mission. According to the rules it is going to still have the Path as an option for initiation anyway, so what is going on here if you are correct? <br /> <br /> Praxis makes the least sense of all. Having neither the shared experience of a Path or shared ideology of an Order, who would trust a mage who merely prepared to receive the first Attainment? If the creators meant what you said instead then why did they mention nothing of diplomacy? The language of the section sounds pretty definitive, using &quot;must&quot; and &quot;requirement&quot; to describe the Path and Order options. They said it was &quot;possible&quot; to enter with a Praxis and it could fail due to &quot;unusual Attainments&quot; rather than anything related to diplomacy.<br /> <br /> I am not interested in arguing any further though. The games are customizable anyway because no one polices the sessions but Storytellers who don't always prioritize tradition. As far as I am concerned a Supernal Boon solves the problem, I assumed anyone else would arrive at the same conclusion. Just do what makes you happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you should try reading the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw2e p197</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Path, Order or Praxis: All Legacies possess an originating Path, and many (though not all) are connected to an Order. <br /> Normally, your mage must either belong to the Legacy\u2019s Path or Order. <b>However, it is possible for a mage of any Path or Order to join a Legacy if she learns a Praxis that duplicates the Legacy\u2019s first Attainment, and utilizes one of the Legacy\u2019s Yantras. She develops the understanding to join without other requirements.</b> <br /> Note that some Legacies possess unusual Attainments that make this impossible. Once she learns the Legacy\u2019s first Attainment, she loses the Praxis it duplicates but receives one standard Experience and one Arcane Beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is clear and unambiguous: either meet the Path or Order reqs or know the praxis and use a yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T06:00:30-07:00","id":1452311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1452307#post1452307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe you should try reading the book:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is clear and unambiguous: either meet the Path or Order reqs or know the praxis and use a yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel this tone would be uncalled for in any case, but it stands out particularly when addressed at a post that it appears to have not properly read or understood.<br /> <br /> Namely that Excess is not disputing the prerequisites for learning Legacies, but KaiserAfini's suggestion that they constitute a soft limit based on cultural values.<br /> <br /> As far as the in-character basis for learning Legacies goes, I feel the logic of it is distributed in a few places.<br /> <br /> The description of Gnosis itself refers to what it feels like per Path; the substance of one's Supernal connection and how it affects insights and outlook. I find that to make sense as a necessary basis to both understand and internalise the nature of the shaping of Gnosis entailed by initiating into and progressing through a Legacy; that there are mystical insights that just can't be communicated to people of another Path, deeper than the simple need to translate the semiotics of Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> The description of Praxis refers to how it's an Imago of such familiarity and significance to the mage that they gain greater insight into it and it exerts a shaping effect upon their Gnosis. I can follow the logic that says that such insight can become a hook for the Legacy mentor to impart its teachings to a mage who otherwise would have no means of internalising them, although notably a Praxis cannot be the basis for actually originating the Legacy.<br /> <br /> Order is one I admit needs to be taken more from what the game as a whole has said rather than specifically what the core had available wordcount for*, but it bears remembering that the Orders are more than just political associations; their ideologies emerge from actual recognition of mystical qualities of reality and engaging in practice and ritual that aligns one to them. That's notably how things like Masques and Egregore are able to work; the capacity to have a Medium sympathetic connection to every single member of the Mysterium while present in one of their communal spaces is not the result of spells, it's because their ideas about magic being alive are actually on to something and living in accordance with that principle allows one to connect to it. The Mysterium book goes so far to say that mages who leave the Order ultimately lose their egregore benefits because it can be reasonably presumed that they're no longer living in accordance with those practices and it results in disengaging from the communal element. In any case, that would also be a basis for Supernal insight into using Legacy practices to shape Gnosis, so long as the Legacy's nature is one that incorporates certain Order perspectives.<br /> <br /> * As far as complaints about how elaborate the description of Legacies is, I would point out that Dave Brookshaw has reported that other things needed to be cut from this book in order for the description of Legacies to be included <i>at all</i>, something that Requiem and Forsaken didn't even get with their Z-splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T22:21:45-07:00","id":1452417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1452299#post1452299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys surprised me with the interpretation of Path/Order/Praxis being diplomatic facilitators and I needed a day to wrap my head around that. I never came across that before. What's next, someone going to say that the Clan requirements for Kindred Bloodlines is optional too? It seemed utterly arbitrary to me. Eventually I began to measure it more precisely and even revisited the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not clearly stated anywhere in 2e to my knowledge. It <i>is</i> however, overtly stated in 1e that Legacy order requirements are a political consideration. Was that intentionally changed? Certainly possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T00:52:15-07:00","id":1452428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1452417#post1452417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that intentionally changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, First Edition had it that Path and Order associations were just commonalities, but anybody with the correct mentor could actually be inducted. Second Edition has made the requirements more rigid, hence why a Praxis is needed outside of them.<br /> <br /> I actually think most people before read it as given that Legacies were restrictive anyway, so the explicit Praxis allowance ends up being more inviting, as well as flavourful.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that of Legacies, it may be some Free Council ones that are most exclusive. The Blank Badge Attainments don't even emulate spells, and I think the Dreamspeaker entry is at the very least beyond any two-dot spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T03:46:51-07:00","id":1453748,"title":"","content":"After a while of ever-hotter summers, political horror, and disappointment I think I will try for 1 to 2 day posting rate. I have problems but this thread will be a relief to them.<br /> <br /> I think we derailed in topic and will be spending tomorrow getting us back on topic. For now I will leave you with a bit of imagery. <br /> <br /> There is a homebrew Legacy I think is called &quot;Illusionists&quot;. Mages passing their Attainments off as stage tricks. One Attainment is based off the Display of Power spell, so the mage can show off to the the Sleeping world a simulation of what they could actually do. What about showing off my Legacy on their stage? Ever wanted to be close to a performance at least as epic as Dumbledore vs Voldemort?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T14:36:06-07:00","id":1453790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1453748#post1453748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a homebrew Legacy I think is called &amp;quot;Illusionists&amp;quot;. Mages passing their Attainments off as stage tricks. One Attainment is based off the Display of Power spell, so the mage can show off to the the Sleeping world a simulation of what they could actually do. What about showing off my Legacy on their stage? Ever wanted to be close to a performance at least as epic as Dumbledore vs Voldemort?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are these Illusionists detailed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T14:52:45-07:00","id":1453792,"title":"","content":"I believe it was a homebrew legacy, I\u2019ll look for it.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/933264-2e-illusionists-of-truth-%E2%80%93-magicians-legacy#post933264\">is this it?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T00:56:07-07:00","id":1453824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1453792#post1453792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it was a homebrew legacy, I\u2019ll look for it.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/933264-2e-illusionists-of-truth-%E2%80%93-magicians-legacy#post933264&amp;quot;]is</a> this it?[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T01:32:23-07:00","id":1453827,"title":"","content":"First Attainment: I am thinking that in addition to investing the bonus from opening Doors to making new ones maybe I should include a Mana cost as well. Some part of me recoils from the idea because when I contemplated making the success requirement for making new Doors ten minus Prime dots I imagined a cosmic event. A great Archmaster of Prime finally achieving Assumption and total total access to Prime would then have zero needed successes in order to create Doors. Adding a Mana requirement might prevent such a cosmic master from enjoying infinite Doors during the Duel. Of course I realize that forsaking game balance for a far-off hypothetical might be a bad idea. <br /> <br /> Second Attainment: still going to make it about starting with additional Doors equal to Prime dots.<br /> <br /> Third Attainment: roll Prime and Intimidation to force the enemy to give up their own Doors to bind their own offers. Clash of Wills ensues with a bonus depending on how many Doors the enemy still has. Failure means the Duelist must give up her own Door to bind the offer. The wager aspect removes the need to balance the Attainment with a Mana cost.<br /> <br /> Fourth Attainment: instead of a bonus for the next spell or rebuilding Doors the mage instead trades successes for removing additional Doors. Five successes and a point of Mana for each additional Door. The reason the Mana reduction of Legacy Attainments does not work here is because each is a separate use of the same Attainment. Perhaps this rationale should be used for the first Attainment. Should have a visual component to show extra losses.<br /> <br /> Fifth Attainment: opening a Door allows the mage to gain extra Arcana immunities. Not sure if this should be the fourth Attainment or have a cost. A visual element as well to show everyone which Arcanum the Duelist chose to shut down.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow I will work on the Pledges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T04:22:48-07:00","id":1453912,"title":"","content":"Looks like I broke my promise. I really ought to start earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T05:05:19-07:00","id":1453918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1453912#post1453912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like I broke my promise. I really ought to start earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t get <i>too</i> caught up in schedules when homebrewing \u2014 it\u2019s going to get stressful!<br /> <br /> I mean, look at me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I\u2019m supposed to be doing the Chronologues\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T20:16:46-07:00","id":1454113,"title":"","content":"First pledge: no cheating. If you attempt to cheat you lose a Door. If you succeed you lose the Duel.<br /> <br /> Second pledge: be magnanimous. You lose the Triumphant condition if you abuse the Defeated, but through reparations you can relieve the Defeated of their condition and make your own more resilient or broader in benefits. <br /> <br /> Third pledge: allow for negotiation. You can only use this if your last spell was for defense. It takes effect between spells and briefly stops the casting to allow for negotiations. Therfore you cannot trick your foe into casting and getting punished. If you attack before you both agree to resume the Duel then while the ban lifts for you both the spell still fails and the opponent gets the respective immunity. The Attainment to force your foe to pay with their own Doors cannot be attempted during this Duel and you can even get permission from your foe to keep some of your immunities. <br /> <br /> Fourth pledge: you can forfeit without forfeiting everything. This assumes that the default result of backing out of a Duel in progress is loss. We know animals are dangerous when cornered and Sun Tzu even attests to the power of those without an escape. You can break the will by making cowardice an option, a deceptively hard one. Whatever the mechanics will be it is difficult to attempt without losing Doors in the process. On the low chance you escaped with some then you will be vulnerable to haggling depending on how few Doors are left. <br /> <br /> Fifth pledge: you can cement your victory. Cast a spell right after your victory that affirms the terms you won. The Sacred Dueling Space waits on you before closing down. The spell manifests as a Master level Legacy Attainment. It must strictly be used to enforce the terms agreed upon in and before the Duel. The storyteller may expand the scope as though the terms were a Legacy's Theory if she wishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T23:32:49-07:00","id":1455011,"title":"","content":"The first Attainment will require mana for each use after all. The visual component for the fourth Attainment will be that you can see multiple simultaneous versions of the victim suffering from your hypothetical spell. The visual for the fifth Attainment will be whatever Arcanum you used, no mana requirements, just be initiated into the Arcanum and conquer with it. You can even use multiple Arcana at once for a high risk and reward. Also, I am switching the positions of the last two Attainments. <br /> <br /> Names and requirements: the first Attainment will be called either &quot;surging will&quot; or &quot;conqueror's confidence&quot;. It requires initiation which requires Prime 2 and two dots in occult and intimidation. The second Attainment will be called &quot;expert's confidence&quot; or &quot;fresh will&quot;. I don't intend multiple names, I am just unsure. This requires occult three. The third Attainment will be called &quot;concession's surrender&quot; or &quot;force concession&quot;. This requires two dots in larceny or subterfuge and Prime three. The fourth will be called &quot;the superior/greater/uncontested master&quot; or &quot;better than you&quot;. This requires four dots in intimidation and Prime four. The fifth Attainment will be called &quot;simulated massacre&quot;. This requires four dots in occult and Prime 5.<br /> <br /> Yantras. I am not bothering with the mythic aspect so much. Plus one bonus for emulating a hero or god, plus two if you can live up to that power. Plus one for setting the sacred Dueling space, whether casting &quot;Display of Power&quot; yourself or indirectly helping to do the same. Plus one for causing or reinforcing submissions, plus two if that submission is of someone with comparable ability like a fellow supernatural or a millionaire. If you keep getting stronger than it will need to be adjusted. Vowing one-up-manship before casting will provide plus two because the spell fades away, giving a strong impression of merely being fraudulence, if you cannot deliver. That same bonus shrinks to one if there is no real risk of failing. Plus two if carrying out the terms of the Duel.<br /> <br /> Oblations. Strategizing and contemplating the Duel. Practicing or developing your abilities in preparation for later Duels. Reveling in victory or wallowing in defeat, from the Duel.<br /> <br /> Elaborating on the pledges: for the pledge of magnanimity if you already lost the Triamphant condition than Fate will reciprocate abuse. If you relieve the Defeated than you will regain the Triumphant condition. If you still have it then reroll social failures as you are given a chance to rescue your benefit.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow I will figure out what to do with the fourth pledge and see if I can expand on the founding story. Then maybe we can move on.<br /> <br /> Do forgive if I don't follow through on that schedule because tomorrow I am purchasing a ps5. Not from a scalper. Finally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T03:08:02-07:00","id":1455181,"title":"","content":"Maybe I need to elaborate on the story of Champion. Some inspiration came from my own life and some came from how I imagine others suffered.<br /> <br /> You ever experienced helplessness? Namely in the form of cults or legal bullshit? Champion was raised in a high control group. She saw her friend go back to an abusive father because the courts backed him. All in all, she knows intimately that life is unfair. <br /> <br /> Now comes the Awakening. The story of the Exarchs. Power, belonging, purpose. Joining the Free Council was a given. The intoxication of fighting against tyrants. Then that all went to shit when Trump was elected. Before that, Champion named herself so to answer the drudgery and disappointment and trauma from before the Awakening. Then the craziness of Trump revealed all the excuses made for the ignorant as bullshit. The members of the Free Council was wrong about democracy seeking the truth, and Champion was furious at them for lying to her. Champion remembered how her own sister took the side of her abusive father, and was furious at herself for not learning her lesson.<br /> <br /> So many of the problems of the masses was endemic to the masses, and cannot be culled like tyrants and conspirators. How can she be Champion if she is suspicious of the victims, or unable to forgive millions? She was left in a crisis that dangled over the edge of the Abyss, nearly committing to a number of Left-handed options. Eventually she found her anchor: the Duel Arcane. Having realized she can use it to force the squabbling idiots of the Pentacle into fixing the world she dedicated everything to it like a drunken escape. She joined the Adamantine Arrow to train all the time so she can kill the mages too hostile for the Duel and defeat everyone else in the Duel. Might in place of trust.<br /> <br /> But however good she was, there was always someone better and she needed to tip the odds in her favor somehow without violating the Lex Magica. Cheating was not sustainable in a society of expert secret keepers and Mystery solvers. She needed to be unbeatable and allowed to be so, and thought it efficient to do both at the same time.<br /> <br /> Looking back, she finds her name to be an ironic joke. Still, she is Champion one way or another.<br /> <br /> Some of you guys had opinions on the Theory of her Legacy, so now you know why it is like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T03:14:12-07:00","id":1455182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1453792#post1453792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it was a homebrew legacy, I\u2019ll look for it.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/933264-2e-illusionists-of-truth-%E2%80%93-magicians-legacy#post933264&amp;quot;]is</a> this it?[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how to address you and have it show up on your feed without replying to a specific post.<br /> <br /> Aside from names, skill requirements, and the pledge of retreat. I am done with this Legacy. I am really just testing to see if I took to long and was abandoned before the second Legacy. Cannot blame you guys if you did. Without a reply in two days I will just assume that I ran out of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T03:15:11-07:00","id":1455183,"title":"","content":"Thanks anyway TempleBuilder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T19:49:37-07:00","id":1455230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1455182#post1455182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know how to address you and have it show up on your feed without replying to a specific post.<br /> <br /> Aside from names, skill requirements, and the pledge of retreat. I am done with this Legacy. I am really just testing to see if I took to long and was abandoned before the second Legacy. Cannot blame you guys if you did. Without a reply in two days I will just assume that I ran out of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know about anyone else, but I have spent the last three weeks dealing with life being rougher than usual to me. Car wreaks and uninsured other drivers rough. Because of this I\u2019ve taken something of a hiatus from the forums, with as few posts as I really could get away with while still preparing for my first game of Mage. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve even read any of the new topics, haven\u2019t had the focus. But I have tomorrow off and I swear I will have something tangible for you. I would write it tonight but I am dead tired from work and wrangling student loans.<br /> One thing I can see right now is you need everything thing in one post, otherwise it makes it hard to see if anything is missing. Hope this helps a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 07-19-2021, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T20:06:35-07:00","id":1455286,"title":"","content":"Let it not be said that I, TempleBuilder, second bearer of that name, do not keep my promises. The timeliness of my promises might need some improvement though. I don't actually know when this will be posted, but I have no doubt it will be late. But I don't know, maybe I will surprise myself. So much for today being \u201coff\u201d, and now I\u2019m rushing to finish this. More to follow tomorrow.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1453827#post1453827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Attainment: I am thinking that in addition to investing the bonus from opening Doors to making new ones maybe I should include a Mana cost as well. Some part of me recoils from the idea because when I contemplated making the success requirement for making new Doors ten minus Prime dots I imagined a cosmic event. A great Archmaster of Prime finally achieving Assumption and total total access to Prime would then have zero needed successes in order to create Doors. Adding a Mana requirement might prevent such a cosmic master from enjoying infinite Doors during the Duel. Of course I realize that forsaking game balance for a far-off hypothetical might be a bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div> A interesting first attainment, definitely worth a mana though. though<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1453827#post1453827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Attainment: still going to make it about starting with additional Doors equal to Prime dots.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough. More health is never a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1453827#post1453827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third Attainment: roll Prime and Intimidation to force the enemy to give up their own Doors to bind their own offers. Clash of Wills ensues with a bonus depending on how many Doors the enemy still has. Failure means the Duelist must give up her own Door to bind the offer. The wager aspect removes the need to balance the Attainment with a Mana cost.</div> </div> </div> </div> Niche, but very effective. I actually like this one a lot, it really is a neat idea. Give the duelist a bonus, maybe clash with both Fate and Prime and Gnosis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1453827#post1453827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourth Attainment: instead of a bonus for the next spell or rebuilding Doors the mage instead trades successes for removing additional Doors. Five successes and a point of Mana for each additional Door. The reason the Mana reduction of Legacy Attainments does not work here is because each is a separate use of the same Attainment. Perhaps this rationale should be used for the first Attainment. Should have a visual component to show extra losses.</div> </div> </div> </div> Works for me, but I\u2019m not sure how many successes even a master will get. Perhaps maybe lower the amount of successes required. Spending separately each time is fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1453827#post1453827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fifth Attainment: opening a Door allows the mage to gain extra Arcana immunities. Not sure if this should be the fourth Attainment or have a cost. A visual element as well to show everyone which Arcanum the Duelist chose to shut down.</div> </div> </div> </div> Seems good to me, I think this could fit in earlier if you wanted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1454113#post1454113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First pledge: no cheating. If you attempt to cheat you lose a Door. If you succeed you lose the Duel.</div> </div> </div> </div> This one will need clarification on what is cheating, do the Duelists own attainments count? Does outside help count? Do intentions matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1454113#post1454113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second pledge: be magnanimous. You lose the Triumphant condition if you abuse the Defeated, but through reparations you can relieve the Defeated of their condition and make your own more resilient or broader in benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like! Needs clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1454113#post1454113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third pledge: allow for negotiation. You can only use this if your last spell was for defense. It takes effect between spells and briefly stops the casting to allow for negotiations. Therfore you cannot trick your foe into casting and getting punished. If you attack before you both agree to resume the Duel then while the ban lifts for you both the spell still fails and the opponent gets the respective immunity. The Attainment to force your foe to pay with their own Doors cannot be attempted during this Duel and you can even get permission from your foe to keep some of your immunities.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is the order of this: round ends, then start negotiations? Because that is a seriously awesome ability if so. Definitely a worthy attainment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1454113#post1454113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourth pledge: you can forfeit without forfeiting everything. This assumes that the default result of backing out of a Duel in progress is loss. We know animals are dangerous when cornered and Sun Tzu even attests to the power of those without an escape. You can break the will by making cowardice an option, a deceptively hard one. Whatever the mechanics will be it is difficult to attempt without losing Doors in the process. On the low chance you escaped with some then you will be vulnerable to haggling depending on how few Doors are left.</div> </div> </div> </div> Can\u2019t comment without mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1454113#post1454113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fifth pledge: you can cement your victory. Cast a spell right after your victory that affirms the terms you won. The Sacred Dueling Space waits on you before closing down. The spell manifests as a Master level Legacy Attainment. It must strictly be used to enforce the terms agreed upon in and before the Duel. The storyteller may expand the scope as though the terms were a Legacy's Theory if she wishes.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is\u2026 broad. And strong. But also really niche? I guess it works. Does the immunity to various Arcanum still apply to the spell, because that might be a very interesting and strategic wrinkle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1455011#post1455011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first Attainment will require mana for each use after all. The visual component for the fourth Attainment will be that you can see multiple simultaneous versions of the victim suffering from your hypothetical spell.</div> </div> </div> </div> Good call on the first attainment requiring mana.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1455011#post1455011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The visual for the fifth Attainment will be whatever Arcanum you used, no mana requirements, just be initiated into the Arcanum and conquer with it. You can even use multiple Arcana at once for a high risk and reward. Also, I am switching the positions of the last two Attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div> Cool, I still think<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1455011#post1455011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Names and requirements: the first Attainment will be called either &quot;surging will&quot; or &quot;conqueror's confidence&quot;. It requires initiation which requires Prime 2 and two dots in occult and intimidation. The second Attainment will be called &quot;expert's confidence&quot; or &quot;fresh will&quot;. I don't intend multiple names, I am just unsure. This requires occult three. The third Attainment will be called &quot;concession's surrender&quot; or &quot;force concession&quot;. This requires two dots in larceny or subterfuge and Prime three. The fourth will be called &quot;the superior/greater/uncontested master&quot; or &quot;better than you&quot;. This requires four dots in intimidation and Prime four. The fifth Attainment will be called &quot;simulated massacre&quot;. This requires four dots in occult and Prime 5.</div> </div> </div> </div> Alright<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1455011#post1455011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yantras. I am not bothering with the mythic aspect so much. Plus one bonus for emulating a hero or god, plus two if you can live up to that power. Plus one for setting the sacred Dueling space, whether casting &quot;Display of Power&quot; yourself or indirectly helping to do the same. Plus one for causing or reinforcing submissions, plus two if that submission is of someone with comparable ability like a fellow supernatural or a millionaire. If you keep getting stronger than it will need to be adjusted. Vowing one-up-manship before casting will provide plus two because the spell fades away, giving a strong impression of merely being fraudulence, if you cannot deliver. That same bonus shrinks to one if there is no real risk of failing. Plus two if carrying out the terms of the Duel.</div> </div> </div> </div> Remember that yantras are going to be the main way the legacy interacts with the world outside of the duel if you insist on the legacy only having attainments that directly affect the duel. I would be very ok with the Legacy having broad and strong Yantras in that circumstance, it fits the theme of power. On the other hand, if you decide to build some non-duel functionality into the legacy these are fine as is. I do like the competitive nature of the Yantras, sells the theme of the legacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1455011#post1455011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oblations. Strategizing and contemplating the Duel. Practicing or developing your abilities in preparation for later Duels. Reveling in victory or wallowing in defeat, from the Duel.</div> </div> </div> </div> Good oblations, perfect really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1455011#post1455011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elaborating on the pledges: for the pledge of magnanimity if you already lost the Triamphant condition than Fate will reciprocate abuse. If you relieve the Defeated than you will regain the Triumphant condition. If you still have it then reroll social failures as you are given a chance to rescue your benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div> So rote quality on social rolls?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1455011#post1455011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tomorrow I will figure out what to do with the fourth pledge and see if I can expand on the founding story. Then maybe we can move on.<br /> <br /> Do forgive if I don't follow through on that schedule because tomorrow I am purchasing a ps5. Not from a scalper. Finally.</div> </div> </div> </div> Did you get one? What games are you going to play with it? You don\u2019t have to answer this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1455181#post1455181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I need to elaborate on the story of Champion. Some inspiration came from my own life and some came from how I imagine others suffered.<br /> <br /> You ever experienced helplessness? Namely in the form of cults or legal bullshit? Champion was raised in a high control group. She saw her friend go back to an abusive father because the courts backed him. All in all, she knows intimately that life is unfair.<br /> <br /> Now comes the Awakening. The story of the Exarchs. Power, belonging, purpose. Joining the Free Council was a given. The intoxication of fighting against tyrants. Then that all went to shit when Trump was elected. Before that, Champion named herself so to answer the drudgery and disappointment and trauma from before the Awakening. Then the craziness of Trump revealed all the excuses made for the ignorant as bullshit. The members of the Free Council was wrong about democracy seeking the truth, and Champion was furious at them for lying to her. Champion remembered how her own sister took the side of her abusive father, and was furious at herself for not learning her lesson.<br /> <br /> So many of the problems of the masses was endemic to the masses, and cannot be culled like tyrants and conspirators. How can she be Champion if she is suspicious of the victims, or unable to forgive millions? She was left in a crisis that dangled over the edge of the Abyss, nearly committing to a number of Left-handed options. Eventually she found her anchor: the Duel Arcane. Having realized she can use it to force the squabbling idiots of the Pentacle into fixing the world she dedicated everything to it like a drunken escape. She joined the Adamantine Arrow to train all the time so she can kill the mages too hostile for the Duel and defeat everyone else in the Duel. Might in place of trust.<br /> <br /> But however good she was, there was always someone better and she needed to tip the odds in her favor somehow without violating the Lex Magica. Cheating was not sustainable in a society of expert secret keepers and Mystery solvers. She needed to be unbeatable and allowed to be so, and thought it efficient to do both at the same time.<br /> <br /> Looking back, she finds her name to be an ironic joke. Still, she is Champion one way or another.<br /> <br /> Some of you guys had opinions on the Theory of her Legacy, so now you know why it is like this.</div> </div> </div> </div> I am sorry to read that you have suffered so. We all walk our own roads, and many are not easy to tread, wreathed in thorns and barbed wire. I hope you find happiness, and peace, and true companionship, should you wish it, on your road.<br /> And in finality, a Gift. Feel Free to copy and paste.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>The Dualists</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">description</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Theme</span> </b><br /> <br /> Lore<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Acanthus, Adamantine Arrow,<br /> <b>Background</b>: Background of average member.<br /> <b>Appearances</b>: Appearance<br /> <b>Nickname:</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 2, Occult 2, Intimidation 2<br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Symbolically resonant.<br /> <b>Organization</b>: Description of the social presence of the legacy.<br /> <b>Theory</b>: Description of the type of magic the legacy practices.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b>:<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: (+1); (+2); (+2); (+1, +2 conditionally)<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: Strategizing and contemplating the Duel; Practicing or developing your abilities in preparation for later Duels; Reveling in victory or wallowing in defeat, from the Duel.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">First: &quot;surging will&quot; or &quot;conqueror's confidence&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Fate 1<br /> .<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Second: &quot;expert's confidence&quot; or &quot;fresh will&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 2, Occult 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Fate 2.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Third: &quot;concession's surrender&quot; or &quot;force concession&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 3, Larceny 2 or Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Fate 3<br /> .<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fourth: &quot;the superior/greater/uncontested master&quot; or &quot;better than you&quot;</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 4, Intimidation 4.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Fate 4<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fifth: &quot;simulated massacre&quot;</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 5, Occult 4<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Fate 5.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 07-20-2021, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T05:50:27-07:00","id":1455572,"title":"","content":"When you mentioned that you were having your own issues TempleBuilder I felt a kind of vindication and solidarity, afterall my imagination filled the gaps with what you guys think of me, as though I was the only one with issues that kept me from coming back to the forums. Mostly internal issues but there will always be there asshats who, even having it explained to them, will accuse me of being lazy. <br /> <br /> Remember that Champion's story is not a 1-1 copy of my own with fanciful elements added, but the cult and legal bullshit that divides friends, family, and even interesting acquaintances did happen. <br /> <br /> Whether today or tomorrow, time I will finish this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T03:07:09-07:00","id":1455602,"title":"","content":"You suggested that I include both Prime and Fate when making the opponent pay with his own doors. Three dice pools seem rather excessive to me, so I will add the requirement of mana if she really wants to add Fate to the mix.<br /> <br /> No, I will not lower the successes needed in order to shatter multiple Doors. The reason is that even I think this power is a bit much. Making the Legacy legal will not matter if everyone collectively agrees that it must be undermined to be opposed. In fact, I will add that it needs to be done during the casting that broke the Door. This may be superfluous because we are exchanging the bonus that comes from opening Doors, which will of course have the remainder used up in the next casting.<br /> <br /> HSomething weird is happening with may ktyping system . N","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T03:37:25-07:00","id":1455603,"title":"","content":"Defining cheating, okay. By default the rules are the same as the normal Duel and allows for the Legacy's Attainments. As in: no actual casting and no outside interference. They may be renegotiated every Duel assuming the opponent understands that he can and will be magically held to it. The pledge punishes intent as described but will prevent unintentional violations and outside interference (assuming it wasn't arranged by the cheater, that would be intent) that would trip up the Duel. In the more concerted sabotages of magic a clash of wills will happen between the Duelist and the interference using Gnosis and Fate. If both opponents are Duelists then they both clash of wills against the interference at the same time. Such problems tend to be actual battle or mystical phenomena outside the Duel. Whatever happens all Duelists involved who have Fate initiation at least will be aware of any interference that had to be fated away and what couldn't be fated away. That last one will end the Duel automatically, without any winner and the Dueling mages will suffer the consequences of lost Doors as per the fourth pledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T03:54:38-07:00","id":1455604,"title":"","content":"The second pledge. No, I don't mean rote quality. Though I can see the confusion. I mean there will be a second roll representing an attempt the save your social awkwardness. After failing that, one mana can be spent to keep the blessing longer for another chance to rescue the conversion. The blessing will not help you in this. You also need to rehabilitate any more social slip ups during this. No matter how much mana spent or concerted your efforts, if the conversation ends or is interrupted for any reason and you still haven't saved your blessing then it is just gone. Dice penalties, lowering impressions, and extra Doors are to be expected and added at storyteller fiat. Especially if you didn't succeed at your first second chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T04:21:25-07:00","id":1455605,"title":"","content":"Third pledge: not between rounds, but turns. Spells are automatically canceled if the heat of battle makes you keep going without realizing what is happening. This is reflexive. Maybe I should add a limit. By default both contestants get a number of uses equal to their own Fate dots, negotiation with proper understanding of the Attainment can change the number. If a contestant runs out of uses then they become vulnerable to the third Attainment once the Duel starts up again.<br /> <br /> Fourth pledge: this is going to be tricky. Maybe I should read up on game theory because this will fall flat if players are not torn between winning and retreating in such a way that they simply lose.<br /> <br /> The fifth pledge: how can immunities apply if the foe ran out of Doors? Maybe you just forgot. Remember the Attainment doesn't have to apply to anything more particular than just enforcing the terms. Questioning if I should allow combined spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T04:35:32-07:00","id":1455606,"title":"","content":"Yantras: to clarify on submission. It doesn't have to have anything to do with the Duel, that is already a different Yantra. It could be literal imprisonment or coercion. As for the &quot;make you look like a fraud&quot; Yantra, it works whether you failed the casting entirely or fell short of whatever metric you wanted to surpass. If you need to fall back on a brittle illusion for certain this Yantra will assure it. The impression of fraudulence can be stopped by magic that shields the mind without a clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T04:37:01-07:00","id":1455607,"title":"","content":"I am tired. Continue tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T07:45:28-07:00","id":1455796,"title":"","content":"Later than promised but it is time to tune up the names. After contemplating I figured I liked the names to have a little poetry to them. &quot;Conqueror's and experts confidence&quot; it is. I also realize that names that are like commands or statements are not my style. &quot;Concession's surrender&quot; it is. The fourth Attainment is difficult though. I want something that summarizes the effect, the &quot;proven master&quot; and &quot;the superior master&quot; don't seem to do it completely and I want to be succinct. If I can't find an apt title by the end of this then I will default to &quot;the superior master&quot;. Maybe &quot;the superior wielder&quot;? I am satisfied with the last one.<br /> <br /> I am question if my clarification of two Yantras was even necessary or if I just burdened it down with unnecessary complications. <br /> <br /> Back to naming. Pledges. The first one will be &quot;pledge of lawfulness&quot;, then &quot;pledge of magnanimity&quot;, then &quot;pledge of parley&quot;, then &quot;pledge of retreat&quot;, then &quot;pledge of victory&quot;.<br /> <br /> Finally some nicknames. &quot;Cheaters&quot; will of course will be derogatory and by the resentful who still dispute the legality of the Legacy. &quot;Tyrants&quot;, &quot;champions&quot; and others depends on politics and whether they personally effected the speaker. The only nickname so common as to be tantamount to a formal name is &quot;foregone winners/victors&quot; or just the &quot;foregone&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T13:41:16-07:00","id":1456616,"title":"","content":"Overcame my issues again. <br /> <br /> Okay, the pledge of retreat. I still am uncertain about how to go about this, so I decided to apply the &quot;blunt force&quot; solution to writer's block. Have something at all put down so I have something to work with, no matter how unsatisfied I am at first.<br /> <br /> So... the mage voluntarily sacrifices their Door so that their lost immunities fill a total that, once reached, will let them quit the Duel. There should be a visual component to this that obviously shows self denigration or surrender. Maybe casting at self? Once accomplished the Lasting effects is a weakened will. For Social Maneuvering, use the remaining Doors. There perhaps could be an uncertain way to keep one's current Door but still lose the immunities. Exceptional Success? <br /> <br /> What I also wanted to comment on is how TempleBuilder made that super official looking template for the Legacy. Maybe it is because I use a phone but my attempts at learning how to use editing on this forum have been metaphorically fruitless. I can only guess at how he got the system to say it was from me, or how to copy it since copies don't seem to allow quotes of quotes. When I take two long to post something the system says &quot;missing human identification&quot; or something similar, making me have to copy everything and sign in again. This leaves me amazed at the super long posts that looked edited and refined. Just amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T13:42:11-07:00","id":1456617,"title":"","content":"Next I should work on the flowery language for the Attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T21:18:45-07:00","id":1456735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1456616#post1456616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overcame my issues again.<br /> <br /> Okay, the pledge of retreat. I still am uncertain about how to go about this, so I decided to apply the &quot;blunt force&quot; solution to writer's block. Have something at all put down so I have something to work with, no matter how unsatisfied I am at first.</div> </div> </div> </div> Seems good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1456616#post1456616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... the mage voluntarily sacrifices their Door so that their lost immunities fill a total that, once reached, will let them quit the Duel. There should be a visual component to this that obviously shows self denigration or surrender. Maybe casting at self? Once accomplished the Lasting effects is a weakened will. For Social Maneuvering, use the remaining Doors. There perhaps could be an uncertain way to keep one's current Door but still lose the immunities. Exceptional Success?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds good, maybe a white flag as a symbol? The exceptional success is one way certainly, but maybe a roll for a graceful surrender with a penalty equal to the opponents Wits could work. Depends on how easy you want it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1456616#post1456616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I also wanted to comment on is how TempleBuilder made that super official looking template for the Legacy. Maybe it is because I use a phone but my attempts at learning how to use editing on this forum have been metaphorically fruitless. I can only guess at how he got the system to say it was from me, or how to copy it since copies don't seem to allow quotes of quotes. When I take two long to post something the system says &quot;missing human identification&quot; or something similar, making me have to copy everything and sign in again. This leaves me amazed at the super long posts that looked edited and refined. Just amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, Thank you. I must give credit where it is due, I was given a example Legacy that used that template by KaiserAfini. Their kindness has allowed me to pay it forward. As for the quote thing, I used one of your previous quotes, removed the post identification number and text of the post, and replaced it with my own template. Since it has problems quoting form a quote, I think copying and pasting might work? I mostly learned through experimentation, as I have little prior knowledge of forums. Granted, that experimenting with the forum broke at least one topic I made. I will see if I can post it without quotes, if that\u2019s easier for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 08-13-2021, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T21:20:30-07:00","id":1456736,"title":"","content":"hope this works edit: oh good it did.<br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>The Dualists</b></span></i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:20px\">description</span></i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Theme</span></span> </b><br /> <br /> <i>Lore</i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Origins</b></span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b><i>: Acanthus, Adamantine Arrow,</i><br /> <b>Background</b><i>: Background of average member.</i><br /> <b>Appearances</b><i>: Appearance</i><br /> <b>Nickname:</b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b><i>: Prime 2, Occult 2, Intimidation 2</i><br /> <b>Initiation</b><i>: Symbolically resonant.</i><br /> <b>Organization</b><i>: Description of the social presence of the legacy.</i><br /> <b>Theory</b><i>: Description of the type of magic the legacy practices.</i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span></i><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b><i>:</i><br /> <b>Yantras</b><i>: (+1); (+2); (+2); (+1, +2 conditionally)</i><br /> <b>Oblations</b><i>: Strategizing and contemplating the Duel; Practicing or developing your abilities in preparation for later Duels; Reveling in victory or wallowing in defeat, from the Duel.</i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span></i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:20px\">First: &quot;surging will&quot; or &quot;conqueror's confidence&quot;.</span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b><i>: Initiation.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b><i>: Fate 1</i><br /> <i>.</i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Second: &quot;expert's confidence&quot; or &quot;fresh will&quot;</span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b><i>: Prime 2, Occult 3</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b><i>: Fate 2.</i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Third: &quot;concession's surrender&quot; or &quot;force concession&quot;.</span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b><i>: Prime 3, Larceny 2 or Subterfuge 2</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b><i>: Fate 3</i><br /> <i>.</i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fourth: &quot;the superior/greater/uncontested master&quot; or &quot;better than you&quot;</span></i><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b><i>: Prime 4, Intimidation 4.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b><i>: Fate 4</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fifth: &quot;simulated massacre&quot;</span></i><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b><i>: Prime 5, Occult 4</i><br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b><i>: Fate 5.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T21:28:42-07:00","id":1456737,"title":"","content":"For some reason, the forum differs wildly from a phone to a iPad. Now I\u2019m not a expert or even really a layperson, but wouldn\u2019t a mobile version of a website apply to both a phone and a IPad? The IPad version seems exactly the same as the pc version, but not the phone. It\u2019s weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T06:59:32-07:00","id":1457473,"title":"","content":"You asked about what games I had on my ps5. There was difficulties, but:<br /> <br /> Resident evil 7 and 8<br /> Pathless<br /> Arkham knight <br /> Demon's souls <br /> And Ghost of Tsushima. <br /> <br /> There are others TempleBuilder, but that last one is the reason this auspicious week. I felt more confident about coming back here than usual and then exhausted myself playing rather than replying. At least for once it was a silly reason.<br /> <br /> First Attainment: Conqueror's Confidence <br /> <br /> Every Duelist was literally-soul forged in victory, leaving them aware of arcane conflict in ways even the Mastigos and Obrimos struggle to understand. To see the dance of competing Supernal signs and symbols, and to know and appreciate what it means when one of them is their own will forms the basis of their first lesson. The burst of power from further breaking their opponents in and the refreshment from winning the Duel are the same in the Mysteries of the Legacy. When the cosmos first held their hand up in victory the Duelist learned how to consolidate that into Doors during the Duel.<br /> <br /> Every time the Duelist opens a Door they may invest some or all of the bonus made from doing so into forging additional Doors. This decision must be made before the next spell and cannot be reversed. Every five bonus dice invested can be made into a Door with each use of this Attainment, which is reflexive and costs one mana.<br /> <br /> Optional Fate one: pledge of Lawfullness.<br /> <br /> As Champion founded the Legacy she realized she was paranoid and didn't trust in the referee. So she conscripted a Fae to do the job instead. Just as she did she realized that she established the foundation allowing for different Pledges, representing different enigmatic guardians of Mists and Thorns, to bring strange possibilities to the Duel.<br /> <br /> The Duelist can modify the Sacred Dueling space before engaging the the actual Duel by using an instant action and one mana to invoke a Pledge. Multiple Pledges may be used. Agreement with an opponent on using a Pledge will circumvent the mana cost and allow some parts of the Pledges to be renegotiated, but only if the opponent actually understands the terms, even if he thinks he does. Naturally, knowledge of the Pledges are spreading rapidly to stop any trickery, but maybe some Nameless didn't get the memo. The Pledge of Lawfulness will take away a Door from the an attempting cheater and lose the Duel for a (very short term) successful cheater. Fate will clear away mundane interferences to the rules and magical ones get two clashes of wills of Gnosis and Fate, one for each contestant. The rules are to keep the violence in the magical simulation and to not arrange any external aid or distraction. Further rules can be negotiated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T07:00:50-07:00","id":1457474,"title":"","content":"Now that the ball is rolling, metaphorically, I actually should get back to this tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T07:01:40-07:00","id":1457475,"title":"","content":"My brain is so tired I am not sure if I did a good job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T21:36:56-07:00","id":1457544,"title":"","content":"Second Attainment: Expert's Confidence<br /> <br /> After learning how to get a premature taste of victory a Duelist takes a look at how will gives rise to magic, then reverses the relationship. Thereafter every Duel benefits from insulation of the will. At the start of every Duel the Duelist gains Doors equal to her Prime dots.<br /> <br /> Optional Fate two: Pledge of Magnanimity <br /> <br /> As Champion considered her first Pledge that seemed to account for everything, she realized that it really only accounted for the letter of the law rather than the spirit. The world was full enough of cruelty already, so why add bad sportsmanship to it? After the semantic monster of the first Pledge she called forth a subtle adjudicator of relationships to represent the next.<br /> <br /> If the Triumphant abuses the Defeated then the Triumphant condition will be lost without a beat. If already lost Fate will reciprocate abuse, though alternative or unequal punishments can be negotiated. With meaningful reparations the Triumphant can relieve the Defeated of his condition which still grants a beat. The reward for doing so is a Persistent Triumphant condition that allows one chance for every social fail for a social save that preserves the condition. Alternative rewards can be negotiated for, any mundane or arcane condition gained from Exceptional Success is fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T06:34:09-07:00","id":1458330,"title":"","content":"I am a little sleep deprived but I have resolved that I won't wait another night. Maybe with the mental momentum I can finally finish this quickly.<br /> <br /> Third Attainment: Concession's Surrender<br /> <br /> Between studying the gaps in focus for a mage trying to negotiate and how the Prime Arcanum regulates vows as opposed to the Fate Arcanum, Champion figured out how to conflate the symbols of concession and surrender. Terrible Thorns of light and blood spew forth to render the High Speech runes of promises visible and bound, digging into the innards of speakers. This even reveals previous promises and payments. The drawback is that once unleashed the power doesn't discriminate, so a Duelist better not concede. <br /> <br /> Pay one mana and roll Gnosis and Prime as a reflexive action once per turn to make the opponent seal their selected offer to the Duelist by sacrificing their own Doors, but should the roll fail the Duelist must seal the selected offer with her own Doors. The opponent may contest the roll with Gnosis and Prime as well, additional rolls with different dice pools may occur according to the mechanics of whatever shielding spell or Attainment the opponent is using.<br /> <br /> Once unleashed neither mage may make further offers without paying the price for it for a number of rounds equal to the Duelist's Prime dots as the magic spreads throughout like fire, but just like how even fire can be mastered the winner of the clash of wills is immune if they scored an Exceptional Success. This immunity lasts until the winner's Door opens. Despite how brutal and restrictive it looks the Thorns don't inconvenience movement and disappear when the Attainment expires.<br /> <br /> Optional Fate three: Pledge of Parley<br /> <br /> Champion soon realized that without some regulation no one was ever going to negotiate with her mid-Duel ever again, so she called in another kind of peacekeeping Fae. This one resolved standoffs from small disputes to deadly war, though in this case it won't be speaking, just facilitating speaking. On the other hand, Champion didn't make this Attainment to delay &quot;Concession's Surrender&quot; forever. <br /> <br /> For one time or as many as negotiated a mage may call for a time out. The remaining uses for this privilege is tracked independently between the opponents. Once used the Fae dispels all spells extant and upcoming for the cease-fire. It lasts until both agree to comence again or someone is just stalling for time, the one who didn't call for a cease-fire is allowed only one minute to find a reason or make a plan that is more than stalling. This may even immediately waste a use of the privilege, additional or alternative end conditions can be negotiated.<br /> <br /> During the Cease-fire offers can be made and accepted in relative safety. &quot;Concession's Surrender&quot; cannot be used here, any lingering traces are removed and any offer made during this time is immune until the mage making them runs out of uses of the pledge. Once vulnerable &quot;Concession's Surrender&quot; no longer costs mana and gains the rote quality when used on those offers from cease-fire. Given that there may be dozens of rejected offers and the Duelist will probably get an Exceptional Success, this may lead to disaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T06:36:06-07:00","id":1458331,"title":"","content":"I have noticed I unintentionally make things complicated and I usually go back to simplify things. Do you guys think I overdid it with this one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T06:44:37-07:00","id":1458335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1458331#post1458331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have noticed I unintentionally make things complicated and I usually go back to simplify things. Do you guys think I overdid it with this one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Will have to do a thorough post-by-post read on them to assess that. Unfortunately, I\u2019m trying to overdo my own stuffs at the moment\u2026\u2026 other folks around here could help with that one, perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T22:32:47-07:00","id":1458946,"title":"","content":"Fourth Attainment: Superior Wielder<br /> <br /> It is ironic how the realm of pure truth can be rather reductive. The differing abilities and specialties of the mages involved in the Duel is summarized as &quot;this one is more right than the other&quot;. To Champion, this is confirmation that the universe is ruled by strength rather than morality, so someone must speak truth to power. Contemplating this, she wondered if she could divide that binary assessment by the Arcana and enjoy the benefits early like the first Attainment. Her remaining question is if this made it more or less reductive.<br /> <br /> The only requirements of this Attainment is opening a Door in the Duel using an attack spell. The Duelist automatically gains an immunity to the respective Arcanum she attacked with. This can work with multiple Arcana in the same successful attack spell, permitting high-risk and reward Dueling. There is no further effect if the Duelist already has the respective immunity, the Supernal agrees that the Duelist made her point.<br /> <br /> Optional Fate four: Pledge of Retreat<br /> <br /> Upon her ascent to greatness, Champion realized that many would rather resort to sabotage than agree to a doomed Duel against her and that sometimes she had little heart to finish those that panic in the Duel against her. Sometimes an arrogant asshole realizes that he is out of his depth and wishes he compromised instead. <br /> <br /> To solve this Champion enlisted the help of a Fae that oversees surrender negotiations, foreclosures and regretful promises. Those that wish to escape can attack themselves with their own magic. The Pledge requires that the mage in someway makes it obvious that he is doing it to herself. No immunities prevent this. Progress is made for every sacrificed immunity, including the one for the third Attainment. The default target number is ten minus the Fate dots of the retreating mage. If the attack roll is a Failure than it will be clear that the mage tried something, though the mage will still lose the immunities and make no progress. A Dramatic Failure will still lose the Door. An Exceptional Success will keep the Door even as the immunities are shed. <br /> <br /> Meeting the target number avails nothing if mage actually lost the last Door. Upon retreating any further Social Menuavering or Duel Arcane will on the relevant issue will use the remaining Doors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T21:56:19-07:00","id":1459720,"title":"","content":"Fifth Attainment: Simulated Massacre<br /> <br /> Looking back on all the tricks and powers she amassed, Champion realized that what she was still missing was a finishing move to finish her Legacy. Considering that Doors only opened one at a time, there was no such thing in the traditional Duel. So obviously this was what she had to overcome. <br /> <br /> Just like &quot;Conqueror's Confidence&quot;, she can allocate some or all of her bonus dice from opening Doors to this Attainment and cannot get them back. She requires five bonus dice and one mana per use, since it is reflexive she can use it multiple times at once. The new requirement which is not in common with the first Attainment is that it has to happen during the opening of the opponent's Door.<br /> <br /> Every use sees multiple versions of the opponent suffering from the attack spell, and thereby opening multiple Doors at once. It is a ratio of one extra Door per use and the possibility of the grisly scene of watching multiple versions of the other mage burning and screaming alive. What an impression, and not for kids.<br /> <br /> Optional Fate five: the Pledge of Victory<br /> <br /> Observing that the Supernal, the realm of magic, sides with the victor Champion questioned why there was not more substantial rewards. If the victory tweaked reality to be more in the victor's favor then why was it not more directly beneficial? Maybe the terms needed to allow for greater say from the victor. <br /> <br /> Calling upon the Fae that most directly embodies Champion's cynicism, she got that privilege enshrined for the Legacy that always wins. Whenever a mage wins under this Pledge she can cast one more spell that manifests as a Master Legacy Attainment. The terms of the Duel behave as the &quot;Theory&quot; that constrains or expands the parameters of this final Attainment with the Storyteller as the arbiter. The &quot;ritual&quot; for ritual casting is the ceremonial celebration of victory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T22:09:00-07:00","id":1459721,"title":"","content":"I don't really like &quot;appearance&quot; sections. My instinct is to skimp over them yet I am loath to do so because I know that occasionally something important is put in. <br /> <br /> Appearance: Champion didn't care for superficiallities. If it functioned as clothes she put it on. Whether it would be skimpy tatters or a mascot suit was irrelevant to her. To say it was sometimes jarring was an understatement because she would always have a stern and strong demeanor. Think Batman as a part-time clown In the courthouse.<br /> <br /> Instead her students set the traditions for dress: crude homemade badges commemorating victories and spoils stitched into t-shirts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T06:58:46-07:00","id":1459750,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Excess, the edit button exists for a reason.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T03:14:41-07:00","id":1463077,"title":"","content":"I am back, will respond soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T02:50:39-07:00","id":1463210,"title":"","content":"Two plans or previews of what will eventually happen for the the other Legacies:<br /> <br /> For the Death Priests I am thinking that the Death Arcanum will be focused on dealing with ghosts and Sin-eaters while the Prime Arcanum is focused on the Krewe and ceremonies. As these are interconnected, the categories are not rigid. I think that the best course there is to reread Geist: the Sin-eater and the Arcana sections, then figure out how the mage helps out on a daily basis. After that then we will have a good idea on how to craft the Attainments.<br /> <br /> For the Unashamed I am taking direction from the a certain Coil from &quot;Secrets of the Covenants&quot;. There was a coil that enabled vampires to learn mortal magics, at prohibitive costs and weaknesses to start with and then removing those disadvantages as more coils were learned and even having assets to add to those powers. So let's create an elaborate price for escaping Hubris, then use the spells from the Mind Arcanum section to lower that. You are on the right track if you look at those spells and think &quot;what arbitrary problem can those solve&quot;?<br /> <br /> But those are for later. Right now I am focused on taking my backstory for Champion and make it stop sounding like a pitch. If you guys have suggestions or would like to beat me to it by offering a rough draft, go ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:14:47-07:00","id":1464359,"title":"","content":"&quot;What are you doing pupil? Sparing is done for today. Oh, more questions about our rather short history. In other words, more questions about Champion. Considering that she trained me herself I can confirm a rumor or two.<br /> <br /> Yes, she had been part of the Council of Free Assemblies. Surreal, right? Never in all my years have I come across a greater cynic that still fought for some kind of morality or ideal, let alone with such passion. To think it wasn't too many years ago either. She did admit to me that part of the reason had to do with her dying idealism and was not subtle in comparing that to religious faith, typical Champion.<br /> <br /> In her Sleeping life she was raised both in a cult and under a malignant narcissist. Remember that this was before the world got introduced to Trump the candidate, so very few people understood what an actual narcissist was back then. She tried to tell me before then too, and I am ashamed to say I let her down. I suppose incredulity is one of the greatest barriers to understanding there is, it makes you ignore the people who need the most help.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, Champion learned some pretty savage lessons in life from that. In being betrayed by her community, family, and friends she learned how in developing coping mechanisms victims become enablers for abusers, turning supportive family members over to predators. Specifically, she learned that just because someone is your sibling doesn't mean they won't expose you to the same thug you shielded them from.<br /> <br /> Yes, she is afraid of victims. I can the realization in your eyes light up, this is why every time she planned on saving some poor soul she also accounted for apprehending the downtrodden if need be. Every time we saved the innocent she did stare at them warily as though they planned to knife her in the back, it wasn't in your head. In her darker moments she would talk about abuse like it was a zombie contagion, almost insinuating that we need to burn the innocent in order to survive. Yes, she can rein it in, but we all could feel her nervous paranoia. It's kinda creepy.<br /> <br /> So when democracy went crazy, so did she. It was like her childhood bullshit became the whole damn world. It was my full-time job just to hold her together and not let her go off the rails and into the arms of either the Seers or the Abyss. Yes, that nearly happened more than once. That was two years of me helping her reconcile her need for heroism and her desolate lack of trust for most people, and accidentally inspiring the theory for our Legacy. You know what happened next.&quot;<br /> <br /> -Vanguard, an Adamant Sage.<br /> <br /> That is 2/3 to 9/10 of the fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T04:32:10-07:00","id":1466439,"title":"","content":"Back soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T20:24:23-07:00","id":1466872,"title":"","content":"The sudden and terrible emergence of the new Legacy known as &quot;the Duelists&quot; remains an issue of controversy and speculation, much of it centered on their founder Champion. What is known is that during the first two years of the Trump administration she not only distanced herself from her colleagues in the Free Council but was the subject of inquiry into possible connections with the Seers, Scelesti, liches, reapers, and various other Nephandi. The charges never went through, though, as her few remaining friends were always able to vouch for what was described as &quot;that pathetic-looking alcoholic.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just as the the last two years of the Trump administration began she reamerged from reclusion, announced her new allegiance to the Adamantine Arrow. She then challenged and defeated the majority of mages in the consilium to the Duel Arcane over initiating a campaign to remove every group she was accused of courting over the last two years from the Consilium's city. The Hierarch's protests on the logistical impossibility of the campaign could not stop a majority obligated to do what Champion wanted, and were disproved when the campaign was resolved the same night that she returned. Her great success rendered it impossible to convict her over how she knew where every enemy was hiding. <br /> <br /> Over the next two years she became utterly infamous for conquering entire Consilia using the Duel in days at the longest, committing them to actions that were delayed due to political or cultural controversy. Her attempts at negotiations were simply &quot;comply or we Duel&quot;. Before long it became known that she was aiming to reshape her soul in the Duel, and she decided the best way to do it was to pre-emptively make sure that legality and acceptability of her Duelist Legacy was established through the Duel itself. Every mage that could decide whether it was legal to alter the custom of the Duel through a specialized Legacy was her foe in the Duel. By the time Trump left office, every authority was conquered, and her Legacy was born.<br /> <br /> The following was an interview into the secrets of Champion made by one of her Legacy-members: <br /> <br /> [Okay then, this serves as a prologue to what I previously wrote.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T04:22:18-08:00","id":1469085,"title":"","content":"After more mental hurdles I am back. Will respond soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T03:34:09-08:00","id":1469241,"title":"","content":"Okay final plan:<br /> I still don't know how to quote a quote, but I can quote myself. I still have some misgivings over my own work. I think I ought to have simplified the Yantras and the Attainment that forces the foe to pay with their own doors. This following month is polish month. Every two to five days I will tweak something and ask follow-up questions. Regardless of the final quality I ask whoever made that beautiful framework for the Legacy (forgot name of contributer) to put the polished pieces together because I still don't know how to quote quotes. <br /> <br /> However it ends, the month after will be the start of a new Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T07:24:52-08:00","id":1469577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1455011#post1455011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yantras: Plus one bonus for emulating a hero or god, plus two if you can live up to that power. Plus one for setting the sacred Dueling space, whether casting &amp;quot;Display of Power&amp;quot; yourself or indirectly helping to do the same. Plus one for causing or reinforcing submissions, plus two if that submission is of someone with comparable ability like a fellow supernatural or a millionaire. If you keep getting stronger than it will need to be adjusted. Vowing one-up-manship before casting will provide plus one die, two in the case of a real challenge. Plus two if carrying out the terms of the Duel.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Was thinking that Concession's Surrender should, instead of making a period where everyone is affected, inconvenience just the Duelist that used this rude tactic. That does require rewriting some stuff that referenced the current version. <br /> <br /> Add suggestions before I resolve it myself. Or not. Either way, I am simplifying this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T03:01:58-08:00","id":1470414,"title":"","content":"Back tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T18:01:02-08:00","id":1470490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1458330#post1458330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Third Attainment: Concession's Surrender<br /> <br /> Between studying the gaps in focus for a mage trying to negotiate and how the Prime Arcanum regulates vows as opposed to the Fate Arcanum, Champion figured out how to conflate the symbols of concession and surrender. Terrible Thorns of light and blood spew forth to render the High Speech runes of promises visible and bound, digging into the innards of speakers. This marks all paid promises, before or after, in Thorn curling into burning High Speech. The drawback is that once unleashed the power doesn't discriminate, so a Duelist better not concede. <br /> <br /> Pay one mana and roll Gnosis and Prime as a reflexive action once per turn to make the opponent seal their selected offer to the Duelist by sacrificing their own Doors, but should the roll fail the Duelist must seal the selected offer with her own Doors. The opponent may contest the roll with Gnosis and Prime as well, additional rolls with different dice pools may occur according to the mechanics of whatever shielding spell or Attainment the opponent is using.<br /> <br /> Once unleashed the Duelist will have the Thorns still embedded in her chest, wrapped around her heart. For the rest of the Duel she will have succumbed to the same effect she tried to use on her foe, binding all her own offers even if she didn't have enough Doors. Despite how brutal and restrictive it looks the Thorns don't inconvenience movement and disappear when the Attainment expires.<br /> <br /> Optional Fate three: Pledge of Parley<br /> <br /> Champion soon realized that without some regulation no one was ever going to negotiate with her mid-Duel ever again, so she called in another kind of peacekeeping Fae. This one resolved standoffs from small disputes to deadly war, though in this case it won't be speaking, just facilitating speaking. On the other hand, Champion didn't make this Attainment to delay her forever. <br /> <br /> For one time or as many as negotiated a mage may call for a time out. The remaining uses for this privilege is tracked independently between the opponents. Once used the Fae dispels all spells extant and upcoming for the cease-fire. It lasts until both agree to comence again or someone is just stalling for time, the one who didn't call for a cease-fire is alloted a full minute to find a reason or make a plan that is more than stalling. This may even immediately waste a use of the privilege due to the desire to only escape the danger, additional or alternative end conditions can be negotiated. All negotiable terms for all Attainments can be renegotiated.<br /> <br /> During the Cease-fire offers can be made and accepted in relative safety. &amp;quot;Concession's Surrender&amp;quot; cannot be used here, it is disabled for both in the duration and any offer made during this time is immune until the mage making them runs out of uses of the pledge. Once vulnerable &amp;quot;Concession's Surrender&amp;quot; no longer costs mana and succeeds automatically when used on the foe's offers from cease-fire. Given that there may be dozens of rejected offers, this may lead to disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will be back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T19:54:19-08:00","id":1470496,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>You're being banned for the week, Excess, because it is the SAME thread where I said not to spam posts like these and you seem to have learned nothing.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T03:37:54-08:00","id":1472054,"title":"","content":"As I promised, I didn't finish the Legacy by the deadline so I am abandoning it. I have already read both the mage and sin-eater 2nd edition books, so a week of quick review is in order. By review I mean I will binge-read in my own time in preparation for Death Priests. If you have anything to add just know I will not see it until a week later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T21:08:47-08:00","id":1473724,"title":"","content":"Okay, I am back.<br /> <br /> Perhaps reading two giant books whole while distracted by mental issues is a tall order for &quot;one week&quot;.<br /> <br /> Each of the game lines reference other game lines, yet are not consistent with each other. I think the primary reason is that they were not all reimagined for the second edition at the same time. This means there are inconsistencies for which I must pick and choose what is canon. <br /> <br /> For the most part I will rule that Geist: the sin-eaters 2nd edition takes precedence. <br /> <br /> In any case:<br /> I am sticking to my plan that the Death Arcanum will primarily deal with sin-eating, the bound, and the expected field work of Krewes. While the Prime Arcanum will primarily deal with the Krewe itself, such as other celebrants, the Regalia, and Ceremonies. This is a soft separation of function because these purviews are interrelated. <br /> <br /> One of the most basic Death spells allows the mage to produce plasm from any orifice. There are no mechanics for its value in &quot;plasm points&quot;, nor any other mechanic explaining how this doesn't result in an endless convenient supply for Sin-eaters. Maybe that isn't a problem. I have noticed that Geist is filled with sources of plasm. Sure, most sources require some payment or effort, but by draining Bound and stuffing them into a ghost's vicinity during the Pass On Ceremony you will find that the after-life is a goldmine.<br /> <br /> Since the basis of Haunts for the Bound are conditions or tilts then perhaps we can have a Legacy Attainment that interacts with that basis, a power that synergizes (get it?) well with any Haunt. Maybe helping establish enhancements, shielding the condition, or ending it. <br /> <br /> Perhaps a power that &quot;pays death off&quot;? The Doomed Condition, the price of resurrection for the Bound, Avernian Gates, the Ferry toll. <br /> <br /> Maybe turn the Death Priest into a living Anchor? <br /> <br /> On the subject of Prime.<br /> <br /> Most of these will be handling the Krewe. So then maybe we should have some abilities enhance Ceremonies above and beyond normal. One should provide automatic successes for each dot of prime and extend Legacy Wisdom to any use of Ceremonies. Another should adapt the Platonics Forms to substitute absent materials. <br /> <br /> Ceremonies are but one part of a Krewe and I should not dedicate too many Attainments on that one subject. Maybe two at most? <br /> <br /> As for the Regalia, maybe a chance to use the final effect more than once?<br /> <br /> I have more thoughts, but maybe we should save them for tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T21:50:44-08:00","id":1473728,"title":"","content":"Hey, you\u2019re alive! Good to see you again.<br /> Prime and Death are both great choices by themselves for running a death cult, and frankly all sort of interesting when combined on their own.<br /> I would personally advise against clearly dividing Death and Prime for function, be flexible with attainments.<br /> <br /> As for creating plasm, just say it makes potency units of plasm. Also that spell isn\u2019t Lasting, so that plasm disappears once duration is done. Oh and you have to spend Mana on it if it\u2019s a legacy attainment.<br /> <br /> Haunts and more specifically Keys can be linked to resonance if you want to use Prime for them. According to the Players Guide to Contagion, Fate is used for Dooms, and Space of their use as keys to the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Turning the Death Priest into a anchor can probably be a Death/Prime ruling spell to make your personal resonance/nimbus into a anchor. There are probably other ways to do it. Some might be better.<br /> <br /> As for substituting platonic forms\u2026don\u2019t. It\u2019s a waste of mana. Instead combine materials conceptually with Yantras (because they are basically the same thing), and have have attainments to substitute in or find whatever a given ceremony need. Every spell that\u2019s says it affects Yantras, you can say affects Ceremonies. Heck, use Scribe Grimoire to write down Ceremonies so whoever uses the Grimoire can use the ceremonies, and benefit from the other benefits of Grimoires!\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T05:40:21-08:00","id":1473965,"title":"","content":"Thanks for replying, little details like that can get me out of my own head and connect to a world outside my family and house. I was afraid no one would respond to the procrastinator. Now back to business...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T06:45:52-08:00","id":1473969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1473728#post1473728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, you\u2019re alive! Good to see you again.<br /> Prime and Death are both great choices by themselves for running a death cult, and frankly all sort of interesting when combined on their own.<br /> I would personally advise against clearly dividing Death and Prime for function, be flexible with attainments.<br /> <br /> As for creating plasm, just say it makes potency units of plasm. Also that spell isn\u2019t Lasting, so that plasm disappears once duration is done. Oh and you have to spend Mana on it if it\u2019s a legacy attainment.<br /> <br /> Haunts and more specifically Keys can be linked to resonance if you want to use Prime for them. According to the Players Guide to Contagion, Fate is used for Dooms, and Space of their use as keys to the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Turning the Death Priest into a anchor can probably be a Death/Prime ruling spell to make your personal resonance/nimbus into a anchor. There are probably other ways to do it. Some might be better.<br /> <br /> As for substituting platonic forms\u2026don\u2019t. It\u2019s a waste of mana. Instead combine materials conceptually with Yantras (because they are basically the same thing), and have have attainments to substitute in or find whatever a given ceremony need. Every spell that\u2019s says it affects Yantras, you can say affects Ceremonies. Heck, use Scribe Grimoire to write down Ceremonies so whoever uses the Grimoire can use the ceremonies, and benefit from the other benefits of Grimoires!\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware that other Arcana have their uses, but because this is a Legacy I was going to get stuck with one primary one and one secondary one. So unless you are trying to convince me to switch I am not sure what mentioning them was supposed to do. Maybe to remind me that mages are not limited to their Legacies and these would be useful tools? To inspire new spells? I actually have a lot of respect for content makers who go so far as to invent new spells to go along with their Legacies, including the optional Arcana and Reach effects.<br /> <br /> As for what I was thinking:<br /> <br /> We already know from the &quot;Word of Command&quot; that Prime can not only negate the usual requirements for other magics but pay Mana instead of the usual toll. We also know that Legacies can shift the scope of spells in favor of doing the Legacy's job. We also know that Mana costs beyond one for Legacy Attainments is reduced to one. So I was thinking that there ought to be an Attainment that cheapens the cost of nailing your severed hand to a wall for passage through an Irkalla Gate to one Mana. In my opinion a Legacy isn't complete until you have powers that will endear you to allies.<br /> <br /> Another thing. The reason I suggested using the &quot;Platonic Form&quot; spell was to create an Attainment that replaced symbols, not merely enhance the Ceremony. Think about it. Mages don't need their wands or Grimoires or chrystal balls to cast spells. Yantras help, but a saboteur will regret learning that snapping a wand will only inconvenience, not stop, the mage. It would be oddly disempowering if the Master of Ceremonies could not make due. Afterall, Legacy Attainments cost at most one Mana and their scope is adjustable along thematic lines. In other words, if the Priest finds that he does not have all the materials at hand he will pay just one Mana and the conjured Forms will last for the Performance and any lingering effects, like the curse container from &quot;Crow Girl Kiss&quot;. Just one use to replace everything in a single Ceremony.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking of using &quot;Supernal Vision&quot;, but honed in on everything that has to do with the Underworld and Krewes. It would be silly if allied Sin-eaters can see Mementos and Ylems immediately, but not the mage himself. Perhaps it should especially be honed in on the bloated souls of the Eaters of the Dead and Deathmasks...<br /> <br /> &quot;Ectoplasmic Shaping&quot; was the spell I was thinking of in order to affect Haunts. Fine-tuned to alter the Haunt conditions like they were the originating Bound. Then I thought: &quot;that seems rather strong for dot one&quot;. Now I am not sure which dot to assign it to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T08:00:36-08:00","id":1473974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1473969#post1473969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am aware that other Arcana have their uses, but because this is a Legacy I was going to get stuck with one primary one and one secondary one. So unless you are trying to convince me to switch I am not sure what mentioning them was supposed to do.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think I meant that certain concepts are shocking easy to transfer over to either Primary or Secondary. I don\u2019t know if you\u2019ve kept up with the forums, but I was entertaining the idea of a Prime/Matter legacy of liars and poisoners. I had the mentally separated into Lies for Prime, and Poison for Matter. Come to find out, you can use Prime to achieve poison like effects, no need for Matter. Now I\u2019d still need Mater for immunity to poison, but I had more options for arranging the Legacy than I thought. Be flexible, and try think way out the box, you may be surprised what actually works and is thematic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1473969#post1473969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe to remind me that mages are not limited to their Legacies and these would be useful tools? To inspire new spells? I actually have a lot of respect for content makers who go so far as to invent new spells to go along with their Legacies, including the optional Arcana and Reach effects.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think there is room for plenty new spells for this legacy. We can make them together if you\u2019d like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1473969#post1473969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what I was thinking:<br /> <br /> We already know from the &quot;Word of Command&quot; that Prime can not only negate the usual requirements for other magics but pay Mana instead of the usual toll. We also know that Legacies can shift the scope of spells in favor of doing the Legacy's job. We also know that Mana costs beyond one for Legacy Attainments is reduced to one. So I was thinking that there ought to be an Attainment that cheapens the cost of nailing your severed hand to a wall for passage through an Irkalla Gate to one Mana. In my opinion a Legacy isn't complete until you have powers that will endear you to allies.</div> </div> </div> </div> Seems fine on a technical standpoint. Just needs the Death component\u2026which it should automatically have if you are using it as a attainment. Oh, and if you want, I made a Prime spell expressly meant to buff allies with conditions that relate to the nimbus your mage has. It\u2019s big and showy, though, because it uses the Nimbus Flare. It might not fit the legacy, but I can post it here if you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1473969#post1473969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing. The reason I suggested using the &quot;Platonic Form&quot; spell was to create an Attainment that replaced symbols, not merely enhance the Ceremony. Think about it. Mages don't need their wands or Grimoires or chrystal balls to cast spells. Yantras help, but a saboteur will regret learning that snapping a wand will only inconvenience, not stop, the mage. It would be oddly disempowering if the Master of Ceremonies could not make due. Afterall, Legacy Attainments cost at most one Mana and their scope is adjustable along thematic lines. In other words, if the Priest finds that he does not have all the materials at hand he will pay just one Mana and the conjured Forms will last for the Performance and any lingering effects, like the curse container from &quot;Crow Girl Kiss&quot;. Just one use to replace everything in a single Ceremony.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mages are extraordinarily flexible in what they can use as tools though. Why not instead grant the Ceremony that same flexibility in Yantra/Material choice? Secondly, unless you want a ritual for your ritual, Platonic form is a 4th or 5th level attainment. You would need it to last a scene and be instant, meaning 2 reach. Meanwhile, my suggested spell is at most Ruling, or most likely, Compelling. Gives you more reach to work with. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1473969#post1473969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was also thinking of using &quot;Supernal Vision&quot;, but honed in on everything that has to do with the Underworld and Krewes. It would be silly if allied Sin-eaters can see Mementos and Ylems immediately, but not the mage himself. Perhaps it should especially be honed in on the bloated souls of the Eaters of the Dead and Deathmasks...</div> </div> </div> </div> Should be fine. If you just want to see Death stuff, it\u2019s just Death Vision. If you wanted to use the Prime one for something else. You could also do Prime Unveiling to see through all layers of twilight. That\u2019s\u2026probably less useful, but it is a thing you can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1473969#post1473969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Ectoplasmic Shaping&quot; was the spell I was thinking of in order to affect Haunts. Fine-tuned to alter the Haunt conditions like they were the originating Bound. Then I thought: &quot;that seems rather strong for dot one&quot;. Now I am not sure which dot to assign it to.</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably still should be Ectoplasmic Shaping then, but with lots of Reach and a clash of wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T02:40:20-07:00","id":1477425,"title":"","content":"It is not fun for me that I usually only manage to comment once or twice a month. My new strategy: if I make an outline earlier and accept that it doesn't have to be big changes each time then maybe I will be commenting twice weekly. Including the secondary Arcanum it is ten Legacy Attainments. Let's see if I can organize them tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T04:50:54-07:00","id":1477579,"title":"","content":"Okay then. Ten Attainments. On the Prime side we have the omni-key/payment Attainment I discussed earlier and two for Ceremonies. One is vastly improved ability with them and the other is compensating for lack of ingredients. These three inhabit the lower three dots of Prime. I have no proposals for the fourth to fifth Attainments. Probably should have come up with some by now.<br /> <br /> Now for Death. I am no longer bothering to base the one that tampers with Haunts on any particular Praxis and will place it in the fourth dot. Planning to adapt the &quot;create Anchor&quot; spell into a kind of &quot;liminal aura&quot;. Not the exact same though. This means that there is a rough plan for the the last two dots but not the first three, exactly the opposite of Prime. Really need to start thinking on some of the basics of what a Death Priest would do routinely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T14:36:15-07:00","id":1477645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1477579#post1477579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay then. Ten Attainments. On the Prime side we have the omni-key/payment Attainment I discussed earlier and two for Ceremonies. One is vastly improved ability with them and the other is compensating for lack of ingredients. These three inhabit the lower three dots of Prime. I have no proposals for the fourth to fifth Attainments. Probably should have come up with some by now.<br /> <br /> Now for Death. I am no longer bothering to base the one that tampers with Haunts on any particular Praxis and will place it in the fourth dot. Planning to adapt the &quot;create Anchor&quot; spell into a kind of &quot;liminal aura&quot;. Not the exact same though. This means that there is a rough plan for the the last two dots but not the first three, exactly the opposite of Prime. Really need to start thinking on some of the basics of what a Death Priest would do routinely.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m back. Hmm. So you have all the basic interaction with Ceremonies and Haunts and Ghosts. Why not do stuff for the Krew as a whole? You know, cult stuff, like enhancing your persuasiveness (Prime), or buffing large groups with the Nimbus (also Prime). I\u2019m not quite sure on what exactly, but you probably want something to interact with the normal people to the various mediums and the like, not everyone will be a Ghost or Sin Eater. How about spreading the ability to interact with the Dead? It\u2019s basic, but it\u2019s pretty helpful. Or maybe that\u2019s best left to a ceremony? Oh, here is a basic one, how about a Knowing of Death to find Momentos and other Death touched items? Good for the masters of ceremony to find ceremonial gear easy. Maybe a middle Death one is the use of Ghost Shield? It\u2019s probably pretty effective for Sin Eaters. Maybe a Social Death spell could be in order? Lots of options.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T21:04:03-07:00","id":1477827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1477645#post1477645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I\u2019m back. Hmm. So you have all the basic interaction with Ceremonies and Haunts and Ghosts. Why not do stuff for the Krew as a whole? You know, cult stuff, like enhancing your persuasiveness (Prime), or buffing large groups with the Nimbus (also Prime). I\u2019m not quite sure on what exactly, but you probably want something to interact with the normal people to the various mediums and the like, not everyone will be a Ghost or Sin Eater. How about spreading the ability to interact with the Dead? It\u2019s basic, but it\u2019s pretty helpful. Or maybe that\u2019s best left to a ceremony? Oh, here is a basic one, how about a Knowing of Death to find Momentos and other Death touched items? Good for the masters of ceremony to find ceremonial gear easy. Maybe a middle Death one is the use of Ghost Shield? It\u2019s probably pretty effective for Sin Eaters. Maybe a Social Death spell could be in order? Lots of options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironic. I came to a similar conclusion for spreading the ability to interact with the dead.<br /> <br /> It happened when I tried to put myself into the metaphorical shoes of a Death Priest. What common need or function do my Attainments have to address? Then it came to the question of what I hoped to achieve by making any given Praxis an Attainment. Attainments cannot be Counterspelled or dispelled. They are immune to Hubris, paradox, and do not trigger Dissonance. I realized the last one was the answer. These are Death Priests, if they could not guide others then nothing would distinguish them from charlatans. <br /> <br /> A Death Unveiling spell. Second dot. Reach assigned to instant casting and scene long Duration. Can effect any number of targets that are touching the Death Priest or agree to be guided by said Priest (even ironically). The Duration cannot end until the tour ends. <br /> <br /> Maybe next I should do for Geister and the Deathmasks. They are the crux behind so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T22:24:42-07:00","id":1477832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1477827#post1477827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironic. I came to a similar conclusion for spreading the ability to interact with the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ironic? That just means great minds think alike. Well, maybe your mind is great. I think mine has some bits missing or misplaced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1477827#post1477827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It happened when I tried to put myself into the metaphorical shoes of a Death Priest. What common need or function do my Attainments have to address? Then it came to the question of what I hoped to achieve by making any given Praxis an Attainment. Attainments cannot be Counterspelled or dispelled. They are immune to Hubris, paradox, and do not trigger Dissonance. I realized the last one was the answer. These are Death Priests, if they could not guide others then nothing would distinguish them from charlatans.</div> </div> </div> </div> Reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1477827#post1477827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Death Unveiling spell. Second dot. Reach assigned to instant casting and scene long Duration. Can effect any number of targets that are touching the Death Priest or agree to be guided by said Priest (even ironically). The Duration cannot end until the tour ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Places us at the third attainment. Feels a bit high thematically. But I don\u2019t think there is any way to fix that. If we want it lower, I think we need limitations. Maybe it exclusively works on people who sincerely agree to it. That would play into people doubting mediums don\u2019t get to see ghosts thing. It could be a bit too much like Ascension though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1477827#post1477827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe next I should do for Geister and the Deathmasks. They are the crux behind so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m afraid I can\u2019t help much with that. I haven\u2019t read Geist enough to provide anymore than basic observations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T02:02:41-07:00","id":1478043,"title":"","content":"I think you miscalculated TempleBuilder. Free Reach is available for every dot that meets and exceeds the requirement. Unveiling magic is dot one. Therefore to get the two free Reach we need the Attainment must be Apprentice level. If you think I miscalculated then show me where. <br /> <br /> In any case. My understanding of Legacies is that they are based on but not limited to their parent Paths. Their symbols familiar yet evolved. This is why they usually adopt one of the twin Ruling Arcana as their secondary Arcanum. That is part of the reason I chose Obrimos specifically. The other part is that I like it when mages turn their Inferior Arcanum Ruling.<br /> <br /> Obrimos see the world in terms of hierarchies, rulers crowned in power. With the first dot editing Death Mage Sight to reveal the Chthonic hierarchies in great detail. Geister, Reapers, Kerberoi, Celebrants of rank or wielding Regalia. Any concealment can be contested. I have not worked out the details, but know that any Krewe with a Death Priest in their congregation doesn't fear secret Reapers anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T08:44:02-07:00","id":1478057,"title":"","content":"No, I believe you are correct. Not sure how I messed that up. Maybe I thought was working from Veiling. Sorry. <br /> <br /> Yes, Obrimos is perfect as the main path for the legacy.<br /> <br /> Attaching more information to Mage Sight is interesting. 2 dots with Death allows one to see Ghosts with Mage Sight, this just seems like a enhancement of that. Honestly, it\u2019s probably just a special mixed Prime/Death sight with an Obrimos lens. It reveals that there is a minor Mystery that can be solved to reveal the ghosts rank and other pertinent info. Maybe it could play into the second Attainment, as it shows what the secret chthonic hierarchy to people, allowing them to see the underworld as the Obrimos does. Maybe not mechanically mage sight, but something similar flavor wise, but it should be interesting.<br /> <br /> Looks like we have everything besides the middle dot for Death. We are missing the last two for Prime, yeah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T08:52:41-07:00","id":1478369,"title":"","content":"Yes, I should probably reread the books for inspiration. Maybe a solution for the Descend Numen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T03:01:31-07:00","id":1482234,"title":"","content":"Okay, one part of this rough draft of the Legacy is the portrayal of the hierarchy of the Underworld. Which means I need to have an idea on how it all works. A reoccurring idea for me is that the Eaters of the Dead and the Absent are somehow a part of this system, not to imply that taking Memories is as evil as cannibalism. My current rationale is that the Underworld doubles as an ecosystem. Even without direct allegiance to the Chthonic gods surviving the conditions often means reinforcing those conditions for others, such as the treatment of Memory and ephemera as things to take and consume. By this logic, though, the merchant kings of the river cities have to be included. Any questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T10:27:29-07:00","id":1482264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1482234#post1482234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, one part of this rough draft of the Legacy is the portrayal of the hierarchy of the Underworld. Which means I need to have an idea on how it all works. A reoccurring idea for me is that the Eaters of the Dead and the Absent are somehow a part of this system, not to imply that taking Memories is as evil as cannibalism. My current rationale is that the Underworld doubles as an ecosystem. Even without direct allegiance to the Chthonic gods surviving the conditions often means reinforcing those conditions for others, such as the treatment of Memory and ephemera as things to take and consume. By this logic, though, the merchant kings of the river cities have to be included. Any questions?</div> </div> </div> </div>How would an underworld like Diyu implement such a hierarchical system ? What would it look like ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T05:56:01-07:00","id":1483120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1482264#post1482264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would an underworld like Diyu implement such a hierarchical system ? What would it look like ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Broken AC. Sleepless nights, late packages. I am back and resolved to what I wanted to do in the first place: engage over the course of days rather than months. <br /> <br /> There seems to be a slight misunderstanding. The Obrimos see all forms of power and authority embodied in their mage sight. That includes criminal power too. That means that the hierarchy they routinely see doesn't neatly match any official record or idea of what a hierarchy even is. It essentially has to. So what I am proposing for an Attainment isn't all that different from what they normally see. The difference is that they no longer need Knowing and Unveiling spells and Focused Mage Sight in order to get the Chthonic Dominions to reveal the greater details. This only works if I can develop those details and the mechanics that presents them. After all, I am not going to have the Attainment reveal authority-by-blackmail, am I? <br /> <br /> Also, what is Diyu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T07:34:47-07:00","id":1483310,"title":"","content":"Diyu is the underworld of Chinese mythology. It is characterized by being composed of different courts, which each preside over different hells that punish ghosts via resurrective torment. The number of hells and courts vary based on whether you are looking into the Taoist or Buddhist version, but they are consistent in being a highly organized system for governing the punishment and reincarnation of the dead (originally attributed to the Jade Emperor structuring it as another part of the Celestial Bureaucracy). <br /> <br /> An example is that, before reincarnation, souls needed to drink the Mengpo soup at the Bridge of Helplessness, offered by Grandma Meng. This would wipe their memories before reincarnation, which souds a lot like the effects of the Ocean Oroboros. The system itself sounds like a reinforcement of the cycle of torturous reincarnation the Psychopomp is fond of.<br /> <br /> So considering that many different realms of the dead exist in the Underworld, its plausible Diyu might as well. It contains a structured system for work (organizing and processing the dead within the system), a &quot;legal system&quot; for punishing crimes, provides for ghost a way of surviving (the hells could be Dominions and receiving a day's worth of punishment could grant Essence) and offers a road to reincarnation (which should be verified for misdirection). Because of this, I believe it stands as a possible Mystery and philosophical quandary to be examined by such a Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-07-2022, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T04:22:06-07:00","id":1483568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1483310#post1483310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diyu is the underworld of Chinese mythology. It is characterized by being composed of different courts, which each preside over different hells that punish ghosts via resurrective torment. The number of hells and courts vary based on whether you are looking into the Taoist or Buddhist version, but they are consistent in being a highly organized system for governing the punishment and reincarnation of the dead (originally attributed to the Jade Emperor structuring it as another part of the Celestial Bureaucracy). <br /> <br /> An example is that, before reincarnation, souls needed to drink the Mengpo soup at the Bridge of Helplessness, offered by Grandma Meng. This would wipe their memories before reincarnation, which souds a lot like the effects of the Ocean Oroboros. The system itself sounds like a reinforcement of the cycle of torturous reincarnation the Psychopomp is fond of.<br /> <br /> So considering that many different realms of the dead exist in the Underworld, its plausible Diyu might as well. It contains a structured system for work (organizing and processing the dead within the system), a &amp;quot;legal system&amp;quot; for punishing crimes, provides for ghost a way of surviving (the hells could be Dominions and receiving a day's worth of punishment could grant Essence) and offers a road to reincarnation (which should be verified for misdirection). Because of this, I believe it stands as a possible Mystery and philosophical quandary to be examined by such a Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to correct you on the Psychopomp part, except it turns out He also does that. The more you know.<br /> <br /> Your thoughts on possible Dead Dominions reminded me of my thoughts on Iconography merits. It seems that perception can alter the very medium of death, whether that means ideas about the Underworld becoming Dominions within it or ideas about ghosts becoming more Iconography merits. The constant seems to be that a canvas will remain a canvas. <br /> <br /> The basic facts about what a ghost really is seem to be unaltered by Iconography. Likewise, no Dead Dominion answers the actual question about what happens to ghosts or souls that &quot;pass on&quot;. Exploring these incongruities can possibly explain what the Underworld really is under all the theater and how flexible it really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T04:39:21-07:00","id":1483570,"title":"","content":"One other thing of note: the Geister seem to exist as sacrifices. The loss of identity, the apparent Rank cap on 5, the spawning of Deathmasks, Tyranny replacing Synergy, the source of new innate Keys, the potential for Cabeiros. My headcanon is that the Underworld runs on the symbolic logic that power comes from brutalized death gods, that in some broken timeline the previous chthonic pantheon was sacrificed for the rise of another, and now the Underworld is repeating the story by making new sacrifices.<br /> <br /> Since the Legacy is also my headcanon I am going to be combining the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T00:36:35-07:00","id":1488139,"title":"","content":"A strategy that worked before for me was compilation. Perhaps if I do it all the time I can work in weeks rather than months. Will be back in a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T03:07:15-07:00","id":1488347,"title":"","content":"Okay, I am embarrassed that I already sort of compiled this and failed to keep up. At least I will polish this now.<br /> <br /> Death<br /> <br /> 1. See agents and influence of Chthonic gods and krewes. <br /> 2. Grant ghost sight<br /> 3.<br /> 4. Counter Haunt<br /> 5. Self anchor<br /> <br /> Prime<br /> <br /> 1. Omni key<br /> 2. Enhance ceremony <br /> 3. Supply ceremony<br /> 4. Effect Regalia<br /> 5.<br /> <br /> I should start by saying it would not be useful if a mage just became another Anchor. Those are cheap enough upon mastery, and Sin-eaters have a more robust Liminal Aura than that. Since Death Priests ought to put their lives on the line for ghosts it occurred to me how I should approach this. If a ghost is using them as the universal Anchor they are then by spending mana the Priest becomes a personal anchor to that ghost as well. As long as Priest and ghost are both in the same world the ghost counts as being within the presence of their mage Anchor for the purposes of gaining essence and preventing essence bleed. The only upper limit to this is how long the mage can keep his one life from the angry Reapers for allowing so many ghosts free movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T18:04:19-07:00","id":1489517,"title":"","content":"To confess, an earlier version of the final Death Attainment involved making a promise to the ghost, where the particulars didn't matter. The ghost didn't have to know that the conditions were not &quot;mystically sealed&quot;, leaving a potential for deception. It was left out because such mischief was not becoming of the Death Priests.<br /> <br /> Getting ready to start negotiating mechanics in the next 1 to 2 days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T18:18:31-07:00","id":1489519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1483570#post1483570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One other thing of note: the Geister seem to exist as sacrifices. The loss of identity, the apparent Rank cap on 5, the spawning of Deathmasks, Tyranny replacing Synergy, the source of new innate Keys, the potential for Cabeiros. My headcanon is that the Underworld runs on the symbolic logic that power comes from brutalized death gods, that in some broken timeline the previous chthonic pantheon was sacrificed for the rise of another, and now the Underworld is repeating the story by making new sacrifices.<br /> <br /> Since the Legacy is also my headcanon I am going to be combining the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I REALLY like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T00:22:46-07:00","id":1489849,"title":"","content":"It is going to take a long time to develop the first power if try developing the fancy Symbolism first, so I must develop the details anyway. If in a krewe then status and benefits and active Regalia are revealed. If reaper than registers as such even when mask is in pocket. If lawbreaker of Boneyard or dominion then revealed as such, including punishment. If bound or ferryman or tolltaker of Irkalla gate, or guardian geist to Avernian gate or just a geist, then revealed as such. If Absent or Eater or necromancer, then revealed as such. If kerberos or in a domininion then revealed along with the old laws, If leveraged by any of the aforementioned then revealed as such. Clash of wills to provoke peripheral mage sight anyway if mystically hidden, reduces opacity in relevant mysteries by Death dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T00:25:15-07:00","id":1489850,"title":"","content":"Need to work on the third death dot. Calm rampaging geister and unmasking reapers? Seems too strong. Absorbing plasm as mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T00:13:42-07:00","id":1491873,"title":"","content":"You know what? Figuring out the missing dots is taking too long. I need to focus on the dots I have established. <br /> <br /> For &quot;counter haunt&quot; (name pending) I need to figure out exactly how to this power makes contact. I have some options, I could just simply have the mage see the power and have a clash-of-wills, or perhaps I could mimic banes. Maybe have the mage's touch have this bane quality that works without dicepools and could unmask reapers. The problem with balancing this power is that I don't have an intuitive idea of what is too much when it comes to banes. I am going to be generous and say that the haunt conditions are considered resolved.<br /> <br /> As for that omn-key thing. I think I will have it work on both debtor and creditor. That is to say: when resolving the Doomed condition it can work either on from touching the doomed or touching the memento. The same logic applies to healing the costs of the Irkalla gates and removing the lawbreaker condition. Theoretically you could undo the receipt of all the gates with this, but since it is one mana per payment that might take a while. Perhaps I should have it release those trapped in the walls.<br /> <br /> More to come this week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T20:07:28-07:00","id":1492332,"title":"","content":"The Prime Attainment for enhancing ceremonies should probably transfer some benefits of Attainments and spellcasting to how ceremonies work. So I will add automatic successes equal to Prime dots to the ceremony roll. This should mean that Prime masters should always get exceptional successes, and if the exact number of successes does not matter beyond that then the player probably could skip rolling. As for what I will borrow from spellcasting, ritual intervals will do. If the ceremony would take longer than a ritual interval then use ritual intervals instead. Instead of the usual rules for getting extra dice for taking longer for ceremonies, use the rules for mages doing the same. Theoretically if the mage is both a master of Prime and has a ritual interval of one minute then they could handle the ceremonial burden of an entire crew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T20:29:32-07:00","id":1492334,"title":"","content":"Legacy Attainments have a fixed ritual cast time of one scene (Mage core book page 198), which is unaffected by Gnosis. <br /> <br /> Ceremonies take, at minimum, 15 minutes per dot (Geist core book page 125), meaning 5 dot Ceremonies will always go above this limit. With the highest bonus modifier, they would take one week per dot.<br /> <br /> So a one minute cast time is not possible without a dedicated Attainment to reduce the time, which would require Time 5 and Death 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-04-2022, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T05:51:51-07:00","id":1492359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1492332#post1492332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Prime Attainment for enhancing ceremonies should probably transfer some benefits of Attainments and spellcasting to how ceremonies work. So I will add automatic successes equal to Prime dots to the ceremony roll. This should mean that Prime masters should always get exceptional successes, and if the exact number of successes does not matter beyond that then the player probably could skip rolling. As for what I will borrow from spellcasting, ritual intervals will do. If the ceremony would take longer than a ritual interval then use ritual intervals instead. Instead of the usual rules for getting extra dice for taking longer for ceremonies, use the rules for mages doing the same. Theoretically if the mage is both a master of Prime and has a ritual interval of one minute then they could handle the ceremonial burden of an entire crew.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ceremonies are resolved as a singular rolls, the fixed results of exceptional success on those rolls is that the krewe gets a Krewe Beat, and there are only two published Ceremonies in Geist 2e for which the number of successes matter outside of contested rolls, one of which only affects the radius of its effectiveness.<br /> <br /> A two-dot Attainment would be more sensibly balanced on applying As Above, So Below to a Ceremony roll; being able to give 9-Again (or 8-Again, if the Attainment takes a scene to apply) to any Ceremony allows the krewe to develop faster without trivializing the bonuses the system uses. (Alternately, let the mage substitute their Prime dots for an Attribute in the Ceremony roll if you want to go an unusual route with it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T20:48:18-07:00","id":1494014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1492334#post1492334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legacy Attainments have a fixed ritual cast time of one scene (Mage core book page 198), which is unaffected by Gnosis. <br /> <br /> Ceremonies take, at minimum, 15 minutes per dot (Geist core book page 125), meaning 5 dot Ceremonies will always go above this limit. With the highest bonus modifier, they would take one week per dot.<br /> <br /> So a one minute cast time is not possible without a dedicated Attainment to reduce the time, which would require Time 5 and Death 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you guys for responding, as I was worrying that no one cared about me anymore. As for your criticism, yes it can be shorter. The thing about Legacy Attainments is that their restrictions are softs limits rather than hard limits. The important thing is the symbolism of the Legacy's theory. If it means matching that the limits for Legacy Attainments can and will be adjusted. Sometimes the Praxis will no longer be so broad in effect and other times the power will now do things outside Practice or Arcana. This goes farther in &quot;atypical&quot; Attainments, which ignores the typical rules entirely and only requires you to &quot;eyeball&quot; its balance.<br /> <br /> I always assumed that Legacy Attainments could do things similar to what Arcana Attainments could, such as modifying how spellcasting works. So why not this?<br /> <br /> If you want citation I will give it, but I assume you will find it yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T21:22:24-07:00","id":1494017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1492359#post1492359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ceremonies are resolved as a singular rolls, the fixed results of exceptional success on those rolls is that the krewe gets a Krewe Beat, and there are only two published Ceremonies in Geist 2e for which the number of successes matter outside of contested rolls, one of which only affects the radius of its effectiveness.<br /> <br /> A two-dot Attainment would be more sensibly balanced on applying As Above, So Below to a Ceremony roll; being able to give 9-Again (or 8-Again, if the Attainment takes a scene to apply) to any Ceremony allows the krewe to develop faster without trivializing the bonuses the system uses. (Alternately, let the mage substitute their Prime dots for an Attribute in the Ceremony roll if you want to go an unusual route with it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Also thank you for responding! <br /> <br /> I will remind you that where successes matter Legacy Attainments will produce automatic successes equal to Arcanum dots (or is it the lowest Arcanum dots?). Also, it needs to trivialize something. Think about it. Mages already can do much to contribute to the cause and can only have one Legacy which they must join for life. Why join if it cannot that much more than others?<br /> <br /> Let's put it this way: powers are basically specialization. Within their purview they trivialize something that others will struggle with. The Gangrel from Requiem 2nd edition don't worry about havens from the sun as they can submerge into the ground. Uratha with the Cunning facet of Death from Forsaken 2nd edition can perfectly play dead, heart stopping and all. Both these characters can potentially survive easily where all their comrades die messily. If they couldn't then the players would have always chosen other powers, meaning they might as well not exist.<br /> <br /> That goes double for groups of specialization, offering proprietary power. If they didn't excel beyond everyone else within their purviews than why would anyone join it? This is actually a part of broader topic of &quot;game imbalance&quot; that others can cover better than I can. It's rather interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T21:28:40-07:00","id":1494019,"title":"","content":"I was going to start making oblations, Yantras, origin stories and other stuff. The problem is that this month is going to be especially busy for me and much of my free time is going to other games and Fandom stuff. So most of my time here in the forums will either be at the end of the month or now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T21:50:20-07:00","id":1494021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1494017#post1494017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will remind you that where successes matter Legacy Attainments will produce automatic successes equal to Arcanum dots (or is it the lowest Arcanum dots?). Also, it needs to trivialize something. Think about it. Mages already can do much to contribute to the cause and can only have one Legacy which they must join for life. Why join if it cannot that much more than others?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Legacy Attainment is built to be not significantly more powerful than a spell. It counts as having that many successes in cases where a measurement of its successes would be required because it is unrolled in addition to the normal spell consideration of &quot;you roll one success and all the attached spell factors kick in.&quot; Mages use Attainments because they're <i>reliable</i>, not because they're more effective than spells of the same level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's put it this way: powers are basically specialization. Within their purview they trivialize something that others will struggle with. The Gangrel from Requiem 2nd edition don't worry about havens from the sun as they can submerge into the ground. Uratha with the Cunning facet of Death from Forsaken 2nd edition can perfectly play dead, heart stopping and all. Both these characters can potentially survive easily where all their comrades die messily. If they couldn't then the players would have always chosen other powers, meaning they might as well not exist. </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between providing players with a tool they would not otherwise have and <i>removing the need for characters to engage with a system at all.</i> An Attainment to shortcut a Ceremony doesn't however many successes to the Ceremony roll, it counts as having that many successes <i>to shortcut that Ceremony</i>. Being able to automatically exceptionally succeed at <i>any type of ritual magic</i> is beyond the scope of a Legacy Attainment. If you want that kind of bump, you develop an Attainment with an effect replicating a specific Ceremony.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That goes double for groups of specialization, offering proprietary power. If they didn't excel beyond everyone else within their purviews than why would anyone join it? </div> </div> </div>Because proprietary power is not the main point of Legacies. The main point of a Legacy is that you belong to or have developed a magical school of thought that gives you additional magical insights and lets you tweak the work in less disastrous ways than dragging raw magic into the world across the Abyss. Attainments are there, magically, for ease of use and reduction of complications compared to the rest of the Awakened toolbox, not to remove any need to deal with modifiers for a rolled process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T04:54:43-07:00","id":1494034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1494014#post1494014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you guys for responding, as I was worrying that no one cared about me anymore. As for your criticism, yes it can be shorter. The thing about Legacy Attainments is that their restrictions are softs limits rather than hard limits. The important thing is the symbolism of the Legacy's theory. If it means matching that the limits for Legacy Attainments can and will be adjusted. Sometimes the Praxis will no longer be so broad in effect and other times the power will now do things outside Practice or Arcana. This goes farther in &quot;atypical&quot; Attainments, which ignores the typical rules entirely and only requires you to &quot;eyeball&quot; its balance.<br /> <br /> I always assumed that Legacy Attainments could do things similar to what Arcana Attainments could, such as modifying how spellcasting works. So why not this?<br /> <br /> If you want citation I will give it, but I assume you will find it yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure what you mean by Praxis. A Praxis is just a spell whose Imago you practiced so much that you can make it higher quality more reliably, like the recipe a chef has made a thousand times. Its only used to learn Attainments in some cases, but is otherwise not related to how Legacies work.<br /> <br /> Regarding unusual Attainments:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage The Awakening 2ed, page 198</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atypical: Legacy Attainments generally operate according to the Legacy\u2019s traditions, which may slightly limit or expand their scope. For example, a Legacy of fire worshipers may be <br /> restricted to heat and fire-based versions of Attainments based on Forces spells. <b>These adjustments shouldn\u2019t make Attainments <br /> significantly more or less powerful than they otherwise would be.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are stretching the meaning of atypical way beyond the intent. The Attainment need to have equivalents to Practices and roughly equivalent power. <br /> <br /> A counter Haunt ability, for example, is the equivalent of a counterspell, and subject to the same rules (Death sight must be up and the subject activating it within sensory range) so that would require Death 1 and Prime 1, so it should be in the optional Attainments.<br /> <br /> I second Satchel's feedback. During an emergency, Attainments are much more helpful. A <i>Temporal Pocket</i> could save the caster's life from an ambush if they roll well, an Attainment always will. <i>Levitate</i> may save you from a plane crash, the Attainment guarantees it. Other benefits include no burden on spell control (great for building armies of zombies and golems), they cannot be counterspelled or dispelled (meaning <i>Memory Hole</i> becomes a lot more troublesome), they are free from the Lie (so you can use <i>Acceleration</i> to flee in a crowded street and will have to deal with the consequences of such a breach of the Veil) and transient stacking means you can become extremely competent at what you do in a short burst. Attainments are pure reliability and have much to offer because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-30-2022, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-28T03:54:00-08:00","id":1498197,"title":"","content":"Tests, new video games, mental problems. That was a long delay. Time to actually format this Legacy even if it remains somewhat incomplete. I will do this over the course of a few days. Maybe a week. Tomorrow I will suggest some Yantras, Oblations, and answer some old questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T17:28:42-08:00","id":1498383,"title":"","content":"I don't get it. Reliability is power. Legacy Attainments do away with nearly all the problems typical to spell casting. There seems to be this insinuation in the forums that successes for Legacy Attainments work like like normal spell successes. I don't know if you believe that, but to be clear: that doesn't make sense. In normal spellcasting the successes make two differences assuming no chance die and no paradox successes, whether the spell succeeds and whether exceptional success options are available. That doesn't make sense for Attainments. The power is going to succeed anyway and if Masters got exceptional success options so reliably then they can use the mana-refund-plus-one option, and then they would readily become a font of mana to fuel an entire consilium and render fights over Hallows silly if even one Master did welfare. So the automatic successes have to be for something else, and the answer given is &quot;when required&quot;. For winning clashes-of-wills with greater utility Attainments? For dice pools of atypical Attainments when most Attainments just activate? When making that Attainment I realized that a dice roll is going to be &quot;required&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for your question Kaiserafini, when I mentioned &quot;Praxis&quot; I was referring to how Praxis is lost to create most Legacy Attainments, and it is easy to interpret that as the Praxis turning into Attainments. <br /> <br /> As for Satchel's tool box argument. The &quot;tool box&quot; of Legacies is locked once you take a tool out of it baring time travel, retcon, Imperial-level magic, or switching characters. So the question is &quot;is this worth losing access to all other Legacies&quot;? If answer is no then that tool will be lost and the supposed point of Legacies won't matter anyway. The specialization means they are not likely to compete for the same function. <br /> <br /> The main problem that both of you don't seem to understand is what I proposed is not all that powerful. Have either of you actually read Geist? I would understand if you couldn't afford it but don't understand why you would be making claims like &quot;too powerful&quot;. I actually checked for this and unless my memory is catastrophically failing me and making me look like an idiot then this rarely matters the way you think it does. The majority of Ceremonies do not offer an extra effect for successes besides an exceptional success giving a krewe beat. The mechanics for beats says that a particular category of beat acquisition (like resolving a condition or accepting a dramatic failure) can work no more then once per scene. Players should be trying for a beats anyway and mages try to game the system anyway by creating and resolving conditions in safety. Krewe beats will help empower the krewe. Ceremonies nearly have all the conveniences of Attainments, I only added reliability in most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T19:00:36-08:00","id":1498392,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1498383#post1498383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get it. Reliability is power. Legacy Attainments do away with nearly all the problems typical to spell casting. There seems to be this insinuation in the forums that successes for Legacy Attainments work like like normal spell successes. I don't know if you believe that, but to be clear: that doesn't make sense. In normal spellcasting the successes make two differences assuming no chance die and no paradox successes, whether the spell succeeds and whether exceptional success options are available. That doesn't make sense for Attainments. The power is going to succeed anyway and if Masters got exceptional success options so reliably then they can use the mana-refund-plus-one option, and then they would readily become a font of mana to fuel an entire consilium and render fights over Hallows silly if even one Master did welfare. So the automatic successes have to be for something else, and the answer given is &quot;when required&quot;. For winning clashes-of-wills with greater utility Attainments? For dice pools of atypical Attainments when most Attainments just activate? When making that Attainment I realized that a dice roll is going to be &quot;required&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason people bring up the successes thing is this line here:<br /> <br /> &quot;In most cases, a Legacy Attainment can be activated with an instant action and does not require dice rolls. Like a spell, the Attainment automatically acquires primary spell factor ranks (in Potency or Duration) equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the Attainment\u2019s highest prerequisite Arcanum minus one. [...] If the Attainment would require a measurement of its successes, it automatically scores a number of successes equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the highest prerequisite Arcanum&quot; <b>Mage Core, Page 198</b>.<br /> <br /> If you knew that already, then my apologies. The only part of that that I've really seen people here debate is whether that means it automatically overcomes Withstand, and even that is not a common interpretation. I have <i>never</i> seen anyone argue that Legacy Attainments should be giving you Mana when activated. Even by RAW, that would only mean that a very few Attainments -like one based on <u>Incognito Presence</u>- would give you 1 Mana when cast, since that's the hard-cap cost for an Attainment as per the Mana Break rule on <b>Page 199</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1498383#post1498383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Satchel's tool box argument. The &quot;tool box&quot; of Legacies is locked once you take a tool out of it baring time travel, retcon, Imperial-level magic, or switching characters. So the question is &quot;is this worth losing access to all other Legacies&quot;? If answer is no then that tool will be lost and the supposed point of Legacies won't matter anyway. The specialization means they are not likely to compete for the same function.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is Mage, a game where Hubris is literally a game mechanic. Your character finding out the Legacy they joined isn't all they claimed to be is <i>par for the course for the setting.</i> Look at the True Souls, the Morphean Continuity, or even the Ticktock Men.<br /> <br /> You seem to be approaching this from a purely mechanical angle - &quot;Why would I take a Legacy that isn't all-powerful?&quot;. The gameline intends it from the other angle - &quot;How can I use this Legacy as a storytelling device?&quot;. There's room for optimization, certainly, that's half the fun with sussing out a Legacy on the forums. But that isn't the <i>purpose</i> of Legacies as a game mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1498383#post1498383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main problem that both of you don't seem to understand is what I proposed is not all that powerful. Have either of you actually read Geist? I would understand if you couldn't afford it but don't understand why you would be making claims like &quot;too powerful&quot;. I actually checked for this and unless my memory is catastrophically failing me and making me look like an idiot then this rarely matters the way you think it does. The majority of Ceremonies do not offer an extra effect for successes besides an exceptional success giving a krewe beat. The mechanics for beats says that a particular category of beat acquisition (like resolving a condition or accepting a dramatic failure) can work no more then once per scene. Players should be trying for a beats anyway and mages try to game the system anyway by creating and resolving conditions in safety. Krewe beats will help empower the krewe. Ceremonies nearly have all the conveniences of Attainments, I only added reliability in most cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may want to modulate your condescension there dude. It may not be the intent of what you typed, but the tone is not comming across as positive or even neutral.<br /> <br /> I've read Giest. Not deeply, but I pulled it up to the Ceremonies section as I'm typing this. The mechanics for Ceremonies don't line up well to Mage -and that's a good thing, all lines having the same magic is boring- but the easiest way I can see making it work is either to add Prime to your dice pool on a Ceremony, or allow you to network together multiple Actors into a shared dice pool. Or allow them to treat Ceremonies as spells for the purposes of gaining the bonuses from Ritual Cooperation on <b>page 55 of Signs of Sorcery</b>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <br /> Actually, let's deep-dive that a bit.<br /> <u>Ritual Focus</u> is a Mind 2 spell. If you were to Attaimentize it into the minimum slot of the Apprentice Attainment, you'd generally want to put the Reach into Advanced Duration, and all Secondary Factors into Scale. That way you spend a scene attuning yourself to your (willing, to ignore Withstand) co-ritualists in some way, then you can perform impromptu Ritual Casting with them at the drop of a hat.<br /> <br /> Now, for a Prime Attainment that enhances something superficially resembling Ritual Casting (i.e. Ceremonies), it isn't a huge problem to cross-pollinate <u>Ritual Focus</u> into a Prime version of the spell, using the logic that since Prime is all about symbolism, it's primarily fascilitating the necessary symbolism-understanding for the ritual. Then just have it apply to only Ceremonies, but in exchange grants those Ceremonies all the normal benefits of Cooperative Ritual Spellcasting.<br /> <br /> I would actually recommend it be a Disciple Attainment, to get you a Reach to either Instant Casting, Advanced Scale, or switching Potency to Primary. for the Apprentice Attainment, you could make it so that Prime Mage Sight highlights what symbolic associations for Ceremonies objects have, similar to how it can highlight Yantras. Alternatively, modify the Matter Spell <u>Craftsman's Eye</u> into a Prime spell that tells you how a studied object can be used in a Ceremony you're aware of and concentrating on.<br /> <br /> If you're hard-up on a Prime Master Attainment, have it transmute a Ghost into a Supernal Specter for the Duration. Or something similar - use <u>Eidolon</u> as a basis-spell and you just... create a solid body made out of Mana for them. It gets [Potency] bonus die as a tool, so most would probably jump at the opportunity. Between it being an Attainment and needing a Ghost to run the thing, you could even probably handwave the Mana upkeep.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":".  Confused Specters and Wraiths. 12-05-2022, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T19:10:08-08:00","id":1498393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage, the Awakening 2ed, page 198</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the Attainment would require a measurement of its successes, it automatically scores a number of successes equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the highest prerequisite Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which means that in cases like <i>Word of Command</i> (found in page 166 of the core book), where the number of successes actually have a tangible effect, the mage is considered to have [Arcana]<br /> <br /> I have read <i>Geist</i>, its a terrific book, I even have a physical copy of it. The main issue is that whatever mechanics the mage is emulating or enhancing should be mechanically cohesive with the Arcana requirements and purview. One example is the idea of counterspelling a Haunt at the 4th Death Attainment. But that requires Prime 1 and Death 1, following the precedent established by the Thrice Great (found on pages 110 to 120 of <i>Legacies: The Ancient</i> ). So its in a slot that is too advanced to provide any additional benefit and mechanically inviable. <br /> <br /> Since you specified granting ghost sight, rather than sense, that would require both Prime 1 and Death 1 for <i>Shared Mage Sight</i> (<i>Signs of Sorcery</i> page 28 ) of the Death Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Detecting connections to krewes and the Chtonic gods would require a specialized Death variation of <i>Interconnections </i>(core book page 134) or <i>Correspondence </i>(core book page 172), with the 2 Reach effect of any of them, in order to trace the emotional or narrative threads, if the mage is actively looking. Alternatively, a Death 1 and Prime 1 spell could reveal anyone using anything under the entropic Resonance of a Geist or Cthonic entity. But someone influenced by mundane means would probably not ping.<br /> <br /> Maybe a <i>Platonic Form</i> can provide the supplies for a Ceremony, but those aren't always terribly rare. The Regalia effect is <i>Platonic Form</i> with one Reach and the ability to gain an extra impression level with Sin-Eaters, so arguably they could be condensed into one Attainment to avoid the overlap. <br /> <br /> I have no idea what you meant by an Omni Key, so I cannot comment on it without more information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T21:18:49-08:00","id":1498395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1498383#post1498383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Satchel's tool box argument. The &quot;tool box&quot; of Legacies is locked once you take a tool out of it baring time travel, retcon, Imperial-level magic, or switching characters. So the question is &quot;is this worth losing access to all other Legacies&quot;? If answer is no then that tool will be lost and the supposed point of Legacies won't matter anyway. The specialization means they are not likely to compete for the same function.</div> </div> </div> </div>My &quot;toolbox argument&quot; is that the tools Legacies provide in the larger toolbox of &quot;powers available to mages&quot; have the advantage of not being subject to the core problems spells have, chiefly the risk and unreliability presented by Paradox/Dissonance/Quiescence and the need to roll.<br /> <br /> Legacies are not a toolbox in this sense. Legacy Attainments are reliable tools that always work the same way instead of having to drag Truth across the chasm of impossibility with mnemonic aids to minimize the risk of the products of your enlightened imagination picking up weird glitches at best and catastrophic errors at worst. Legacies are you picking an area of focus for reliable powers of supernatural origin and accompanying magical theory. You get no benefit from refusing to specialize, because the benefits of specializing in anything else do not manifest without actually committing to the specialization.<br /> <br /> Yes, the right sort of Legacy Attainments can trivialize certain types of problem if you define &quot;trivializing a problem&quot; in the vein of &quot;being able to suspend your vital functions allows you to remain in a place with no breathable air.&quot; This is not on the same level of problem as &quot;the full scope of ritual magic available to mortals \u2014 Phenomenal, externally-sourced power \u2014 can be rendered consistent and reliable by an internal power this Legacy can cultivate in a character before they're even far enough into the Legacy to initiate new members.&quot;<br /> <br /> A certain stripe of mage will turn up their nose at a Legacy for having Attainments that don't impress them. Other sorts of mage will be more interested in the Legacy for its oblations, or its Yantras, or its Ruling Arcanum, or its magical theory, or the networking opportunities it presents, or because someone they care about is involved with it, and so on. The fact that Legacy Attainments are not significantly stronger than spells built on the same principles prevents the first sort of mage from twisting the game into an absurd shape by making them objectively right instead of simply focused on a particular type of optimization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T21:27:30-08:00","id":1498398,"title":"","content":"Wait, this has been going on for almost two years? Fuck it, blackjack and hookers time.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ok, Obrimos Death-Mages who truck with Sin Eaters. Fluff is as always my weak point, but as of 0721 01Dec2022, here's a viable Legacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Order of the Gilded Death-Mask</b><br /> Mages who cooperate regularly with Sin-Eaters<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Ghostbusters, Gravedancers, Calaveras, Necrophiles (Derogatory)<br /> <br /> <b>Organization</b>: The Calaveras may call themselves an order (although not in the Nameless sense), but they are shockingly disorganized as a group. Calaveras' Legacy-facing life mostly revolves around whichever Krewe they're currently assisting, which may or may not include other members of the Legacy. Even the Silver Ladder members seem happy with this state of affairs, treating their deathly associates as a private endevor that other thearchs should be polite enough to not enquire about.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory</b>: Death holds many secrets, and the only way to find them is to steep yourself in the Silent Angel's domain.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: When the Four Virtues Krewe and the High Street Theurges Cabal nearly martyred themselves to save downtown Bellingham from being thrown into the Underworld, a bond was formed between Sin-Eater and Mage. The two groups had never heard of each other, or even imagined that the other kind of Supernatural existed, but quickly realized how effective their cooperation could be. As the years wore on, the junior members of the Cabal elected to shape their own Legacy based on this alliance.<br /> <br /> Though not a particularly popular Legacy -Sin-Eaters are thin on the ground, and most Obrimos have little interest in Death- the High Street Theurges have gone out of their way to pass on the Legacy to as many Consilli as they can.<br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Obrimos; Free Council, Silver Ladder, Mysterium<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras</b>: Objects that have been used in Ceremonies (+1); Candy skulls (+1); Items made of Plasm (+2); Resolved Anchors - good luck identifying them! (+2)<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Eulogize a nearby ghost; Intercede in the world of the living on behalf of a Ghost; [Party with Sin-Eaters? I honestly don't know enough about the line to make solid Oblations related to them]<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prereq</b>: Occult 2, Mystery Cult (Krewe) 1<br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Go through the Krewe-binding Ceremony with a friendly Krewe<br /> <br /> <b>Glimpses of the Beyond</b><br /> (Death \u25cf) <i>Initiation</i><br /> All things are cause and effect - if something is dead, then there was a cause. The Calaveras have a way with spotting the telltale signs of those connections.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><u>Forensic Gaze</u></i><br /> Potency = Death<br /> Duration = N/A<br /> Range = Touch/Aimed<br /> Casting Time = Instant (Reach to Instant Casting)<br /> NOTE: Automatically activates when coming into direct physical contact with a given Sin-Eater for the first time. Always works on Sin Eaters, treating their original death as the subject of the spell, regardless of how often they've died since.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> (Prime \u25cf)<br /> All things have cause and effect, but the relationship between the two can sometimes be murky.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><u>*Non-Spell Effect*</u></i> - The Mage's Active Prime Mage Sight highlights objects that can be used in Ceremonies as if they were Yantra. This effect only applies to Ceremonies that the Mage has been educated on, either by having directly witnessed it or having had it thoroughly explained to them by a practitioner. The Prime Mage Sight also treats Ceremonies as spells for the purposes of detection; a Krewe bond, for example, registers on Peripheral Mage Sight and is obvious under Active Prime Mage Sight. The Mage still cannot Dispell non-Awakened magic, including Ceremonies.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Eyes In All Worlds</b><br /> (Death \u25cf\u25cf) <i>Occult 2, Krewe 2</i><br /> All Calaveras are expected to deal with The Dead, and it very quickly becomes second nature to speak with them. By spending a scene in meditation at an Avernian Gate, the Calavera attunes themself to the layer of reality populated by The Dead.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><u>Speak With The Dead</u></i><br /> Duration = Death (Reach to Advanced Duration)<br /> Potency = N/A<br /> Range = Self<br /> Casting Time = Scene<br /> NOTE: Reach to &quot;Universal Language of the Dead&quot;<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> (Prime \u25cf\u25cf)<br /> The lines of Resonance that any mage with a hint of Prime can see transcend certain boundaries - know the flows, and you can find all kinds of interesting things. So long as the Calavera is able to speak with The Dead, they are sufficiently in-tune with the unseen to observe resonance, leylines, and other ephermeral phenomena.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><u>Sacred Geometry</u></i><br /> Duration = Prime (Reach to Advanced Duration)<br /> Potency = N/A<br /> Range = Self<br /> Casting Time = Scene<br /> NOTE: Death Conjunctive effect.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Between Two Worlds</b><br /> (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <i>Occult 3, Krewe 3</i><br /> The Calaveras has begun to grow adept at acting amidst The Dead, and yet they stand apart from the hollow echoes of the departed. This is probably for the best; a truely impartial judge is one who does not fear their constituents. So long as the Calavera can speak with The Dead, they are also shielded from deathly depridations.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><u>Ghost Shield</u></i><br /> Duration = Death (Reach to Advanced Duration)<br /> Potency = N/A<br /> Range = Self<br /> Casting Time = Scene<br /> NOTE: Reach to &quot;Protection from Ghost attacks&quot;. ATYPICAL - while in effect, the Mage is not considered &quot;Alive&quot; for the purposes of breaking The Old Laws<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> (Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> While true understanding yet eludes them, Calaveras have a surprising knack for binding groups together for the purposes of Ceremonial rituals. By having a thorough discussion about ritual ceremonies with other Mages or Sin Eaters, the Calavera can create a unifying bond of competence between them when participating in Ceremonies<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><u>*Ritual Focus Variant*</u></i><br /> Duration = Prime (Reach to Advanced Duration)<br /> Potency = 2, 3 at Prime 4<br /> Scale = 5 Subjects (Reach to Advanced Scale)<br /> Range = Touch/Aimed<br /> Casting Time = Scene<br /> NOTE: ATYPICAL - modifying than the normal effect of <u>Ritual Focus</u>, the Mage can treat Ceremonies as Cooperative Ritual Spellcasting for the purposes of adding additional dice to the Ceremony's activation roll. Any Ceremonies conducted in this way benefit from <u>Ritual Focus'</u> normal effects (I.e. the [Potency] bonus dice)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>The Quick, The Dead, And The Quick Dead</b><br /> (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <i>Occult 4, Krewe 4</i><br /> Sometimes all a grave problem needs to resolve itself is a push. Calaveras are experts at providing such nudges, bolstering Corpus and revitalizing stilted echoes.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><u>Quicken Ghost</u></i><br /> Potency = Death<br /> Duration = One Week (Reach to Advanced Duration)<br /> Range = Touch/Aimed<br /> Casting Time = Instant (Reach to Instant Casting)<br /> NOTE: In addition to being able to temporarily boost a Sin-Eater's Geist, the &quot;Potency Healing&quot; effect can be applied to the Sin-Eater.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> (Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Though innert, dull lead is not a favored currency of the Aether, there is plenty that can be bough with such a weighty coin. The Calaveras know better than to turn their noses up at good coinage.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><u>*Creative Spell - The Lead Exchange*</u></i><br /> Potency = Death<br /> Duration = 3 Turns<br /> Withstand = Composure / Rank<br /> Range = Touch<br /> Casting Time = Instant (Reach to Instant Casting)<br /> Description: Drains [Potency] points of Essence from a target and converts it into [Potency-1] points Mana, or vise versa. When used on a Sin-Eater, treat Plasm as Essence<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Kick In The Door</b><br /> (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <i>Occult 5, Krewe 5</i><br /> When you work long enough with something, short-cuts and underlying theory become ingrained techniques. By dint of long grave-work, Master Calaveras learn to create universal Anchors wholesale, perfect for bribing the dead or using as a life preserver for a vital Ghost. This requires a short period of ritual dedication, anointing the intended Anchor with sweet oils and brightly colored symbols.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><u>Create Anchor</u></i><br /> Duration = Death (Reach to Advanced Duration)<br /> Potency = 3<br /> Withstand = Resolve<br /> Range = Touch<br /> Casting Time = Scene<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> (Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Encasing the conceptual idea of their universal Anchors in a complex sheath of Prime, a Second-Degree Master Calavera can give Ghosts a body of Supernal Truth. Self-aggrandizing Calaveras will often refer to these constructs as Specters, though Moros summoners often take offense.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><u>Eidolon</u></i><br /> Potency = Prime<br /> Duration = One Week<br /> Scale = Size 5 Or Less<br /> Range = Touch/Aimed<br /> Cost = 1 Mana<br /> Casting Time = Scene<br /> NOTE: Death Conjunctive Effect - Must be used on a Ghost, which pilots the construct ala <u>Golem</u>.<br /> ATYPICAL - The construct requires only 1 Mana per day to function. The Ghost may spend 2 points of Essence in place of 1 point of Mana to fuel the construct.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-05-2022, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T00:26:16-08:00","id":1498410,"title":"","content":"I'm sure I'm going to regret this, but.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26112\" data-vbnamecard=\"26112\">Excess</a>, could you do me a favor and explain in your own terms what the current conversation is about and why it's happening? I think I'd rather start there than my own read for a change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T04:40:48-08:00","id":1498750,"title":"","content":"Sorry I got distracted. Returning tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T23:08:16-08:00","id":1498818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1498410#post1498410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure I'm going to regret this, but.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, could you do me a favor and explain in your own terms what the current conversation is about and why it's happening? I think I'd rather start there than my own read for a change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Truth be told I am also confused. It seems to be that there is a dispute of balance. Geist ceremonies are magic that can be learned by anyone. Not only do they tend to be cheap but you don't always have to learn them by spending your own experiences. They can be canonized as part of the Krewe mythos or lore using Krewe experiences, after which anyone of sufficient rank can use them. Not only would the mage absolutely have access to such cheap and available magic but conceptually is supposed to be a priest for the Krewe. They are supposed to have certain Attainments that synergize with those Krewe powers. The Regalia and the Krewe virtue and creed are all well and good, but since the majority of Krewe powers are just ceremonies then I felt justified dedicating two Attainments to them.<br /> <br /> The problem we have been stuck on was my idea of one Attainment just adding automatic successes to ceremonies equal to prime dots. The majority of ceremonies wouldn't be more powerful for it but just more reliable. An exceptional success gives a Krewe beat, and beat rules say it will work no faster than one per scene. <br /> <br /> I am not entirely sure what happened after that. I tried to argue that the speciality of Legacies is license to try to make them potent and that it means that their quality is not directly competing with other Legacies, and that their mutual exclusivity means that it cannot be too weak either. Cauthon has misunderstood me and thought I was trying to argue for an all-powerful Legacy. This Legacy was always supposed to be a story devise about the Supernal attempting to reclaim the Cthonic. Cauthon has also thought my writing was condescending, not sure what happened either.<br /> <br /> I will explain more tomorrow as I understand it. That will also be when when I examine what prototype he wrote. Thanks for that Cauthon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T00:21:10-08:00","id":1498825,"title":"","content":"I will readily admit that I took offense at what I perceived as rudeness towards people I think highly of. I may not particularly get along with Satchel, but they are unquestionably one of the best sources of inter-splat information on the forums, and KaiserAfini is very knowledgeable about making Legacies. Lack of tonal conveyance in text means word choice is very important, and...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main problem that both of you don't seem to understand is what I proposed is not all that powerful. Have either of you actually read Geist? I would understand if you couldn't afford it but don't understand why you would be making claims like &quot;too powerful&quot;. </div> </div> </div>...doesn't read as particularly polite.<br /> <br /> Satchel's argument -one I wholeheartedly agree with- is that simply adding automatic successes means that Ceremonies will go off without issue 100% of the time barring ST fiat. Sure, the small sample of Ceremonies I've seen aren't game-breakingly powerful, but a) it's boring to auto-win an entire category of skill checks at all times, b) Legacy Attainments aren't set up to make you auto-win anyway, and c) pragmatic future-proofing would dictate that the publishing a game-breaking Ceremony is always a possibility.<br /> <br /> Extrapolating further - while not every Attainment maps perfectly to a spell, the rule of thumb is to at least conform them to the limitations set for spells between <b>Page 125-127</b>. The most you get for dice-alteration is the Rote Action quality; the rest of the time you're either adding dice, or getting 8-/9-Again.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you want an all-powerful Legacy, I'm saying the logic you've applied as to why &quot;auto-successes as an Attainment is a good idea&quot; implies a very specific kind of playstyle. Apply the same logic to, say, a Mind or Fate Legacy, and you could just use <u>Serendipity</u> to apply auto-successes to any problem with impunity. It sets a bad precedent. <br /> <br /> Hope the Sugar-Skulls help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-05-2022, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T12:10:00-08:00","id":1498877,"title":"","content":"So I feel like a) you're making the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390164#post1390164\">same mistake</a> you did when I first recall having met you, in that you are trying answer game design issue for a Mage component with something a another game, which doesn't make sense since Mages are not the Bound*, b) You're not taking advantage of the several legacies we have as guidelines, and as an extension of that, c) you're trying to argue for attainments being more powerful than they are. There's a pretty stark difference between what I'm seeing and literally any published Legacy.<br /> <br /> And mind you, all of that <i>is fine</i>, but you need to be clear about your intentionality, cause it feels like you're trying to argue that this is how it always works versus something deliberately breaks the mold.<br /> <br /> *Just because I feel like this might be getting in the way of it, I should note that just because a mage can lead/participate in a Ceremony, that does not make a Ceremony viable for the making of an attainment, since attainments have their roots in the Supernal shaping of self, which Ceremonies don't do. I doubt that's actually the problem, but on the off chance, pays to lay that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T17:40:20-08:00","id":1498902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1498877#post1498877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I feel like a) you're making the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334170-spun-or-unspun-the-paradox-of-time-travel?p=1390164#post1390164\">same mistake</a> you did when I first recall having met you, in that you are trying answer game design issue for a Mage component with something a another game, which doesn't make sense since Mages are not the Bound*, b) You're not taking advantage of the several legacies we have as guidelines, and as an extension of that, c) you're trying to argue for attainments being more powerful than they are. There's a pretty stark difference between what I'm seeing and literally any published Legacy.<br /> <br /> And mind you, all of that <i>is fine</i>, but you need to be clear about your intentionality, cause it feels like you're trying to argue that this is how it always works versus something deliberately breaks the mold.<br /> <br /> *Just because I feel like this might be getting in the way of it, I should note that just because a mage can lead/participate in a Ceremony, that does not make a Ceremony viable for the making of an attainment, since attainments have their roots in the Supernal shaping of self, which Ceremonies don't do. I doubt that's actually the problem, but on the off chance, pays to lay that out.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Bringing back material from years ago is pretty much the very definition of necromancy and working to make this an ongoing feud.<br /> <br /> I am going to ask you to drop this topic and never bring it up again.<br /> <br /> Or this thread will be closed.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T23:21:44-08:00","id":1501850,"title":"","content":"Nearly ready to return. Let's hope I last a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T04:18:13-08:00","id":1502092,"title":"","content":"Cauthon. Thank you.<br /> <br /> what you wrote isn't exactly what I wanted, but what else would I expect? I was taking so long so you filled in the details yourself, and you cannot read minds. At this point I don't think it matters what version the viewers would have preferred if you are the one who finishes his content. I don't even know how to do the fancy collapsible text trick.<br /> <br /> so for what it is worth I will mention some of the differences between our ideas this week, then move on to the last Legacy.<br /> <br /> The Legacy's theory kinda makes it sound like a hobby, but what I imagined was a bit more focused and ambitious than that. It did involve understanding that both the Supernal and the Underworld have the principle of &quot;as above, so below&quot; and vice versa. It continued that these things could be linked like a chain, and already are to some extent. Just as the Guardians have hidden rules that are either an extreme version or a logical deduction of their revealed rules, my death priests believe in Catabasis. Elaboration tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T05:24:53-08:00","id":1502096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1502092#post1502092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even know how to do the fancy collapsible text trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>[ spoiler] blah blah blah[ /spoiler]. Delete the space between the first brackets and the &quot;s&quot; and &quot;/&quot; respectively. Similarly, you can <b>Bold</b> words ([ b][ /b]), <i>italicize</i> ([ i][ /i]) and <u>underline</u> ([ i][ /i]) the same way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1502092#post1502092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so for what it is worth I will mention some of the differences between our ideas this week, then move on to the last Legacy.<br /> <br /> The Legacy's theory kinda makes it sound like a hobby, but what I imagined was a bit more focused and ambitious than that. It did involve understanding that both the Supernal and the Underworld have the principle of &quot;as above, so below&quot; and vice versa. It continued that these things could be linked like a chain, and already are to some extent. Just as the Guardians have hidden rules that are either an extreme version or a logical deduction of their revealed rules, my death priests believe in Catabasis. Elaboration tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... sounds more like you want a Mystery Cult or a Nameless Order than a Legacy. Legacies can have elements of that, but aside from a few like the Daksha -which have gone out of their way to basically be a splinter-faction in the Mysterium- I usually interpret Legacies as being a focusing lens by which a Mage refines their normal behaviors. That is, a Forge Master of the Guardians and an 11Q of the Guardians will apply their talents differently, but they're still ultimately Guardians and will behave as such. There just aren't enough Mages per Legacy per Consilium to create sweeping subcultures, unless they're heavily and aggressively evangelizing.<br /> <br /> Take for example the Shapers of the Invisible in <b>Nameless and Accursed</b>. They're a Legacy that's borderline inextricably interwoven with the Order of the Rose Mystery Cult/Nameless Order. But the only reason their identity is so closely tied to that Cult is that the Cult is the only practitioners. A Pentacle Mage who initiated into the Legacy might use it in a completely different manner than UOPS and her followers do.<br /> <br /> Granted, that's very much my personal interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-05-2023, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T18:42:54-08:00","id":1502337,"title":"","content":"Imagine making up a god or monster to manipulate people, or using gods and monsters others made up to do it. Then discover that said God or monster somehow existed. As surreal as that might be the Underworld is a medium for mythology about death, and under the right circumstances allows that mythology to come &quot;alive&quot;. So to speak.<br /> <br /> stories about liars or storytellers that warp reality already have potential, but what about a mage that wanted to make a new front for the Supernal in an increasingly Fallen world, a new source of power? The issue is that for that to happen the new vision of the Underworld needs Doctrines to define it, and that is not part of the Legacy's Theory at all. The Founder's priority was to create a tool to achieve Supernal Catabasis, then figure out what the Doctrines were going to be later. <br /> <br /> That is why the Legacy itself is apolitical. As an anomaly it only counted krewes as Orders for induction. The initiation was going to be to interpret the Krewe's mysteries through the Supernal and canonizing that perspective. Inventing and abandoning a Krewe for that purpose works. Potentially every opposing cause might have their Death Priest if the Founder loses their hold on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T22:29:33-08:00","id":1502347,"title":"","content":"I need to preface this with a question. I\u2019m really not intending it to be rude or catty, I just need it for context on how to approach this. Are you drafting these posts at all? They read very stream-of-conscious, or like they were machine-translated, which makes it hard to parse where the important parts are under the prose.<br /> <br /> <s>Setting aside my strong aversion to having one splat directly influence the endgame of another (I don't like it, but I'm not going to call it badwrongfun), I need some clarification on why this needs to be a Legacy. If the focus is on bringing about Catabasis, then from my cursory look at Giest it would make more sense to focus on Death/Mind to shape how people perceive the afterlife, or to use Death/Prime to alter the ley resonance of Avernian Gates and ultimately the Underworld itself. Both of those focuses could be acheived just as easily as a Cabal or mages, or even a Mystery Cult.<br /> <br /> A Legacy is ultimately another lens through which the Mage is filtering their Gnosis, alongside Path, Order, and Shadow Name. It's not the lever shifting the universe, it's the wrapping that allows you to better grasp the handle. It's a personal journey with other travelers coming into view now and then, rather than Catabasis' united lockstep towards a particular goal. From your description, it sounds like your &quot;Founder&quot; is abandoning Krewe at a moments notice, which doesn't exactly inspire confidence in them taking on apprentices. Without apprentices, there isn't really a Legacy culture to lean into, which... well, it's boring. Creating a new Legacy in-play can be really fun, in that the ripples it creates can have interesting impacts. Creating a culture-less Legacy on the forums is... well, what ripples are really being made? Legacies posted to the forums tend to be more interesting when they can be slotted fairly easily into any game, and add a social dimension. How does it impact the character if their Legacy Mentor is from a different Order, and broke custom by initiating them? How is a character who learned their Legacy from a Daikonomicon gained in an Acquisitive Awakening received by local practitioners? Or one who\u200b was denied entry, but entered by bargaining with the relevant Aeon?</s><br /> <br /> I've spent too much time re-writing and trying to draft out what rubs me wrong about this Death Priest idea you're trying to convey. Bottom line - to make a good Legacy, you need two things. First, be able to point to a clear Theory. 1-3 sentences that clearly define the ethos. They don't necessarily need to be a goal, but it should imply a philosophy;<ul><li>&quot;You must master youself before you can master the world&quot; (Pure Sovereigns)</li> <li>&quot;Every question has an answer&quot; (Eleventh Question)</li> <li>&quot;People are unpredictable. Masses are not.&quot; (Subtle Ones)</li> <li>&quot;A subtle hand is a steady hand. Visible power is a liability.&quot; (Sisterhood of the Blessed)</li> <li>&quot;Be quick or be dead&quot; (Expedious Explorers)</li> <li>&quot;I am greater than this hollow husk&quot; (Chrysiladis)</li> </ul>I don't see a clear Theory so far in this thread. I'd recommend settling on one before you start your next Legacy, or before you keep tackling the Death Priests.<br /> <br /> Second, you need a clear idea of what you want the Attainments to do. This needs to be more concrete than &quot;Omnikey&quot;. Again, at least a full sentence but no more than three, outlining the basic benefits and limitations. Map it to spells or Utility Attainments as much as you can. They also need to line up with the Theory - a Death Priest who can re-route Ley Lines into the Underworld in pursuit of reshaping the afterlife makes sense. One who makes themself into a living anchor makes less sense, but is still manageable. One who goes around hucking Attainment-ized balls of Supernal Fire has utterly departed the theme.<br /> <br /> And the most important counterpoint to either the Theory or the Attainments is to not overthink it. Find what's close enough, then start polishing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-07-2023, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T01:18:58-08:00","id":1502360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1498398#post1498398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Kick In The Door</b><br /> (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <i>Occult 5, Krewe 5</i><br /> When you work long enough with something, short-cuts and underlying theory become ingrained techniques. By dint of long grave-work, Master Calaveras learn to create universal Anchors wholesale, perfect for bribing the dead or using as a life preserver for a vital Ghost. This requires a short period of ritual dedication, anointing the intended Anchor with sweet oils and brightly colored symbols.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><u>Create Anchor</u></i><br /> Duration = Death (Reach to Advanced Duration)<br /> Potency = 3<br /> Withstand = Resolve<br /> Range = Touch<br /> Casting Time = Scene<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>One question on this, why is the withstand resolve?<br /> <br /> This seems odd, ok i see it is what is written in the example spell in the book... Whose resolve? If you create an anchor out of a necklace which has no resolve is that not withstood?<br /> <br /> It seems like it should he withstood by the Ghost's rank if you are forcing a ghost to be anchors (as an extra subject).<br /> <br /> Am i misreading something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T01:58:45-08:00","id":1502367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1502360#post1502360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One question on this, why is the withstand resolve?<br /> <br /> This seems odd, ok i see it is what is written in the example spell in the book... Whose resolve? If you create an anchor out of a necklace which has no resolve is that not withstood?<br /> <br /> It seems like it should he withstood by the Ghost's rank if you are forcing a ghost to be anchors (as an extra subject).<br /> <br /> Am i misreading something?</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to transcribe the spells exactly unless the Attainment has some hinky special modification, so that's the only reason it's there. As for why the original spell has it... I <i>think</i> you can make living entities into Anchors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-11-2023, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T03:41:32-08:00","id":1502373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1502367#post1502367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to transcribe the spells exactly unless the Attainment has some hinky special modification, so that's the only reason it's there. As for why the original spell has it... I think you can make living entities into Anchors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. And living entities can withstand... But a building or key can not. Which does slightly affect the utility of the attainment. But i was confused at first... It is not necessary that a ghost is the subject of the effect, but if they are, why would they resist getting an anchor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T06:00:10-08:00","id":1502383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1502373#post1502373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. And living entities can withstand... But a building or key can not. Which does slightly affect the utility of the attainment. But i was confused at first... It is not necessary that a ghost is the subject of the effect, but if they are, why would they resist getting an anchor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the Attainment was mostly meant to be a precursor to the Eidolon-form. Besides, I'd imagine it has more utility creating a bunch of &quot;talismans&quot; that the Sugar-Skull keeps on hand to support a small army of ghostly retainers.<br /> <br /> I'm not an expert on Ghosts, but I imagine it's for the same reason subjects can resist being given good luck with Fate spells. Just because something is -at a glance- good for you doesn't mean your pattern will treat it as any less of an invasion of autonomy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T08:10:54-08:00","id":1502392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1502383#post1502383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, the Attainment was mostly meant to be a precursor to the Eidolon-form. Besides, I'd imagine it has more utility creating a bunch of &quot;talismans&quot; that the Sugar-Skull keeps on hand to support a small army of ghostly retainers.<br /> <br /> I'm not an expert on Ghosts, but I imagine it's for the same reason subjects can resist being given good luck with Fate spells. Just because something is -at a glance- good for you doesn't mean your pattern will treat it as any less of an invasion of autonomy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Ghost have a resolve stat, not sure whether they would use their Resistance or their Rank, but Ghost summons is resisted by Rank.<br /> <br /> I am just not sure, would it be Resolve/Rank (whichever is higher) +1 if the subject (anchor) and the ghost (anchored) both resisted, almost surprised that the extra subject isn't a reach factor...<br /> <br /> But as a default an 'open condition for any ghost' is fairly strong (though this is mastery, so, not all the OP in the scheme of things).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:34:12-08:00","id":1502423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1502392#post1502392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Ghost have a resolve stat, not sure whether they would use their Resistance or their Rank, but Ghost summons is resisted by Rank.<br /> <br /> I am just not sure, would it be Resolve/Rank (whichever is higher) +1 if the subject (anchor) and the ghost (anchored) both resisted, almost surprised that the extra subject isn't a reach factor...<br /> <br /> But as a default an 'open condition for any ghost' is fairly strong (though this is mastery, so, not all the OP in the scheme of things).</div> </div> </div> </div>If Ghosts resist it, I'd assume they still use Resistance - the rule of thumb being that any roll requiring Stamina, Resolve or Composure rolls Resistance for Invisible Entities.<br /> <br /> But ultimately I don't think Ghosts resist it at all. I don't think they can be made into Anchors themselves, although it would be interesting to have two Ghosts be each other's Anchors. Muddling things slightly is that the nearest Spirit equivalent is <u>Opener of the Way</u>, which has no Withstand at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T15:44:53-08:00","id":1502454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1502337#post1502337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine making up a god or monster to manipulate people, or using gods and monsters others made up to do it. Then discover that said God or monster somehow existed. As surreal as that might be the Underworld is a medium for mythology about death, and under the right circumstances allows that mythology to come &quot;alive&quot;. So to speak.<br /> <br /> stories about liars or storytellers that warp reality already have potential, but what about a mage that wanted to make a new front for the Supernal in an increasingly Fallen world, a new source of power? The issue is that for that to happen the new vision of the Underworld needs Doctrines to define it, and that is not part of the Legacy's Theory at all. The Founder's priority was to create a tool to achieve Supernal Catabasis, then figure out what the Doctrines were going to be later.<br /> <br /> That is why the Legacy itself is apolitical. As an anomaly it only counted krewes as Orders for induction. The initiation was going to be to interpret the Krewe's mysteries through the Supernal and canonizing that perspective. Inventing and abandoning a Krewe for that purpose works. Potentially every opposing cause might have their Death Priest if the Founder loses their hold on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like what an archmage of the Alienated Entente would do. Their Omens create a new framework of occult theory for Krewes to leverage (mundane Omen), redefine the nature of the Underworld's systems and a system to support it (supernatural Omen) and then places the mage with admin privileges to harness its power (personal Omen). When the new system has been enstated, they Ascend alongside the new Cthonic God that they created. The objective as defined by the outline seem far beyond the scope of a Legacy's purview.<br /> <br /> I also second Cauthon's recommendations, I think you need to narrow the scope of the their focus will lead to more synergistic Attainments. Regarding why <i>Create Anchor</i> is resisted by Resolve, I believe its because in the case of a living being, you are creating a specialized Death resonant sympathetic connection, in which your thoughts, memories and emotions can be used to sustain any ghost. Since the spell is applying a change to a being's mind, it is resisted by Resolve. Should an unwilling ghost be targeted, they can Withstand the effect with Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-07-2023, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T21:49:31-07:00","id":1507263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1502454#post1502454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like what an archmage of the Alienated Entente would do. Their Omens create a new framework of occult theory for Krewes to leverage (mundane Omen), redefine the nature of the Underworld's systems and a system to support it (supernatural Omen) and then places the mage with admin privileges to harness its power (personal Omen). When the new system has been enstated, they Ascend alongside the new Cthonic God that they created. The objective as defined by the outline seem far beyond the scope of a Legacy's purview.<br /> <br /> I also second Cauthon's recommendations, I think you need to narrow the scope of the their focus will lead to more synergistic Attainments. Regarding why <i>Create Anchor</i> is resisted by Resolve, I believe its because in the case of a living being, you are creating a specialized Death resonant sympathetic connection, in which your thoughts, memories and emotions can be used to sustain any ghost. Since the spell is applying a change to a being's mind, it is resisted by Resolve. Should an unwilling ghost be targeted, they can Withstand the effect with Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am back for the week. Responding to this first. I like the Alienated, but the source material mentioned that their allegiance was to a set of Fallen gods, restoring something old rather than creating something new. I think you are onto something, however. What cause can't be helped by recrafting a metaphysical plane of existence? How many causes actually require something so dramatic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T02:24:38-07:00","id":1507464,"title":"","content":"Skeleton key? Mm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T03:50:11-07:00","id":1513518,"title":"","content":"I Am back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T05:17:38-07:00","id":1513760,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is what I need to consider: do I progress to the next idea or do I keep refining a different version of an idea already done? To better represent this I perhaps should explain what the next idea even is. I once had my Unashamed retorted to as &quot;if you want to play Rapt, play Rapt&quot;. Probably not the exact words but close enough. This response confused me because I am not even sure how those two got conflated. I must have failed terribly in the explanation somewhere. The Rapt may be an interesting phenomenon and enemy, but not good characters to play as (in my opinion). Their lack of restraint, character, subtlety, perspective, ability to enter the Temenos, among others makes them unappealing as player characters. Especially since they cannot manage Paradox at all. Problems my Unashamed don't have at all. <br /> <br /> the real purpose of them? A significant part of both the mechanics and themes of mage revolves around the preservation or loss of Wisdom, which some mages conflate with morality, or with the Lie depending on who you ask. A powerful (or destructive) way to test the setting is to see what happens when some mages don't have that requirement any more. A perverse &quot;what if&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T09:00:22-07:00","id":1513779,"title":"","content":"I would recommend the next idea, work with a fresh perspective and spend a little more time distilling the core theme. Right now most of your ideas seem to be the result of a stream of consciousness, they need to be made clear and concise. Boil down a concept to one phrase, without commas or pauses. Then use that to guide you design, from the Legacy's philosophy, to Attainments and yantras. If it doesn't fit with the theme phrase, it needs to be revised.<br /> <br /> Keep it simple, pursue flavor above power. See a Legacy as a lens, a philosophy that shapes how the characters sees and specializes their magic. Stick to what you can accomplish with Creative Thaumaturgy, your previous Legacy designs tended to give too much when compared to other ones with the unusual Attainments, such as the <i>Logophages</i> or <i>Reality Stalkers</i>.<br /> <br /> I would also encourage re-reading the feedback Cauthon posted on this thread, I believe it can be of great help for that process.<br /> <br /> That is the best advice I can provide at the moment, hope it proves helpful.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T23:20:18-07:00","id":1519317,"title":"","content":"I suppose some final complaints before I bury the Death Priests. When I said &quot;Omni-key&quot; I really meant &quot;it opens every deathly Door or pays any normal Chthonic toll. Still specialized to the Legacy's purpose but stretching that definition as far as it will go. I must have done a terrible job explaining that. Another thing: just because the Legacy doesn't have some universal politics doesn't mean the individual mages won't use this power for their politics. There are already so many competing philosophies among the Bound that could suddenly become a terrible threat because they started recruiting these guys. It could make you think: maybe these guys could achieve it (Catabasis) first?<br /> <br /> as for strategies concerning this new Legacy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T23:38:32-07:00","id":1519318,"title":"","content":"I must have typed this before but my main inspiration for the mechanics is the Coil of Zirnitra. Mechanics often have common elements to them (dice rolls and degrees of failure), and that Coil translated them by referencing those elements and explaining what would happen additionally or alternatively. It also started with those restored powers being rather flawed, then removed those flaws and left them better than when when those vampires were human. Why this? Because I realize that what I am trying to do is not a set of discrete powers but some rule changes. Still I am rather lost, then I remembered that I am deliberately trying to subvert some philosophies, perhaps by mocking them maybe I will know what this is supposed to look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T23:05:25-07:00","id":1521805,"title":"","content":"I have been reviewing some materials, tomorrow I will quickly review Cauthon's materials and will make a decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T23:53:52-07:00","id":1521859,"title":"","content":"Okay. I have been thinking. The thematic vs the mechanical. <br /> <br /> I reviewed somethings about Wisdom and its place in the story. One thing I am still confused about is whether the Silver Ladder still disdains Wisdom. In the first edition they regarded it as part of the Lie. In the second edition they still are rather reckless and such but I cannot find what their official statement about Wisdom is. So the only other Order that has special concern or opinion about Wisdom beyond the practical day-to-day is the Guardians of the Veil. <br /> <br /> I have been thinking that the Esoteric Tenents are but the logical extremes of the Exoteric Tenents. The problem with logical extremes is that they tend to make some assumptions. I thinking about what would happen if they saw this Legacy challenge their assumptions about Wisdom.<br /> <br /> I have mostly decided now that &quot;Unashamed&quot; means &quot;at least slightly sociopathic&quot;. I think the spell &quot;Amorality&quot; will do quite nicely (eventually) . The founder was so focused on reshaping their soul to preserve their own ego that they slightly over did it. These mage will not easily succumb to Rapture and retain a far greater degree of personality and self control but the creepy costs will start to show. Imagine someone trying to better protect themselves from peer-pressure (or tenemos corruption) but overdid the mental shield, creating callousness slowly. So gradually the effects worsen as the founder performed more experiments on themselves until it started to resemble the prelude to Rapture ironically, yet never could become as weak or unstable as the actual Rapt. They even accounted for soul disruption that could cause Wisdom loss and added Death as the second Arcanum. Should I eventually have an effect that reverses the property of Wisdom to limit how far the long-term nimbus has spread along sympathetic ties, reasoning that a mage without shame shouldn't have to hide their power completely? <br /> <br /> either way, it cannot be too evil or problematic or else it there will no dilemma: why exactly are the mages joining this flawed Legacy in order to save their Wisdom? Any comment about it becomes a value judgement about what is so appreciated about Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T23:54:40-07:00","id":1521860,"title":"","content":"I won't be here tomorrow. It will be an important day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T05:31:39-07:00","id":1522053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1521860#post1521860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't be here tomorrow. It will be an important day.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">Please avoid making posts like this, I almost mistook you for a bot. </span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T23:28:09-07:00","id":1523391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1522053#post1522053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">Please avoid making posts like this, I almost mistook you for a bot. </span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Then what am I supposed to say? We all have important days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T08:10:00-07:00","id":1523416,"title":"","content":"Excess... there isn't really a point to saying &quot;I won't be here tomorrow&quot; when there's usually a month or two between your posts. We wont be surprised if you aren't posting anything. It's also really vague and doesn't seem to have anyone in particular you're talking to, which makes it seem like a bot is just posting things to seem active.<br /> <br /> Now, if you wanted to elaborate on what's happening, the Vent or Gush threads would be good places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T14:18:20-07:00","id":1523439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1445034-since-everyone-is-doing-legacies?p=1521859#post1521859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. I have been thinking. The thematic vs the mechanical.<br /> <br /> I reviewed somethings about Wisdom and its place in the story. One thing I am still confused about is whether the Silver Ladder still disdains Wisdom. In the first edition they regarded it as part of the Lie. In the second edition they still are rather reckless and such but I cannot find what their official statement about Wisdom is. So the only other Order that has special concern or opinion about Wisdom beyond the practical day-to-day is the Guardians of the Veil.<br /> <br /> I have been thinking that the Esoteric Tenents are but the logical extremes of the Exoteric Tenents. The problem with logical extremes is that they tend to make some assumptions. I thinking about what would happen if they saw this Legacy challenge their assumptions about Wisdom.<br /> <br /> I have mostly decided now that &quot;Unashamed&quot; means &quot;at least slightly sociopathic&quot;. I think the spell &quot;Amorality&quot; will do quite nicely (eventually) . The founder was so focused on reshaping their soul to preserve their own ego that they slightly over did it. These mage will not easily succumb to Rapture and retain a far greater degree of personality and self control but the creepy costs will start to show. Imagine someone trying to better protect themselves from peer-pressure (or tenemos corruption) but overdid the mental shield, creating callousness slowly. So gradually the effects worsen as the founder performed more experiments on themselves until it started to resemble the prelude to Rapture ironically, yet never could become as weak or unstable as the actual Rapt. They even accounted for soul disruption that could cause Wisdom loss and added Death as the second Arcanum. Should I eventually have an effect that reverses the property of Wisdom to limit how far the long-term nimbus has spread along sympathetic ties, reasoning that a mage without shame shouldn't have to hide their power completely?<br /> <br /> either way, it cannot be too evil or problematic or else it there will no dilemma: why exactly are the mages joining this flawed Legacy in order to save their Wisdom? Any comment about it becomes a value judgement about what is so appreciated about Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wisdom is the ability of the mage to be precise in their use of magic. In the short term, it means they are more subtle, creative and know how to calibrate what is needed to solve a situation. In the mid to long term, it means they know how to wield their magic in a way that diminishes or avoids longer terms negative consequences. This means both mundane and magical actions, because to be Awakened is to be in control of one's action, to take ownership of oneself, to have the magic to defy bad fortune. However, Wisdom is not linked to morality. A Wise mage might erase your memories of your sibling that was taken to Arcadia in order to experiment on how a Fetch reacts to having a wrench thrown in its prime directive, and in so doing learn how to exploit the process to gain a new tool to rise in their Ministry.<br /> <br /> When the mage looses Wisdom, it means they are being controlled by the magic, rather than they controlling it. They are giving into the urge to wield the power indiscriminately. The Silver Ladder posit that since it makes mages fit easier into the world, and given that the world is the Soul Cage created by the Exarchs, it makes it easier for them to manipulate them. You can see it in Dave Brookshaw's Broken Diamond AP (an incredible read that I highly recommend), in that when they gain the ability to see the Exarchial influence upon people, its the low Wisdom Wolsey that has the least. Does it directly correlate to the Tyrant's influence ? Who knows.<br /> <br /> Characters like Harry Dresden are low Wisdom, although he usually acts heroic, he started the series using raw power to solve things before asking questions ,and becoming more precise is part of his character development. What worries the Guardians is that such an approach invites situations that cause you to over Reach and risk unleashing Abyssal maladies upon the world, as well as exposing more Sleepers to the Supernal, causing them deep psychological trauma due to The Curse.<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking, Wisdom exists to prevent players from taking a Big Hammer Theory to problemsolving. Its much more interesting for players to try to be clever and subtle. This helps build the tension to make the big, bombastic moments all the more poignant. The Chronicles of Darkness is a dangerous place, where cheating is the way to gain an edge, where murderhobos will stand out to the police, other supernaturals and hunters as a major issue. In this way, there is an integration of mechanics and setting to disincentivize what is called First Order Optimal Strategies, the boring, safe solutions that require the least effort to execute. Here is an example on <a href=\"https://youtu.be/cUbyNJKsi7E?si=UWvc1wYrMeE9L-90\" target=\"_blank\">how this influenced the design of an indie game</a>, which might draw a helpful parallel.<br /> <br /> I believe all of those need to be addressed on a practical, mechanical and philosophical level to make that Legacy viable. Hope that proves helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-01-2023, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T23:49:55-07:00","id":1525056,"title":"","content":"KaiserAfini (it's difficult to remember the spelling), annoyingly, Wisdom is linked to morality. I can't find where the new source books (maybe old) called Wisdom objective morality, but if you look into the lexicon for 'Wisdom' and 'Hubris' it will have words like 'ethics' and 'moral' in it.<br /> <br /> this reminds me of when the different 'morality' systems of the first edition was mostly just morality plus a few strange rules. Then second edition came along and replaced it with 'integrity' systems. The splat unique systems likewise measure something like integrity but often with wildly different rules. I like that it sometimes coincided mechanically and thematically with morality, yet those systems are something alien. <br /> <br /> For example: a vampire's Humanity can be lost by ignoring morality yet can also be lost by surviving something a human couldn't. The reason for both is that they are losing the feel and influence of their previous human existence. <br /> <br /> we can obviously see the details of how Wisdom is built and recognize it is about self-control and an unnaturally expanded capacity to lose it. Yet it failed to cleanly distinguish itself from morality in several cases or even just to define what it even is. What I mean by that last part is an example act of hubris: using magic to do something you could just as easily do without it. How is that a problem? We know the systems of how Paradox works, so circumstances can be made so that magic is completely safe to use, and if we stretch the definition of 'risk' to include such anyway then then that would include nearly all magic. If you could justify it being an act of hubris, then why didn't they make the explanation the act of hubris instead of this uncontextualized example? Can't they just say &quot;pointlessly using magic when it is not safe to do so&quot;? <br /> <br /> players need to be able to intuit why an example breaking point fits a system, and I have seen arguments about how Wisdom works in these forums. Can you blame me for making a &quot;what if scenario&quot; that makes sure to split Wisdom and morality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T17:31:07-08:00","id":1528136,"title":"","content":"Guys, i may have mentioned \u201cissues\u201d here and there when explaining why updates are so infrequent. I had to deal with them whenever i got ready to make one or two posts a month. I have decided they were too much. I am ending my attempts at this thread. Do what you will. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}